parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-start MM-LP (distance linearization) + block-Newton polish (safe, persisted)\"\ntags: \"circle packing, linear programming, majorization-minimization, dual gradients, block-Newton, persistence\"\nabstract: \"We improve over prior MM-LP by running a multi-start schedule from persisted and 7-row 5/4 seeds, performing more MM-LP steps with adaptive trust regions, then polishing with a block-Newton ascent using LP duals. Radii are always finalized by exact HiGHS LP and strict shrink. The best configuration is persisted; a 6×6-minus-corners r=1/12 baseline guarantees non-regression.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  # ---------------- Basic helpers ----------------\n\n  def _clip_box(C: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(C, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\
    \n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _pairwise_indices(n: int):\n      I = []\n      J = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              I.append(i); J.append(j)\n      return np.array(I, dtype=int), np.array(J, dtype=int)\n\n  # ---------------- Exact LP for radii (given centers) ----------------\n\n  def _solve_radii_exact(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1.0/12.0) * 0.999\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True, None, None\n\n      I, J = _pairwise_indices(n)\n      D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n      m = len(I)\n\n      A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n      A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n      A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n      b_ub = D\n\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0,\
    \ bi))) for bi in b]\n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, None\n\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      obj = float(-res.fun)\n\n      y_pairs = None\n      try:\n          if hasattr(res, \"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin, \"marginals\") and res.ineqlin.marginals is not None:\n              y_pairs = np.maximum(0.0, np.asarray(res.ineqlin.marginals, dtype=float))\n      except Exception:\n          y_pairs = None\n\n      return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\n  # ---------------- Validation and safety shrink ----------------\n\n  def _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      if C.shape != (32, 2) or r.shape != (32,):\n          return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n          return False\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      if np.any(x - r < 0) or\
    \ np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n          return False\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n      R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      iu = np.triu_indices(32, 1)\n      if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12):\n          return False\n      return True\n\n  def _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      r2 = np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C)).astype(float)\n      r2 *= 0.999\n      r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n      for _ in range(6):\n          if _validate(C, r2):\n              break\n          r2 *= 0.95\n      r2 = np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C))\n      r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n      return r2\n\n  # ---------------- MM-LP: joint center–radius LP with distance linearization ----------------\n\n  def _mm_lp_step(C0: np.ndarray, delta: float, margin: float = 1e-6):\n      \"\"\"\n      One MM step: linearize distances around C0, solve LP over r,x,y with trust-region bounds\
    \ |C - C0|_inf <= delta.\n      Variables order: [r(0..n-1), x(0..n-1), y(0..n-1)].\n      \"\"\"\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          return C0, *_solve_radii_exact(C0), True\n\n      n = C0.shape[0]\n      I, J = _pairwise_indices(n)\n      m_pairs = len(I)\n\n      V0 = C0[I] - C0[J]\n      d0 = np.linalg.norm(V0, axis=1)\n      eps = 1e-9\n      d0 = np.maximum(d0, eps)\n      U = (V0.T / d0).T\n      ux = U[:, 0]\n      uy = U[:, 1]\n      x0 = C0[:, 0]\n      y0 = C0[:, 1]\n\n      rows = 4 * n + m_pairs\n      cols = 3 * n\n      A_ub = np.zeros((rows, cols), dtype=float)\n      b_ub = np.zeros(rows, dtype=float)\n\n      def idx_r(i): return i\n      def idx_x(i): return n + i\n      def idx_y(i): return 2 * n + i\n\n      row = 0\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] = -1.0; b_ub[row] = 0.0; row += 1  # r_i <= x_i\n          A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] = 1.0;  b_ub[row] = 1.0; row += 1  # r_i + x_i <= 1\n\
    \          A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] = -1.0; b_ub[row] = 0.0; row += 1  # r_i <= y_i\n          A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] = 1.0;  b_ub[row] = 1.0; row += 1  # r_i + y_i <= 1\n\n      for k in range(m_pairs):\n          i = int(I[k]); j = int(J[k])\n          A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] += 1.0\n          A_ub[row, idx_r(j)] += 1.0\n          A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] += -ux[k]\n          A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] += -uy[k]\n          A_ub[row, idx_x(j)] += ux[k]\n          A_ub[row, idx_y(j)] += uy[k]\n          b_ub[row] = d0[k] - ux[k]*x0[i] - uy[k]*y0[i] + ux[k]*x0[j] + uy[k]*y0[j]\n          row += 1\n\n      c = np.zeros(cols, dtype=float)\n      c[:n] = -1.0  # maximize sum r_i\n\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bounds.append((0.0, 0.5))  # r_i\n      for i in range(n):\n          lo = float(max(margin, x0[i] - delta)); hi = float(min(1.0 - margin, x0[i] + delta))\n          bounds.append((lo, hi))\n      for i in range(n):\n        \
    \  lo = float(max(margin, y0[i] - delta)); hi = float(min(1.0 - margin, y0[i] + delta))\n          bounds.append((lo, hi))\n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n          return C0, np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n\n      x = res.x\n      r = x[:n].astype(float)\n      X = x[n:n + n].astype(float)\n      Y = x[n + n:].astype(float)\n      C_new = np.stack([X, Y], axis=1)\n      return C_new, r, float(-res.fun), True\n\n  def _mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int = 30, delta0: float = 0.015, margin: float = 1e-6):\n      \"\"\"\n      Multiple MM-LP steps with adaptive trust region; exact LP objective used for acceptance.\n      \"\"\"\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      r_best, obj_best, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(best_C)\n      if not ok:\n          return C_start, r_best, obj_best\n      delta = float(delta0)\n      C_anchor = C_start.copy()\n\n      for t in range(iters):\n\
    \          C_lin, r_lin, obj_lin, ok_lin = _mm_lp_step(C_anchor, delta=delta, margin=margin)\n          if not ok_lin:\n              delta = max(0.008, 0.6 * delta)\n              continue\n          r_exact, obj_exact, ok_exact, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(C_lin)\n          if ok_exact and obj_exact > obj_best + 1e-12:\n              best_C, r_best, obj_best = C_lin.copy(), r_exact.copy(), obj_exact\n              C_anchor = C_lin.copy()\n              delta = min(0.07, 1.18 * delta)\n          else:\n              # Conservative anchor update and reduce delta\n              C_anchor = 0.7 * C_anchor + 0.3 * C_lin\n              delta = max(0.008, 0.85 * delta)\n      return best_C, r_best, obj_best\n\n  # ---------------- Block-Newton polish using LP duals ----------------\n\n  def _dual_grad_hess(C: np.ndarray, y_pairs, IJ, eps: float = 1e-12):\n      \"\"\"\n      Per-circle gradient and 2x2 Hessian blocks from pair duals:\n        g_i = sum_{(i,j)} y_ij * u_ij\n        H_i ≈ sum_{(i,j)}\
    \ (y_ij / d_ij) * (I - u_ij u_ij^T)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      G = np.zeros_like(C)\n      H = np.zeros((n, 2, 2), float)\n      if y_pairs is None:\n          return G, H\n      I, J = IJ\n      V = C[I] - C[J]\n      d = np.linalg.norm(V, axis=1)\n      d = np.maximum(d, eps)\n      U = (V.T / d).T\n      YU = (y_pairs.reshape(-1,1) * U)\n      np.add.at(G, I, YU)\n      np.add.at(G, J, -YU)\n      y_over_d = (y_pairs / d)\n      I2 = np.eye(2)\n      uuT = np.einsum('bi,bj->bij', U, U)\n      M = y_over_d.reshape(-1,1,1) * (I2 - uuT)\n      np.add.at(H, I, M)\n      np.add.at(H, J, M)\n      return G, H\n\n  def _solve_2x2(A: np.ndarray, b: np.ndarray, lam: float = 1e-3):\n      A2 = A + lam * np.eye(2)\n      try:\n          return np.linalg.solve(A2, b)\n      except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n          nrm = np.linalg.norm(b)\n          return (b / nrm) if nrm > 0 else np.zeros_like(b)\n\n  def _block_newton_polish(C0: np.ndarray, steps: int = 40, step_max: float =\
    \ 0.02, lam0: float = 1e-3):\n      C = C0.copy()\n      r, obj, ok, y_pairs, IJ = _solve_radii_exact(C)\n      if not ok:\n          return C0, r, obj\n      best_C, best_r, best_obj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n      lam = lam0\n\n      for _ in range(steps):\n          G, H = _dual_grad_hess(C, y_pairs, IJ)\n          S = np.zeros_like(C)\n          for i in range(C.shape[0]):\n              s_i = _solve_2x2(H[i], G[i], lam=lam)\n              nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(s_i))\n              if nrm > step_max and nrm > 0:\n                  s_i = (step_max / nrm) * s_i\n              S[i] = s_i\n          # short backtracking\n          improved = False\n          for a in (0.6, 0.35, 0.2):\n              C_try = _clip_box(C + a * S, margin=1e-6)\n              r_try, obj_try, ok, y_pairs_try, IJ_try = _solve_radii_exact(C_try)\n              if ok and obj_try > obj + 1e-12:\n                  C, r, obj = C_try, r_try, obj_try\n                  y_pairs, IJ = y_pairs_try, IJ_try\n  \
    \                improved = True\n                  break\n          if improved:\n              if obj > best_obj + 1e-12:\n                  best_C, best_r, best_obj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n              lam = max(1e-4, 0.9 * lam)\n              step_max = min(0.035, 1.05 * step_max)\n          else:\n              lam = min(1e-2, 1.4 * lam)\n              step_max = max(0.008, 0.8 * step_max)\n      return best_C, best_r, best_obj\n\n  # ---------------- Seed layouts ----------------\n\n  def _rows_y_positions(rows: int, margin: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if rows <= 1:\n          return np.array([0.5], dtype=float)\n      return np.linspace(margin, 1.0 - margin, rows)\n\n  def _row_linspace(k: int, margin_x: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if k <= 1:\n          return np.array([0.5], dtype=float)\n      return np.linspace(margin_x, 1.0 - margin_x, k)\n\n  def _make_7row_alt_5_4(y_margin: float, m5: float, m4: float, delta_4: float):\n      counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]\n      ys = _rows_y_positions(len(counts),\
    \ y_margin)\n      xs5 = _row_linspace(5, m5)\n      xs4 = np.clip(_row_linspace(4, m4) + delta_4, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n      C = []\n      for rid, k in enumerate(counts):\n          xs = xs5 if k == 5 else xs4\n          for x in xs:\n              C.append([x, ys[rid]])\n      return _clip_box(np.array(C, dtype=float))\n\n  def _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      s = 1.0 / 6.0\n      r0 = 0.5 * s\n      xs = r0 + s * np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n      ys = r0 + s * np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n      centers = []\n      for i in range(6):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if (i == 0 and j == 0) or (i == 0 and j == 5) or (i == 5 and j == 0) or (i == 5 and j == 5):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n      C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n      r = np.full(32, r0 * (1.0 - 1e-12), dtype=float)\n      return C, r, float(np.sum(r))\n\n  # ---------------- Persistence ----------------\n\n  SAVE_PATH = 'storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz'\n\
    \n  def _load_persisted():\n      if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH):\n          try:\n              data = np.load(SAVE_PATH)\n              C = data['centers'].astype(float)\n              r = data['radii'].astype(float)\n              if C.shape == (32, 2) and r.shape == (32,):\n                  return C, r, float(np.sum(r))\n          except Exception:\n              return None\n      return None\n\n  def _save_best(C, r):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n          np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=C, radii=r, obj=float(np.sum(r)))\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  # ---------------- Main entry ----------------\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n\n      # Strong baseline (non-regression)\n      C_base, r_base, obj_base = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n      best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_base, r_base, obj_base\n\n      # Gather starts: persisted best + several 7-row 5/4 seeds\n      starts = []\n\n      persisted\
    \ = _load_persisted()\n      if persisted is not None:\n          Cp, rp, objp = persisted\n          rp2, objp2, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Cp)\n          if ok:\n              starts.append((objp2, Cp))\n\n      seeds = [\n          (0.10,  0.08, 0.08,  0.00),\n          (0.105, 0.085, 0.085, 0.015),\n          (0.11,  0.08, 0.08,  0.02),\n          (0.115, 0.085, 0.085, -0.015),\n          (0.12,  0.07, 0.07, -0.02),\n      ]\n      for (ym, m5, m4, d4) in seeds:\n          C0 = _make_7row_alt_5_4(ym, m5, m4, d4)\n          r0, obj0, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(C0)\n          if ok:\n              starts.append((obj0, C0))\n\n      # Rank and keep top 3 starts\n      starts.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n      starts = starts[:3] if starts else []\n\n      # Run MM-LP on each start (moderate iterations), keep best\n      for obj0, C0 in starts:\n          C_mm, R_mm, O_mm = _mm_lp_optimize(C0, iters=34, delta0=0.015, margin=1e-6)\n          if O_mm > best_obj + 1e-12:\n\
    \              best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_mm, R_mm, O_mm\n\n      # Polish with block-Newton on the current best\n      C_pol, R_pol, O_pol = _block_newton_polish(best_C, steps=44, step_max=0.022, lam0=1e-3)\n      if O_pol > best_obj + 1e-12:\n          best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_pol, R_pol, O_pol\n\n      # Final strict feasibility and validation; fallback if needed\n      best_r = _safety_shrink(best_C, best_r)\n      if not _validate(best_C, best_r) or best_obj < obj_base - 1e-9:\n          return C_base, r_base\n\n      _save_best(best_C, best_r)\n      return best_C, best_r\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering optimization strategies**\n\nI’m thinking about potential improvements for my approach, like using more trust region steps with a two-phase schedule, where I increase the coarse delta until I see no improvement, and then switch to smaller changes, maybe over 30 iterations. \n\nTrying various starting seeds is also a good idea, along with using multiple anchors from the top three seeds while keeping iterations smaller to save time. I’ll refine everything further with coordinate adjustments and implement an early stopping time limit to ensure efficiency while running the process.**Implementing optimization enhancements**\n\nI want to ensure safety in my code while considering a few improvements. First, I plan to add strict feasibility shrink and include a “persist best” feature. \n\nI’m proposing a new submission combining multi-start MM-LP with exact LP refinement and micro-jitter. I’ll use seeds from the best persisted results and triangular patterns. The\
  \ approach will involve a delta schedule during optimization, refining with dual-gradient or block Newton adjustments afterwards. \n\nAdditionally, I'll update anchors accordingly and incorporate pair-splitting if the MM-LP step fails.**Refining optimization techniques**\n\nI’m diving into the earlier block-Newton method, which used dual weights requiring y_pairs. Now, I think we can utilize gradients from the exact distances, but it’s tricky since the gradient of the sum of radii concerning centers isn’t straightforward. I’ll extract duals from the HiGHS solver and keep the block Newton code referencing y_pairs, and if those are absent, I’ll look at slacks from the exact LP for heuristics.\n\nThere’s also the idea of combining local micro jitter with worst circle relocation, but I need to be mindful of increasing code complexity and staying within the token budget. Currently, I’m at 93k tokens but have some room left for submissions and may write a best file for storage and analysis later\
  \ on.**Creating a refined submission**\n\nI'm planning to produce a new submission called \"Multi-start MM-LP v2 + block Newton polish.\" This will combine earlier functions with an enhanced schedule, targeting about 20 iterations per start with two starts in total. I’d like to implement a two-phase acceptance criterion, keeping it if the exact objective improves by more than 1e-10.\n\nI’ll structure the code clearly and include necessary functions like _pairwise_indices, _boundary_margins, and others. The core will focus on distance linearization while maintaining a trust region. \n\nAfter selecting the best MM-LP result, I'll run a block Newton refinement with a cap of 40 iterations and a step maximum of 0.02, ensuring to set \"persist best.\"**Optimizing code submission**\n\nI’ve improved our solution to 2.87826 and I'm aiming for over 2.9 with careful new code. At the end, I’ll ensure we return best_C and best_r after applying a shrink. \n\nI’ll include error handling, resist bigger\
  \ loops, and keep iterations low to avoid timeouts when crafting the YAML submission titled \"Multi-start MM-LP (distance linearization) + block-Newton polish (safe, persisted).\"\n\nWe might revise the MM-LP formulation so that boundary constraints are only applied as needed, ensuring circles fit within the square. I'll also establish trust region bounds and use a single \"linprog\" for each step, optimizing to keep within time limits.\n\nNow I’ll generate the code and include minimal commentary before executing the submission."
