- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 40\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 176,907 / 270,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 40 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Fast loader: return persisted best packing with strict feasibility guard (fallback to quick grid)' (ID: 105) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.926307382593416\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.926307\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research\
    \ submission 'SOCP-refined aggressive multi-start: MM-LP + relocations + line-search + block-Newton, then cvxpy polish (persist if improved)' (ID: 102) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9292366192126282\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.929237\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 102\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing function error. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.93.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) called a function `_refine_seed()` on line 246 that was never defined in the code. This function was intended to apply aggressive multi-stage refinement to seed configurations using various optimization techniques (MM-LP, relocations, line-search, block-Newton polish).\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. The agent planned to implement a sophisticated refinement pipeline\n2. The function call was added to `construct_packing()`\n3. The actual implementation of\
    \ `_refine_seed()` was never written\n\nThis is a classic case of incomplete implementation - the function signature was referenced but the function body was missing.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated the missing `_refine_seed()` function in `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following implementation:\n\n```python\ndef _refine_seed(C0: np.ndarray, rnd_seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"Apply aggressive multi-stage refinement to a seed configuration.\"\"\"\n    # Start from seed\n    Cb, rb, ob = C0.copy(), None, 0.0\n    rb, ob, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Cb)\n    if not ok:\n        return Cb, rb, ob\n\n    # Stage 1: MM-LP optimization\n    C1, r1, o1 = _mm_lp_optimize(Cb, iters=32, delta0=0.016)\n    if o1 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C1, r1, o1\n\n    # Stage 2: Relocate worst circles\n    C2, r2, o2 = _relocate_worst(Cb, rb, trials=3, grid_n=21, topk=14)\n    if o2 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C2, r2, o2\n\n    # Stage 3: Two-worst relocate\n    C3, r3, o3 = _two_worst_relocate(Cb,\
    \ rb, grid_n=19, topk=8)\n    if o3 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C3, r3, o3\n\n    # Stage 4: Per-circle line search\n    C4, r4, o4 = _per_circle_line_search(Cb, steps=60, step=0.0095, seed=rnd_seed)\n    if o4 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C4, r4, o4\n\n    # Stage 5: Block-Newton polish\n    C5, r5, o5 = _block_newton_polish(Cb, steps=30, step_max=0.020, lam0=1e-3)\n    if o5 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C5, r5, o5\n\n    return Cb, rb, ob\n```\n\nThe function implements a 5-stage refinement pipeline:\n1. **MM-LP optimization**: Trust-region based majorization-minimization\n2. **Relocate worst**: Grid-based relocation of the smallest circle\n3. **Two-worst relocate**: Joint optimization of two smallest circles\n4. **Per-circle line search**: Stochastic gradient-based and push-based movements\n5. **Block-Newton polish**: Second-order optimization using dual information\n\nEach stage conditionally updates the best configuration only if it improves the objective (sum\
    \ of radii).\n\n## Verification\n- Executed `monitor_evaluation.py 2` to verify the fix\n- Code ran successfully without errors\n- Achieved score: **2.9292366192126282**\n- Exit code: 0 (success with score)\n\n## Conclusion\nThe fix was straightforward - implementing the missing function with a logical sequence of the refinement techniques that were already available in the codebase. The agent's overall approach was sound; it simply forgot to implement one critical function before calling it.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\n\n# Optional deps\nCVXPY_AVAILABLE = False\nSCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\ntry:\n    import cvxpy as cp\n    CVXPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    CVXPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n\
    \    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\nSAVE_PATH = 'storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz'\n\n# ---------------- Utilities ----------------\n\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _pair_indices(n: int):\n    I = []\n    J = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i); J.append(j)\n    return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\ndef _pairwise_distances(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n    return np.sqrt(np.maximum(d2, 0.0))\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    if C.shape != (32, 2) or r.shape != (32,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <=\
    \ 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n    r2 = np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C)).astype(float) * factor\n    r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r2):\n            break\n        r2 *= 0.95\n    r2 = np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n    return r2\n\n# ---------------- Exact LP for radii (given centers) ----------------\n\ndef _solve_radii_exact(C: np.ndarray):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        r = np.minimum(b, 1.0/12.0) * 0.999\n        return r, float(np.sum(r)),\
    \ True, None, (None, None)\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n    A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, (None, None)\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n    y_pairs = None\n    I_ret, J_ret = None, None\n    try:\n        if hasattr(res, \"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin, \"marginals\") and res.ineqlin.marginals is not None:\n            y_pairs = np.maximum(0.0, np.asarray(res.ineqlin.marginals, dtype=float))\n            I_ret, J_ret = I, J\n    except Exception:\n        y_pairs = None\n    return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I_ret, J_ret)\n\n# ----------------\
    \ Seeds and persistence ----------------\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s = 1.0 / 6.0\n    r0 = 0.5 * s\n    xs = r0 + s * np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s * np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i == 0 and j == 0) or (i == 0 and j == 5) or (i == 5 and j == 0) or (i == 5 and j == 5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\ndef _seed_7row_5_4(y_margin: float = 0.11, m5: float = 0.08, m4: float = 0.08, phase: float = 0.02):\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]\n    ys = np.linspace(y_margin, 1.0 - y_margin, len(counts))\n    def row(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0 - m, k) if k > 1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n    xs5 = row(5, m5); xs4 = _clip01(row(4, m4) + phase)\n    C = []\n    rid = 0\n    for k in counts:\n        xs = xs5 if k == 5 else xs4\n        for x in xs:\n            C.append([x, ys[rid]])\n        rid\
    \ += 1\n    return np.array(C, dtype=float)\n\ndef _rot(theta: float):\n    c, s = np.cos(theta), np.sin(theta)\n    return np.array([[c, -s], [s, c]], float)\n\ndef _tri_lattice(theta: float, s: float, tx: float, ty: float, margin: float = 1e-4):\n    R = _rot(theta)\n    u = R @ np.array([s, 0.0]); v = R @ np.array([0.5*s, (np.sqrt(3)/2.0)*s])\n    span = 1.0 + 2.0*s\n    N = int(np.ceil(span / max(1e-6, np.linalg.norm(u)))) + int(np.ceil(span / max(1e-6, np.linalg.norm(v)))) + 2\n    pts = []\n    t = np.array([tx, ty], float)\n    for i in range(-N, N + 1):\n        for j in range(-N, N + 1):\n            p = t + i*u + j*v\n            if (margin <= p[0] <= 1.0 - margin) and (margin <= p[1] <= 1.0 - margin):\n                pts.append(p)\n    if not pts:\n        return np.zeros((0, 2), float)\n    return _clip01(np.array(pts, float), eps=1e-6)\n\ndef _prune_to_32(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    Cw = C.copy()\n    while Cw.shape[0] > 32:\n        D = _pairwise_distances(Cw)\n\
    \        dnn = np.min(D, axis=1)\n        b = _boundary_margins(Cw)\n        score = np.minimum(dnn, 2.0 * b)\n        idx = int(np.argmin(score))\n        Cw = np.delete(Cw, idx, axis=0)\n    return Cw\n\ndef _farthest_sampling(n: int = 32, margin: float = 0.02, candidates: int = 600, seed: int = 0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    C = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], float)]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        cand = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(candidates, 2))\n        exist = np.array(C, float)\n        d2 = np.sum((cand[:, None, :] - exist[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2>0))\n        min_to_pts = np.min(d, axis=1); b = _boundary_margins(cand)\n        score = np.minimum(min_to_pts, 2.0 * b)\n        C.append(cand[int(np.argmax(score))])\n    return _clip01(np.array(C, float))\n\ndef _load_seeds(n=32):\n    seeds = []\n    persisted = None\n    if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH):\n        try:\n            data = np.load(SAVE_PATH)\n\
    \            Cp = data['centers'].astype(float); rp = data['radii'].astype(float); objp = float(np.sum(rp))\n            if Cp.shape == (n, 2) and rp.shape == (n,):\n                seeds.append((objp, Cp, rp))\n                persisted = objp\n        except Exception:\n            persisted = None\n    # Row seeds\n    for (ym, m5, m4, ph) in [(0.10, 0.08, 0.08, 0.00), (0.11, 0.08, 0.08, 0.02), (0.115, 0.085, 0.085, -0.015), (0.105, 0.085, 0.085, 0.015)]:\n        C = _seed_7row_5_4(y_margin=ym, m5=m5, m4=m4, phase=ph)\n        r, obj, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(C)\n        if ok: seeds.append((obj, C, r))\n    # Rotated hex seeds\n    for th in [0.0, np.pi*0.03, -np.pi*0.03, np.pi*0.06]:\n        for s in [0.160, 0.168, 0.176]:\n            for fx in [0.0, 0.5]:\n                for fy in [0.0, 0.5]:\n                    Cr = _tri_lattice(th, s, fx*s, fy*s)\n                    if Cr.shape[0] >= 32:\n                        Cr = _prune_to_32(Cr)\n                        r, obj,\
    \ ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Cr)\n                        if ok: seeds.append((obj, Cr, r))\n    # Farthest seeds\n    for sd in [101, 202, 303, 404]:\n        C = _farthest_sampling(n=32, margin=0.02, candidates=650, seed=sd)\n        r, obj, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(C)\n        if ok: seeds.append((obj, C, r))\n    seeds.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n    best_known = seeds[0][0] if seeds else 0.0\n    return seeds[:10], (persisted if persisted is not None else best_known)\n\ndef _save_best_if_improved(C, r, prev_best_obj):\n    try:\n        obj = float(np.sum(r))\n        if obj > prev_best_obj + 1e-12:\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n            np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=C, radii=r, obj=obj)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n# ---------------- MM-LP trust-region core ----------------\n\ndef _mm_lp_step(C0: np.ndarray, delta: float, margin: float = 1e-6):\n    n = C0.shape[0]\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        return C0,\
    \ *_solve_radii_exact(C0), True\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n    V0 = C0[I] - C0[J]\n    d0 = np.linalg.norm(V0, axis=1)\n    eps = 1e-9\n    d0 = np.maximum(d0, eps)\n    U = (V0.T / d0).T\n    ux = U[:, 0]; uy = U[:, 1]\n    x0 = C0[:, 0]; y0 = C0[:, 1]\n    rows = 4 * n + len(I)\n    cols = 3 * n\n    A_ub = np.zeros((rows, cols), dtype=float)\n    b_ub = np.zeros(rows, dtype=float)\n    def idx_r(i): return i\n    def idx_x(i): return n + i\n    def idx_y(i): return 2 * n + i\n    row = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] = -1.0; b_ub[row] = 0.0; row += 1\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] = 1.0;  b_ub[row] = 1.0; row += 1\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] = -1.0; b_ub[row] = 0.0; row += 1\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] = 1.0; A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] = 1.0;  b_ub[row] = 1.0; row += 1\n    for k in range(len(I)):\n        i = int(I[k]); j = int(J[k])\n        A_ub[row, idx_r(i)] += 1.0\n        A_ub[row,\
    \ idx_r(j)] += 1.0\n        A_ub[row, idx_x(i)] += -ux[k]\n        A_ub[row, idx_y(i)] += -uy[k]\n        A_ub[row, idx_x(j)] += +ux[k]\n        A_ub[row, idx_y(j)] += +uy[k]\n        b_ub[row] = d0[k] - ux[k] * x0[i] - uy[k] * y0[i] + ux[k] * x0[j] + uy[k] * y0[j]\n        row += 1\n    c = np.zeros(cols, dtype=float); c[:n] = -1.0\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n): bounds.append((0.0, 0.5))\n    for i in range(n):\n        lo = float(max(margin, x0[i] - delta)); hi = float(min(1.0 - margin, x0[i] + delta))\n        bounds.append((lo, hi))\n    for i in range(n):\n        lo = float(max(margin, y0[i] - delta)); hi = float(min(1.0 - margin, y0[i] + delta))\n        bounds.append((lo, hi))\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n        return C0, np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n    x = res.x\n    r = x[:n].astype(float)\n    X = x[n:n + n].astype(float)\n    Y = x[n + n:].astype(float)\n\
    \    C_new = np.stack([X, Y], axis=1)\n    return C_new, r, float(-res.fun), True\ndef _mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int = 32, delta0: float = 0.016):\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    r_best, obj_best, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(best_C)\n    if not ok: return C_start, r_best, obj_best\n    delta = float(delta0)\n    C_anchor = C_start.copy()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        C_lin, r_lin, obj_lin, ok_lin = _mm_lp_step(C_anchor, delta=delta, margin=1e-6)\n        if not ok_lin:\n            delta = max(0.008, 0.6 * delta); continue\n        r_exact, obj_exact, ok_ex, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(C_lin)\n        if ok_ex and obj_exact > obj_best + 1e-12:\n            best_C, r_best, obj_best = C_lin.copy(), r_exact.copy(), obj_exact\n            C_anchor = C_lin.copy()\n            delta = min(0.06, 1.18 * delta)\n        else:\n            C_anchor = 0.7 * C_anchor + 0.3 * C_lin\n            delta = max(0.008, 0.85 * delta)\n    return best_C, r_best, obj_best\n\n# ----------------\
    \ Gradient/push line-search ----------------\n\ndef _dual_grad(C: np.ndarray, y_pairs, IJ, eps: float = 1e-12):\n    n = C.shape[0]; G = np.zeros_like(C)\n    if y_pairs is None or IJ[0] is None: return G\n    I, J = IJ\n    V = C[I] - C[J]; d = np.linalg.norm(V, axis=1); d = np.maximum(d, eps)\n    U = (V.T / d).T\n    YU = (y_pairs.reshape(-1,1) * U); np.add.at(G, I, YU); np.add.at(G, J, -YU)\n    return G\n\ndef _nearest_push(C: np.ndarray, idx: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = C - C[idx]; d2 = np.sum(diff*diff, axis=1); d2[idx] = np.inf\n    j = int(np.argmin(d2)); v = C[idx] - C[j]; nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n    if nrm == 0.0: return np.array([1.0, 0.0], float)\n    return v / nrm\n\ndef _per_circle_line_search(C: np.ndarray, steps: int = 60, step: float = 0.0095, seed: int = 0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    Cb = C.copy(); rb, ob, ok, y_pairs, IJ = _solve_radii_exact(Cb)\n    if not ok: return C, rb, ob\n    for _ in range(steps):\n        i = int(rng.integers(0,\
    \ Cb.shape[0]))\n        G = _dual_grad(Cb, y_pairs, IJ)\n        dirs = []\n        gi = G[i]; nrm = np.linalg.norm(gi)\n        if nrm > 0: dirs.append(gi / nrm)\n        dirs.append(_nearest_push(Cb, i))\n        improved = False\n        for u in dirs:\n            for s in (step, 0.7*step, 0.5*step):\n                Ct = Cb.copy(); Ct[i] = _clip01(Cb[i] + s * u)\n                rt, ot, ok2, y2, IJ2 = _solve_radii_exact(Ct)\n                if ok2 and ot > ob + 1e-12:\n                    Cb, rb, ob, y_pairs, IJ = Ct, rt, ot, y2, IJ2\n                    improved = True; break\n            if improved: break\n    return Cb, rb, ob\n\n# ---------------- Clearance relocations ----------------\n\ndef _clearance_candidates(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, grid_n: int = 21, topk: int = 14):\n    n = C.shape[0]; w = int(np.argmin(r))\n    g = np.linspace(1e-4, 1.0 - 1e-4, grid_n)\n    GX, GY = np.meshgrid(g, g, indexing=\"xy\"); P = np.stack([GX.ravel(), GY.ravel()]).T\n    mask = np.ones(n,\
    \ bool); mask[w] = False\n    Co = C[mask]; ro = r[mask]\n    bx = np.minimum(P[:,0], 1.0 - P[:,0]); by = np.minimum(P[:,1], 1.0 - P[:,1]); bP = np.minimum(bx, by)\n    diff = P[:,None,:] - Co[None,:,:]; d = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff*diff, axis=-1))\n    feas = np.min(d - ro[None,:], axis=1)\n    est = np.maximum(0.0, np.minimum(bP, feas))\n    idxs = np.argsort(-est)[:topk]\n    return w, P[idxs]\n\ndef _relocate_worst(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, trials: int = 3, grid_n: int = 21, topk: int = 14):\n    Cb = C.copy(); rb = r.copy(); ob = float(np.sum(rb))\n    for _ in range(trials):\n        w, cand = _clearance_candidates(Cb, rb, grid_n=grid_n, topk=topk)\n        best_local = ob; Cbest = Cb; rbest = rb\n        for p in cand:\n            Ct = Cb.copy(); Ct[w] = p; Ct = _clip01(Ct)\n            rt, ot, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Ct)\n            if ok and ot > best_local + 1e-12:\n                best_local, Cbest, rbest = ot, Ct, rt\n        if best_local > ob + 1e-12:\n           \
    \ Cb, rb, ob = Cbest, rbest, best_local\n    return Cb, rb, ob\n\ndef _two_worst_relocate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, grid_n: int = 19, topk: int = 8):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    idxs = np.argsort(r)[:2]\n    i1, i2 = int(idxs[0]), int(idxs[1])\n    g = np.linspace(1e-4, 1.0 - 1e-4, grid_n)\n    GX, GY = np.meshgrid(g, g, indexing=\"xy\"); P = np.stack([GX.ravel(), GY.ravel()]).T\n\n    def topk_for(i):\n        mask = np.ones(n, bool); mask[i] = False\n        Co = C[mask]; ro = r[mask]\n        bx = np.minimum(P[:,0], 1.0 - P[:,0]); by = np.minimum(P[:,1], 1.0 - P[:,1]); bP = np.minimum(bx, by)\n        diff = P[:,None,:] - Co[None,:,:]; d = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff*diff, axis=-1))\n        feas = np.min(d - ro[None,:], axis=1)\n        est = np.maximum(0.0, np.minimum(bP, feas))\n        return P[np.argsort(-est)[:topk]]\n\n    Cand1 = topk_for(i1); Cand2 = topk_for(i2)\n    best_C = C.copy(); best_r = r.copy(); best_obj = float(np.sum(r))\n    for a in Cand1:\n        for b in Cand2:\n\
    \            Ct = C.copy()\n            Ct[i1] = a; Ct[i2] = b\n            Ct = _clip01(Ct)\n            rt, ot, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Ct)\n            if ok and ot > best_obj + 1e-12:\n                best_C, best_r, best_obj = Ct, rt, ot\n    return best_C, best_r, best_obj\n\n# ---------------- Block-Newton polish ----------------\n\ndef _dual_grad_hess(C: np.ndarray, y_pairs, IJ, eps: float = 1e-12):\n    n = C.shape[0]; G = np.zeros_like(C); H = np.zeros((n,2,2), float)\n    if y_pairs is None or IJ[0] is None: return G, H\n    I, J = IJ\n    V = C[I] - C[J]; d = np.linalg.norm(V, axis=1); d = np.maximum(d, eps)\n    U = (V.T / d).T\n    YU = (y_pairs.reshape(-1,1) * U); np.add.at(G, I, YU); np.add.at(G, J, -YU)\n    y_over_d = (y_pairs / d)\n    I2 = np.eye(2); uuT = np.einsum('bi,bj->bij', U, U)\n    M = y_over_d.reshape(-1,1,1) * (I2 - uuT); np.add.at(H, I, M); np.add.at(H, J, M)\n    return G, H\n\ndef _solve_2x2(A: np.ndarray, b: np.ndarray, lam: float = 1e-3):\n   \
    \ A2 = A + lam * np.eye(2)\n    try: return np.linalg.solve(A2, b)\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        nrm = np.linalg.norm(b); return (b / nrm) if nrm > 0 else np.zeros_like(b)\n\ndef _block_newton_polish(C0: np.ndarray, steps: int = 30, step_max: float = 0.020, lam0: float = 1e-3):\n    C = C0.copy()\n    r, obj, ok, y_pairs, IJ = _solve_radii_exact(C)\n    if not ok: return C0, r, obj\n    best_C, best_r, best_obj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n    lam = lam0\n    for _ in range(30):\n        G, H = _dual_grad_hess(C, y_pairs, IJ)\n        S = np.zeros_like(C)\n        for i in range(C.shape[0]):\n            s_i = _solve_2x2(H[i], G[i], lam=lam)\n            nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(s_i))\n            if nrm > step_max and nrm > 0: s_i = (step_max / nrm) * s_i\n            S[i] = s_i\n        improved = False\n        for a in (0.6, 0.35, 0.2):\n            Ct = _clip01(C + a * S)\n            rt, ot, ok2, y2, IJ2 = _solve_radii_exact(Ct)\n            if ok2 and ot > obj +\
    \ 1e-12:\n                C, r, obj = Ct, rt, ot\n                y_pairs, IJ = y2, IJ2\n                improved = True; break\n        if improved:\n            if obj > best_obj + 1e-12:\n                best_C, best_r, best_obj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n            lam = max(1e-4, 0.9 * lam); step_max = min(0.035, 1.05 * step_max)\n        else:\n            lam = min(1e-2, 1.35 * lam); step_max = max(0.008, 0.85 * step_max)\n    return best_C, best_r, best_obj\n\n# ---------------- SOCP polish via cvxpy (accept only if improves) ----------------\n\ndef _socp_polish(C_init: np.ndarray):\n    if not CVXPY_AVAILABLE:\n        return None, None, False\n    n = 32\n    r = cp.Variable(n, nonneg=True)\n    x = cp.Variable(n)\n    y = cp.Variable(n)\n    cons = [x >= 0, x <= 1, y >= 0, y <= 1, r <= x, r <= 1 - x, r <= y, r <= 1 - y]\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n    for i, j in zip(I, J):\n        cons.append(cp.norm(cp.hstack([x[i] - x[j], y[i] - y[j]]), 2) >= r[i] + r[j])\n    obj =\
    \ cp.Maximize(cp.sum(r))\n    prob = cp.Problem(obj, cons)\n    try:\n        x.value = C_init[:, 0]\n        y.value = C_init[:, 1]\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    solved = False\n    for solver, kwargs in [\n        (cp.ECOS, dict(abstol=1e-8, reltol=1e-8, feastol=1e-8, max_iters=4000, verbose=False)),\n        (cp.SCS,  dict(max_iters=8000, eps=5e-7, alpha=1.5, verbose=False))\n    ]:\n        try:\n            prob.solve(solver=solver, **kwargs)\n            if prob.status in (cp.OPTIMAL, cp.OPTIMAL_INACCURATE):\n                solved = True\n                break\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n    if not solved or x.value is None or y.value is None or r.value is None:\n        return None, None, False\n    C = np.column_stack([np.array(x.value).astype(float), np.array(y.value).astype(float)])\n    rr = np.array(r.value).astype(float)\n    return C, rr, True\n\n# ---------------- Missing _refine_seed function ----------------\n\ndef _refine_seed(C0:\
    \ np.ndarray, rnd_seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"Apply aggressive multi-stage refinement to a seed configuration.\"\"\"\n    # Start from seed\n    Cb, rb, ob = C0.copy(), None, 0.0\n    rb, ob, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Cb)\n    if not ok:\n        return Cb, rb, ob\n\n    # Stage 1: MM-LP optimization\n    C1, r1, o1 = _mm_lp_optimize(Cb, iters=32, delta0=0.016)\n    if o1 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C1, r1, o1\n\n    # Stage 2: Relocate worst circles\n    C2, r2, o2 = _relocate_worst(Cb, rb, trials=3, grid_n=21, topk=14)\n    if o2 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C2, r2, o2\n\n    # Stage 3: Two-worst relocate\n    C3, r3, o3 = _two_worst_relocate(Cb, rb, grid_n=19, topk=8)\n    if o3 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C3, r3, o3\n\n    # Stage 4: Per-circle line search\n    C4, r4, o4 = _per_circle_line_search(Cb, steps=60, step=0.0095, seed=rnd_seed)\n    if o4 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C4, r4, o4\n\n    # Stage 5: Block-Newton polish\n    C5, r5, o5 = _block_newton_polish(Cb,\
    \ steps=30, step_max=0.020, lam0=1e-3)\n    if o5 > ob + 1e-12:\n        Cb, rb, ob = C5, r5, o5\n\n    return Cb, rb, ob\n\n# ---------------- Main entry ----------------\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    seeds, persisted_best = _load_seeds(n)\n    if not seeds:\n        Cb = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb, _, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Cb)\n        rb = _safety_shrink(Cb, rb)\n        return Cb, rb\n\n    best_C, best_r, best_obj = seeds[0][1], seeds[0][2], seeds[0][0]\n\n    # Aggressive basin-hopping per top seeds\n    for idx, (obj0, C0, r0) in enumerate(seeds[:8]):\n        Cb, Rb, Ob = _refine_seed(C0, rnd_seed=8000 + idx)\n        if Ob > best_obj + 1e-12:\n            best_C, best_r, best_obj = Cb, Rb, Ob\n\n    # Optional SOCP polish from current best; accept only if improves\n    C_socp, r_socp, ok = _socp_polish(best_C)\n    if ok:\n        rf, objf, ok2, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(C_socp)\n        if ok2 and objf > best_obj + 1e-12:\n  \
    \          best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_socp, rf, objf\n\n    # Strict feasibility and persistence\n    best_r = _safety_shrink(best_C, best_r, factor=0.999)\n    if not _validate(best_C, best_r):\n        Cb = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb, _, ok, *_ = _solve_radii_exact(Cb)\n        rb = _safety_shrink(Cb, rb)\n        return Cb, rb\n\n    try:\n        prev = float(persisted_best)\n    except Exception:\n        prev = 0.0\n    try:\n        if float(np.sum(best_r)) > prev + 1e-12:\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n            np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=best_C, radii=best_r, obj=float(np.sum(best_r)))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return best_C, best_r\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is\
    \ a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Fast loader: return persisted best packing with strict feasibility guard (fallback to quick grid)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 105.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 105 | 1 | Fast loader: return persisted best packing with strict feasibility guard (fallback to quick grid) | Verity I | 39 | 2.9263074 |\n| 102 | 1 | SOCP-refined aggressive multi-start: MM-LP + relocations + line-search + block-Newton, then cvxpy... | Verity I | 38 | 2.9292366 |\n| 99 | 1 | Aggressive diverse multi-start: MM-LP + two-worst clearance relocation + per-circle line-search +... | Verity I | 37 | 2.9292366 |\n| 97 | 1 | Basin-hopping MM-LP with clearance relocations, per-circle line search, and block-Newton polish (... | Verity I | 36 | 2.9292366 |\n| 93 | 1 | Diverse multi-start MM-LP + block-Newton (rows + rotated-hex + farthest) with persistence | Verity I | 35 | 2.9292366 |\n| 91 | 1 | Restored multi-start MM-LP + block-Newton (do-not-overwrite unless improved) | Verity I | 34 | 2.8392217 |\n| 87 | 1 | Hybrid SOCP→MM-LP→Block-Newton (ECOS-first, SCS retry) with LP finalize and strict shrink | Verity I | 33 | 2.8392217 |\n\
    | 84 | 1 | SOCP (cvxpy) joint optimization of centers+radii with exact LP finalize; MM-LP fallback | Verity I | 32 | 2.8392217 |\n| 79 | 1 | Exact joint NLP (trust-constr) for centers+radii with vector-Jacobians + LP finalize | Verity I | 31 | 1.5831923 |\n| 72 | 1 | Sparse-pairs MM-LP (nearest-neighbor cutting-plane) + block-Newton polish (persisted, safe) | Verity I | 27 | 2.8782627 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
