parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Circle Packing status @tick 41: 2.9292366 best, method recap and next steps\"\ntags: \"research, circle packing, methods, plan, persistence\"\ncontent: |\n  Status\n  - Best score: 2.9292366192126282 (valid).\n  - Persisted at: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz (centers, radii, obj).\n  - Reliable production paths:\n    1) Loader that returns persisted best as-is (no double-shrink), rebuilding radii via exact LP if needed.\n    2) Diverse multi-start with MM-LP trust-region + relocations (worst/two-worst) + per-circle line-search + LP-dual block-Newton polish (+ optional SOCP polish).\n\n  Methods summary (what worked)\n  - MM-LP (distance linearization + trust region) for joint centers+radii, accepted only via exact LP check.\n  - Clearance-field relocations of worst radii; “two-worst” joint relocation best-of-k grid.\n  - Per-circle line search: dual-gradient direction and nearest-neighbor push, short\
    \ step trials.\n  - Block-Newton using LP duals (pair multipliers) to build per-circle 2x2 curvature; Armijo-like backtracking.\n  - SOCP (cvxpy ECOS/SCS) can improve poor starts but plateaued below the heuristic peak unless combined after heuristic stages.\n  - Strict feasibility guard: multiplicative shrink (0.999) + iterative fallback; avoid nextafter-only shrink (risked borderline overlaps).\n  - Persistence discipline: only overwrite if strictly improved; loader avoids double-shrink loss.\n\n  What did not help or regressed\n  - “Pure” trust-constr NLP was unstable and gave poor scores (≈1.58) on this platform.\n  - SOCP alone (from simple seeds) plateaued ≈2.84; needed heuristic pre-polish to reach >2.92.\n  - Huge combinatorial searches can timeout; prefer targeted seeds + acceptance checks.\n\n  Repro tips\n  - Start from persisted best; if absent, generate seeds: 7-row 5/4 rows, rotated triangular lattices (prune to 32), farthest-point sampling.\n  - Run MM-LP (Δ≈0.015–0.016),\
    \ accept only if exact LP improves sum radii.\n  - Do (A) worst-circle clearance relocations (grid_n≈19–21, topk≈12–14), (B) two-worst joint relocation (limited topk×topk pairs).\n  - Per-circle line search (50–60 trials), try {step, 0.7×, 0.5×} on dual-gradient and nearest-push directions.\n  - Block-Newton (≈26–30 steps, step_max≈0.02, lam≈1e-3) with Armijo-like backtracking.\n  - Optional SOCP polish from current best; accept only if exact LP improves.\n\n  Next steps (research directions)\n  1) Contact-graph active-set Newton: Solve small KKT systems on the set of near-active pair constraints + boundary, adjusting centers with r re-optimized by LP each iteration (exact Newton/Levenberg–Marquardt on linearized distances). Our block-Newton is a diagonal approximation—full active-set could yield sharper steps.\n  2) Dual-aware target balancing: from LP duals build a “stress” equilibrium (desired distance increments) and solve a least-squares for center displacements under box constraints\
    \ (projected LS) before LP re-solve.\n  3) Structured super-seeding: richer rotated/anisotropic hex mosaics and “gap filling” seeds driven by clearance maps; add mild jitter and re-prune to 32.\n  4) Tighter accept/reject with model agreement: compare MM-LP linearized objective delta to exact LP delta; adapt trust region more aggressively.\n  5) Precision management: try selective higher-precision shapes for near-degenerate pairs (scipy highs tolerances or cvxpy solver tolerances) to reduce conservative shrink.\n\n  Engineering guardrails\n  - Deterministic RNG seeds for reproducibility; limit per-stage time and iterations to avoid 20 min cap.\n  - Persist only if improved; keep loader script as default submission for robustness.\n  - Avoid double-shrink: save strict-feasible radii once and reuse as-is.\n\n  Publishing plan (post-maturity)\n  - Prepare an Archive capsule with: (a) method overview, (b) ablations (each stage’s gain), (c) final code snapshot (loader + optimizer), (d) persisted\
    \ artifact checksum, and (e) guidance for descendant improvements.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering code adjustments**\n\nI’m thinking we might need to document to private memory more or shift to reflection for planning. The prompt doesn’t ask for any specific action, but I feel we should focus and perhaps stop submitting code to save tokens. \n\nThere’s a better approach: we could attempt smooth constraints via convex methods or compute gradients using KKT. However, that sounds heavy. I’m also considering refining our parameters for basin-hopping, which could yield improvements. There’s a time constraint too, so I need to prioritize robust coding.**Exploring improvement methods**\n\nI’ve noticed we’ve included block-Newton approximations using y_pairs and diagonal Hess approximations but am considering an additional improvement through contact balancing. The idea is to solve least squares to minimize violations in active constraints by moving centers slightly. However, moving the centers changes distances, so we can linearize distances and solve a small\
  \ quadratic program (QP). \n\nIf we can't use a QP solver, we can apply least squares to minimize the sum of weighted deviations. The goal is to increase distances along tight pairs by adjusting centers in the right directions.**Reviewing progress and options**\n\nI’m considering making improvements by intensifying the per-circle line search loops and trying different relocation combinations. However, the expected improvements seem small. Maybe it’s time to tidy things up and think about publishing to the Archive, but we’re in an isolation period. \n\nWith our current progress at 41 ticks, I can’t access Public Memory since maturity requires 50 ticks. The \"production loader\" ensures that we're always using the best found solution. I could write a summary for Private Memory and make suggestions for when I mature. But for now, I might just reflect or store a capsule.**Storing thoughts and ideas**\n\nI think it’s a good idea to store a summary in Private Memory, along with parameter snapshots,\
  \ reproducibility steps, and ideas like the contact graph active-set method. I’ll also consider global patterns and different seeds. \n\nFirst, I could verify the storage for the previous best file, even though we can’t read raw data. Next, I’ll create a capsule summarizing the results and my plan. I might also think about a minimal script for autoloading later, but I don’t need to rush that. Finally, I could run a loader test, but it isn’t essential.**Planning actions for memory storage**\n\nI need to take some specific actions. First, I’ll go to private memory and create a capsule that includes a summary, the best score, the approach, saved paths, reproduction steps, and next steps. \n\nThese next steps might involve things like the active-set contact graph QP or pseudo-Newton methods and refining the SOCP. I must be cautious about potential quoting issues with YAML since the content includes colons. Single-line titles need to be enclosed in quotes, so I’ll ensure I wrap those correctly.\
  \ Let’s move forward with this!"
