parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Design an Active-Set Newton (ASN) module to push our 32-circle packing beyond sum(r)=2.9292366 within the 20-minute limit, integrating cleanly with our current pipeline (MM-LP → ASN → Block-Newton → optional SOCP → exact LP finalize → strict shrink → persist-if-improved).\n\n  Targets:\n  - Use LP (HiGHS) duals to select an active set of near-tight constraints (pairs and boundary).\n  - Build a centers-only Newton step that predicts improvement in sum(r) and respects the box.\n  - Accept steps only if exact LP re-solve improves the true objective; adapt trust region and damping accordingly.\n\n  Concrete design questions:\n  1) Active-set builder:\n     - From LP duals: choose A_pair = {(i,j): y_ij ≥ τ_pair} and A_bound = {i,face: u_i,face ≥ τ_bound}.\n     - Add hysteresis: once active, keep if y ≥ τ_keep < τ_pair; allow drop if y < τ_drop.\n     - Cap sizes: top-K pairs by y_ij (e.g., K≈200–300) and per-circle at most one boundary\
    \ face.\n     - How to initialize τ_pair, τ_keep, τ_drop; and K versus runtime?\n\n  2) Newton system:\n     - Gradient per circle: g_i = Σ_(j∈N(i)∩A_pair) y_ij * u_ij + Σ_(face∈A_bound(i)) u_i,face * v_face,\n       where u_ij is unit from j→i and v_face is outward unit normal of nearest face.\n     - Curvature per circle (2×2): H_i = Σ_(j∈N(i)∩A_pair) (y_ij / d_ij) * (I − u_ij u_ijᵀ) + μI (damping μ>0).\n     - Solve (block-diagonal) (H_i) δc_i = g_i to get a proposed step; optionally add weak neighbor couplings on top-K pairs.\n     - Trust region: scale step by α ∈ {1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2}; clip to box (ε margin).\n\n  3) Acceptance and adaptation:\n     - Predicted gain: ĝ = Σ y_ij ⟨u_ij, δc_i − δc_j⟩ + Σ u_i,face ⟨v_face, δc_i⟩.\n     - Compute C' = clip(C + α δC); solve exact LP for r' and objective f' = Σ r'.\n     - Accept if f' > f + ε (ε≈1e-12); else reduce α or increase μ, or expand active set.\n     - Agreement ratio ρ = (f'−f) / ĝ; if ρ small, shrink trust region / raise μ;\
    \ if large, ease μ and possibly tighten τ.\n\n  4) Control flow and safeguards:\n     - Iterations: 5–10 ASN steps per seed (bounded).\n     - If 3 consecutive rejects, trigger clearance relocation or per-circle line search, then retry ASN once.\n     - Always finalize with exact LP + strict shrink; validate; persist only on strict improvement.\n\n  5) Parameter sketch for first trial:\n     - τ_pair = 1e-3; τ_keep = 6e-4; τ_drop = 3e-4; K_pairs ≈ 240.\n     - τ_bound = 1e-4; at most one face per circle.\n     - μ start = 1e-3; α candidates = [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]; ε = 1e-12; ε_box = 1e-6.\n\n  6) Integration plan:\n     - Implement ASN as a function: asn_refine(C, steps=8, params) → (C*, r*, obj*).\n     - Insert after our MM-LP stage, before Block-Newton; time-box ASN to ~2–3 minutes per top seed.\n     - Log acceptance stats and active-set sizes; fail safe to current best if ASN stalls.\n\n  Think through edge-cases:\n  - Degenerate pairs (very small d_ij): guard by ε in d, cap y_ij\
    \ contributions.\n  - Boundary conflicts when moving away from one face increases pressure on the opposite face; rely on exact LP acceptance gate.\n  - Numeric stability: prefer float64; moderate μ to avoid singular H_i.\n\n  Deliverable next turn: skeleton code for ASN module with active-set builder, g/H assembly, line search+accept loop, plugged into our best multi-start pipeline.\ntick: 5\n```"
