tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "Thoughts (Tick 1/5): Concrete ASN design, thresholds, and skeleton\n\n1) Active-set builder (from LP duals)\n- Inputs: centers C ∈ R^{32×2}, exact LP solution r, objective f = Σr, LP duals:\n  - Pairwise y_ij ≥ 0 for constraints r_i + r_j ≤ ||c_i − c_j|| (only for i<j),\n  - Boundary duals u_i,face ≥ 0 for faces {left (x≥r), right (1−x≥r), down (y≥r), up (1−y≥r)}; many LP APIs expose upper-bound marginals; compute per-face duals consistently.\n- Thresholds and caps:\n  - Start τ_pair = 1e−3, τ_keep = 6e−4, τ_drop = 3e−4.\n  - Let K_pairs = 240 cap. Build candidates S = {(i,j) : y_ij ≥ τ_keep}. Enforce hysteresis:\n    - If (i,j) was active last iteration and y_ij ≥ τ_drop, keep it (until set needs trimming).\n    - Otherwise require y_ij ≥ τ_pair to add.\n  - If |S| > K_pairs: keep top-K_pairs by y_ij.\n  - Boundary: for each i, choose at most one face with maximum u_i,face if max ≥ τ_bound (τ_bound ≈ 1e−4). Hysteresis analogous: keep if ≥ τ_bound/2, else drop.\n- Auto-tuning (first\
    \ iteration): If too few active pairs (|S|<60), drop τ_pair by ×0.5 until |S|≥60 or τ_pair hits 2e−4; if too many (|S|>K_pairs), increase τ_pair ×1.2 until within cap. Record τ history to dampen oscillations.\n\n2) Newton system (centers-only)\n- Geometry:\n  - For each active pair (i,j), define vector v_ij = c_i − c_j, d_ij = ||v_ij|| (guard d_ij ← max(d_ij, ε_d) with ε_d ≈ 1e−9), unit u_ij = v_ij / d_ij.\n  - For boundary face selections, set v_face as outward normal:\n    - left: [1,0], right: [−1,0], down: [0,1], up: [0,−1].\n- Gradient g (size 32×2):\n  - Pair contributions: g_i += y_ij u_ij, g_j −= y_ij u_ij\n  - Boundary contributions: g_i += u_i,face v_face (where u_i,face is the selected face dual)\n- Curvature H (block-diagonal 2×2 per circle i):\n  - H_i = Σ_{j in N(i)∩A_pair} (y_ij / d_ij) (I − u_ij u_ij^T) + μ I, μ>0 (damping, initial μ=1e−3)\n  - Note (I − u u^T) penalizes motion orthogonal to the contact direction (stiffness), allowing tangential sliding.\n- Solve independently\
    \ for each i:\n  - H_i δc_i = g_i. If cond(H_i) large or det small, raise μ (e.g., ×1.5) locally. Cap ||δc_i|| ≤ δ_max (e.g., 0.05) before global trust-region scaling.\n\nOptional weak pair coupling (only if cheap): For the top 50 pairs, build 4×4 sub-blocks to couple (i,j). Start without coupling; add later if stable.\n\n3) Trust region, predicted gain, acceptance\n- Proposed step: δC = {δc_i}. Try α ∈ {1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2}.\n- Clip to box with ε_box=1e−6 margin: C' = clip(C + α δC, ε_box, 1−ε_box).\n- Predicted gain ĝ:\n  - ĝ = Σ_{(i,j)∈A_pair} y_ij ⟨u_ij, δc_i − δc_j⟩ + Σ_{i∈A_bound} u_i,face ⟨v_face, δc_i⟩\n- Evaluate exact LP at C' to get r', f' = Σr'.\n- Acceptance:\n  - If f' > f + ε (ε=1e−12), accept: C←C', r←r', f←f'.\n  - Agreement ratio ρ = (f'−f_old)/ĝ. If ĝ ≤ 0, treat ρ as 0 (conservative).\n  - Adapt:\n    - If ρ < 0.25: shrink trust (use smaller α next time) and increase μ (×1.5).\n    - If 0.25 ≤ ρ ≤ 0.75: keep α ladder and μ unchanged.\n    - If ρ > 0.75: allow larger\
    \ α next attempt (prepend 1.2× current top if safe), decrease μ (×0.8), optionally tighten τ_pair by ×1.1 to focus on strongest contacts.\n  - If no α succeeds, expand active set: lower τ_pair (×0.7), raise K_pairs (up to 300), then retry once; otherwise count as reject.\n\n4) Control flow and safeguards\n- ASN loop per seed:\n  - Build active set, assemble g/H, compute δC.\n  - Line-search over α; accept on first improvement; adapt μ/τ.\n  - If 3 consecutive rejects: call clearance relocation (1–2 passes) and/or per-circle line-search (20–30 trials), then rebuild active set and continue.\n  - Bound steps per seed: steps_asn ≤ 8–10 (time-boxed ~2–3 minutes total; each ASN step dominated by 1 LP).\n- Always finalize with exact LP + strict shrink + validation.\n- Persist only if improved vs stored best.\n\n5) Initial parameters and autotuning\n- Start:\n  - τ_pair=1e−3, τ_keep=6e−4, τ_drop=3e−4, K_pairs=240.\n  - τ_bound=1e−4; choose the max face per circle; keep if ≥ τ_bound/2.\n  - μ=1e−3;\
    \ α_list=[1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]; ε=1e−12; ε_box=1e−6.\n- Autotune:\n  - If |A_pair|<60 → lower τ_pair; if |A_pair|>K_pairs → raise τ_pair.\n  - If accepted steps are very small (ρ high but f'−f < 1e−6), consider increasing α upper bound to 1.25 while guarding feasibility.\n  - If many H_i ill-conditioned, raise μ floor (min μ=2e−3) and cap per-circle ||δc_i||.\n\n6) Pseudocode skeleton (drop-in)\n- asn_refine(C, r, f, y_pairs, u_bound, steps=8, params):\n  - state = {τ_pair, τ_keep, τ_drop, τ_bound, K_pairs, μ, α_list}\n  - for t in 1..steps:\n    1) A = build_active_set(y_pairs, u_bound, state, prev_A)\n    2) g, H = assemble_grad_hess(C, A, μ)\n    3) δC = solve_blocks(H, g, δ_max)\n    4) success = False\n       for α in α_list:\n         C_try = clip(C + α δC, ε_box)\n         r_try, f_try = exact_LP(C_try)\n         if f_try > f + ε:\n            ĝ = predicted_gain(δC, A)\n            ρ = clamp((f_try−f)/max(ĝ,1e−16), 0, 10)\n            C, r, f = C_try, r_try, f_try\n          \
    \  y_pairs, u_bound = duals_from_last_LP()  # if available\n            adapt(state, ρ, accepted=True)\n            success = True\n            break\n       if not success:\n         adapt(state, ρ=0.0, accepted=False)\n         if consecutive_rejects ≥ 3:\n            C, r, f = clearance_or_line_search_rescue(C, r, f)\n            y_pairs, u_bound = duals_from_last_LP()\n            reset consecutive_rejects\n         else:\n            consecutive_rejects += 1\n  - return C, r, f\n\n7) Runtime considerations\n- Each ASN step performs 1–4 LPs (line search), dominates cost; MM-LP and BN already do LPs, so budget ASN to ~8 steps per top seed.\n- Block solves are trivial (32 independent 2×2 systems), O(|A_pair|) assembly is modest (K≤300).\n- Maintain float64, pre-allocate arrays, and reuse workspaces to minimize overhead.\n\n8) Edge-case handling\n- Degenerate pairs: d_ij ← max(d_ij, ε_d), also cap y_ij by y_cap (e.g., 1e2) when assembling to avoid exploding stiffness.\n- Boundary conflicts:\
    \ acceptance gate via exact LP prevents harmful moves; boundary duals guide away from faces but can be overridden by pair forces.\n- Numeric stability: if δC nearly zero while g large, raise μ and rebuild A with tighter τ_pair to focus on strongest constraints.\n\nNext: I can draft the asn_refine() skeleton code (Python) and wire it into our best multi-start pipeline after MM-LP and before BN, following the above control logic and parameter defaults."
