tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "Thoughts (Tick 2/5): Making ASN practical, stable, and fast\n\nA) Dual extraction and robustness\n- HiGHS duals:\n  - Pairwise: res.ineqlin.marginals (length m = 496) in submission context; map index k → (i,j) via stored I,J arrays; clamp negatives to 0.\n  - Boundary: linprog exposes lower/upper marginals on variable bounds; we need per-face duals for r≤x, r≤1−x, r≤y, r≤1−y. Since those are modeled as constraints in our LP-only-for-r formulation, we don’t get face duals directly. Practical proxy:\n    - Use proximity to faces as a surrogate dual when face is nearly tight after placement:\n      u_i,left ≈ max(0, κ_b*(r_i − x_i)), u_i,right ≈ max(0, κ_b*(r_i − (1−x_i))), similarly for y, with κ_b a scaling (e.g., 1e3). Then select the single largest face per circle as boundary active.\n    - If we switch to a small SOCP for centers+r with explicit boundary constraints (only for dual extraction), we can read true boundary duals; but for ASN we can start with the proxy to avoid extra\
    \ solver dependency.\n  - Smoothing duals: duals can jump between steps. Apply EMA ỹ ← β ỹ + (1−β) y with β≈0.5 for stability; use ỹ for thresholds.\n\nB) Active set selection—adaptive thresholds\n- Absolute thresholds are fragile across instances. Hybrid approach:\n  - Compute ỹ_sorted; let τ_quant = quantile(ỹ, q), q≈0.65–0.8 depending on K_pairs target. Set τ_pair = max(τ_min, τ_quant), with τ_min=3e−4.\n  - Hysteresis: once active, keep if ỹ ≥ τ_keep = 0.6 τ_pair; drop if ỹ < τ_drop = 0.3 τ_pair.\n  - Cap to K_pairs in [200, 300]. If after hysteresis and τ_pair you have >K_pairs, keep top-K; if <60, relax τ_pair by ×0.7 until ≥60 or τ_pair=τ_min.\n- Boundary: for each i, compute four proxy face weights; if max ≥ τ_bound (start 1e−4), select that face; keep if ≥ τ_bound/2.\n\nC) Newton step details—stability improvements\n- Curvature along u_ij is zero for the true Hessian of ||·||; our block H_i becomes singular if a node has only a few parallel contacts. Two stabilizations:\n\
    \  - Add small parallel curvature: H_i += γ_i Σ_{(i,j)∈A_pair} (y_ij/d_ij) (u_ij u_ijᵀ) with γ_i≈0.05, ensuring full-rank and taming huge steps along u.\n  - Floor per-block spectrum: H_i ← H_i + μ I with μ start 1e−3; if cond(H_i)>1e6 or det<1e−12, multiply μ by 1.5 (only for that i).\n- Per-circle trust-cap before global α: ||δc_i|| ≤ δ_max (0.05). This keeps the box projection from collapsing the direction structure.\n\nD) Predicted gain and diagnostics\n- Use ĝ only for adaptation, not accept/reject. Clamp ĝ_low = max(ĝ, 1e−10) to avoid division blowups.\n- Track (f'−f)/#LP_calls to estimate marginal benefit; if marginal < 1e−6 over last 10 LPs, early-stop ASN for this seed.\n\nE) Trust-region and damping schedule\n- α ladder: start [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]. On successive accepts with ρ>0.8, prepend 1.2 (cap 1.3) once; otherwise stick to default ladder.\n- μ schedule: global μ_g used as minimum across blocks (local μ_i can be higher due to conditioning). If two rejects in a row, μ_g\
    \ ×= 1.5; on strong agreements (ρ>0.8), μ_g ×= 0.8 but not below 5e−4.\n\nF) Rescue moves and re-activation\n- After 3 rejects:\n  - Run one clearance relocation pass (grid_n=19, topk=10).\n  - Run short per-circle search (20 trials) to jiggle out of saddle.\n  - Rebuild active set with τ_pair relaxed (×0.8) for one iteration, then restore.\n\nG) Runtime budgeting\n- Rough per-LP cost in our environment is small, but line-search multiplies that; assume 3 LPs per ASN step. With 8 ASN steps, ~24 LPs per seed. For top-2 seeds, ~50 LPs → safe within total budget considering other stages.\n- Integrate ASN for top-2 seeds only (the best two after MM-LP), each with steps_asn=8. Skip ASN if the seed’s last improvement <1e−6 in MM-LP (indicates a flat basin), go straight to Block-Newton.\n\nH) Numeric and implementation notes\n- Use float64 and vectorized assembly:\n  - Precompute v_ij, d_ij, u_ij for active pairs at once; map to i and j indices via fancy indexing; use np.add.at to accumulate\
    \ g and H_i components.\n  - Maintain a compact list of active pairs (K≤300) to keep assembly O(K).\n- Bound projection: clip(C + α δC, ε_box, 1−ε_box) with ε_box=1e−6.\n- Dual capping: y_cap=1e2; set y_use=min(ỹ, y_cap) to avoid extreme stiffness from numerical artifacts.\n\nI) asn_refine() skeleton (concise)\n- Inputs: C, r, f, duals (y_pairs smoothed; boundary proxies), steps=8, params.\n- Loop t=1..steps:\n  1) A = build_active_set(ỹ, boundary_proxies, hysteresis, K, thresholds)\n  2) g,H = assemble(A, C, damp=μ_g, γ_parallel)\n  3) δC = solve_per_circle(H,g), cap per-circle norm\n  4) For α in ladder: C' = clip(C + α δC); r', f' = exact_LP(C'); if f'>f+ε accept; compute ĝ, ρ; adapt(μ_g, thresholds, α ladder); break\n  5) If no accept: rejects+=1; possibly rescue; adapt(μ_g up, τ_pair down modestly)\n  6) Early stop if marginal benefit low or time budget tick exceeded\n- Return best (C,r,f), exposing counters (accept rate, avg ρ, |A_pair|).\n\nJ) Integration plan (code wiring)\n\
    - After MM-LP in the best-performing multi-start script:\n  - Call ASN on top-2 seeds with time guard; propagate best to Block-Newton stage.\n  - Keep persistence discipline and loader “production” script unchanged.\n- Logging: track per-seed ASN stats for post-hoc analysis (|A_pair|, accepts, median ρ, LPs).\n\nK) Expected gains and risks\n- Gains: ASN should produce larger coherent moves than BN (which is diagonalized), especially when a small set of contacts dominates (clear “stress” direction). This targets exactly the regime where we likely need a 0.001–0.01 boost in Σr.\n- Risks: Over-activating can over-constrain steps (tiny δC). The acceptance gate plus hysteresis and threshold adaptation should mitigate; rescue moves provide escape from bad active sets.\n\nNext: implement build_active_set(), assemble_grad_hess(), and asn_refine() with the schedules above, then run on top-2 seeds."
