tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "Thoughts (Tick 3/5): ASN implementation specifics, pseudo-code, and runtime plan\n\n1) Dual sourcing and proxies (concrete)\n- Pairwise duals:\n  - We already compute I, J for all pairs and call LP for radii with HiGHS. When available, read res.ineqlin.marginals into y_raw (length m=496) and clamp negatives to 0. Store y_smooth as EMA: y_smooth ← β y_smooth + (1−β) y_raw (β≈0.5). On first call, y_smooth=y_raw.\n- Boundary “duals” proxy:\n  - From LP-for-radii, the boundary influence manifests when r_i equals the boundary margin b_i = min(x_i, 1−x_i, y_i, 1−y_i). Define per-face slack:\n    s_left = x_i − r_i, s_right = (1−x_i) − r_i, s_down = y_i − r_i, s_up = (1−y_i) − r_i.\n  - Map to proxy weights with a soft-relu near tightness:\n    w_face = max(0, κ_b (s_thresh − s_face)), with s_thresh ≈ 1e−3, κ_b ≈ 1e3 (scale to match typical y magnitudes).\n  - Choose at most one face per circle with largest w_face; keep hysteresis (keep if ≥ 0.5 τ_bound).\n  - Optional normalization: rescale\
    \ all selected boundary proxies by a factor so that median selected w_face ≈ median y_ij among active pairs (stability).\n\n2) Active-set builder (vectorized)\n- Inputs: y_smooth (m,), I, J, previous active pair mask A_prev (m,), thresholds τ_pair, τ_keep, τ_drop, cap K_pairs (200–300).\n- Build candidates:\n  - keep_mask = A_prev & (y_smooth ≥ τ_drop)\n  - add_mask = (~A_prev) & (y_smooth ≥ τ_pair)\n  - cand_mask = keep_mask | add_mask\n  - If sum(cand_mask) > K_pairs: pick top-K by y_smooth among cand_mask.\n  - If sum(cand_mask) < 60: lower τ_pair by ×0.7 iteratively (down to τ_min=3e−4) and rebuild; then cap again if needed.\n- Return active pairs (arrays I_act, J_act, y_act_idx) and per-circle boundary face selections (face_idx ∈ {−1,left,right,down,up}).\n\n3) Gradient/Hessian assembly (vectorized and stable)\n- For active pairs:\n  - V = C[I_act] − C[J_act] (K×2), d = sqrt(sum(V^2, axis=1)) clamped by ε_d=1e−9, U = V / d[:,None].\n  - y_use = clip(y_smooth[act_idx], 0, y_cap)\
    \ with y_cap≈1e2 (guard).\n- Gradient:\n  - g = zeros_like(C)\n  - np.add.at(g, I_act, y_use[:,None] * U)\n  - np.add.at(g, J_act, −y_use[:,None] * U)\n- Hessian (block diag per circle):\n  - H = zeros((n,2,2))\n  - M_orth = (I2 − U Uᵀ) for each pair: via uuT = U[:, :, None] * U[:, None, :]\n  - M_orth *= (y_use/d)[:,None, None]\n  - np.add.at(H, I_act, M_orth); np.add.at(H, J_act, M_orth)\n  - Add parallel curvature: M_par = γ (y_use/d)[:,None,None] * (U Uᵀ) with γ≈0.05; accumulate similarly.\n  - Damping: H[i] += μ_g I2. If det(H[i]) < 1e−12 or cond too big (estimate via 2×2 formula), increase μ_local until safe (max 10× μ_g).\n- Boundary contributions:\n  - For circle i with chosen face and proxy weight w_face: g[i] += w_face v_face, where v_face ∈ {[1,0], [−1,0], [0,1], [0,−1]}.\n  - (Optional) small diagonal stiffness for boundary: H[i] += η_b I2 with η_b≈1e−4 to prevent runaway when only boundary active.\n\n4) Step solve and trust caps\n- Solve per-circle: δc_i = H_i^{-1} g_i (2×2\
    \ solve); cap per-circle norm ||δc_i|| ≤ δ_max=0.05 before global α.\n- α ladder: [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2] initially; optionally expand with 1.2 if two strong accepts.\n\n5) Predicted gain and acceptance gate\n- Predicted gain ĝ:\n  - Pair term: sum_k y_use[k] * dot(U[k], δc_{i(k)} − δc_{j(k)})\n  - Boundary term: sum_i w_face[i] * dot(v_face[i], δc_i) for selected faces.\n  - ĝ_clamped = max(ĝ, 1e−10) for adaptation.\n- For each α in ladder:\n  - C_try = clip(C + α δC, ε_box=1e−6)\n  - (r_try, f_try, ok) = exact_LP(C_try)\n  - If ok and f_try > f + ε (ε≈1e−8 for numerical noise): accept; compute ρ=(f_try−f)/ĝ_clamped; adapt μ_g and α policy; refresh y_smooth (EMA) with new duals if available; break.\n  - If none accept: increase μ_g×=1.5; optionally relax τ_pair ×0.8 once; count reject.\n\n6) ASN control and rescue\n- Iterate steps_asn = 8 per seed (top-2 seeds only).\n- If 3 consecutive rejects:\n  - Run clearance relocation (grid_n=19, topk=10) OR per-circle line search (20 trials).\n\
    \  - Recompute LP duals; reset reject counter; continue.\n- Early stop ASN if marginal_f_gain_per_LP < 1e−6 over last 10 LP calls.\n\n7) Pseudo-code skeleton (Python-style)\n\ndef asn_refine(C, r, f, y_pairs, I, J, steps=8, params):\n    # params: τ_pair, τ_keep, τ_drop, τ_min, K_pairs, τ_bound, μ_g, α_list, ε, ε_box, γ, y_cap\n    y_smooth = ema_init(y_pairs)  # or reuse across calls\n    A_prev = np.zeros_like(y_pairs, dtype=bool)\n    rejects = 0\n    for t in range(steps):\n        I_act, J_act, act_idx, faces = build_active_set(y_smooth, A_prev, C, r, params)\n        g, H = assemble_grad_hess(C, I_act, J_act, act_idx, faces, y_smooth, params)\n        dC = solve_per_circle(H, g, params)  # per-circle 2x2 solves + per-circle cap\n        accepted = False\n        ĝ = predicted_gain(dC, I_act, J_act, act_idx, faces, y_smooth, params)\n        for α in params.α_list:\n            C_try = clip_box(C + α * dC, params.ε_box)\n            r_try, f_try, ok = exact_LP(C_try)\n         \
    \   if ok and f_try > f + params.ε:\n                ρ = (f_try - f) / max(ĝ, 1e-10)\n                C, r, f = C_try, r_try, f_try\n                y_new = read_pair_duals_last_LP()  # if available\n                if y_new is not None:\n                    y_smooth = β*y_smooth + (1-β)*np.clip(y_new, 0, None)\n                adapt_hyperparams(params, ρ, accepted=True)\n                accepted = True\n                break\n        if not accepted:\n            adapt_hyperparams(params, ρ=0.0, accepted=False)\n            rejects += 1\n            if rejects >= 3:\n                C, r, f = rescue_move(C, r, f)  # clearance or line-search\n                y_new = read_pair_duals_last_LP()\n                if y_new is not None:\n                    y_smooth = β*y_smooth + (1-β)*np.clip(y_new, 0, None)\n                rejects = 0\n        A_prev = np.zeros_like(y_pairs, dtype=bool); A_prev[act_idx] = True\n    return C, r, f\n\n8) Runtime and integration\n- Hook into our best multi-start\
    \ script:\n  - After MM-LP on each of the top-2 seeds, call ASN with steps=8 and params above; then proceed to Block-Newton.\n  - Maintain a per-run LP counter and time.time() budget; if ASN nears budget (e.g., 3–4 minutes of the total), truncate remaining steps.\n- Logging:\n  - Track per-step f, accepted flag, ρ, |A_pair|, μ_g, α used; dump minimal stats for analysis.\n\n9) Expected behavior and debugging checklist\n- If ASN steps produce negligible updates (|A_pair| small), lower τ_pair and allow more pairs (up to K_pairs); if still small, fallback to BN (often recovers micro-gains).\n- If ASN oscillates (accept/reject alternation), increase μ_g floor and reduce α ladder top to 0.8 for a few steps.\n- Verify no double-shrink: only strict shrink at final return or loader; do not shrink within ASN loop.\n\nNext tick: draft concrete function signatures and the minimal code skeleton (type-hinted), plus a list of integration points and metrics to print or store for quick inspection."
