tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "Thoughts (Tick 4/5): Concrete function signatures, code skeleton, and integration hooks\n\nA) Core types and params\n- ASNParams (dataclass-style)\n  - τ_pair: float = 1e−3\n  - τ_keep: float = 6e−4\n  - τ_drop: float = 3e−4\n  - τ_min: float = 3e−4\n  - τ_bound: float = 1e−4\n  - K_pairs: int = 240            # cap on active pairs\n  - K_min: int = 60               # minimum active pair count\n  - μ_g: float = 1e−3             # global damping floor\n  - γ_parallel: float = 0.05      # small parallel curvature fraction\n  - y_cap: float = 1e2            # cap dual magnitude\n  - α_list: list[float] = [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]\n  - ε_improve: float = 1e−8       # improvement threshold on sum(r)\n  - ε_box: float = 1e−6\n  - δ_max: float = 0.05           # per-circle step cap\n  - ema_beta: float = 0.5         # EMA smoothing for duals\n  - grid_n_worst: int = 19        # for rescue clearance\n  - topk_worst: int = 10\n  - max_rejects: int = 3\n  - steps_asn: int = 8\n  - time_budget_s:\
    \ float = 120.0  # per seed (2 min), tune up to 180 if needed\n\nB) External closures we reuse\n- exact_lp(C) -> (r, f, ok, y_pairs, (I_all, J_all))\n  - Existing function that computes radii via HiGHS LP and optionally returns pair duals and cached I,J.\n- rescue_clearance(C, r, obj) -> (C2, r2, o2)   # existing worst-circle relocation (1 pass)\n- rescue_line_search(C, trials=20) -> (C2, r2, o2)  # short per-circle line-search\n- Optional: get_boundary_proxies(C, r) -> (faces_idx, w_face_per_circle) using slack-based proxy\n\nC) Function signatures (with type hints)\n\ndef build_active_set(\n    y_smooth: np.ndarray,\n    I_all: np.ndarray, J_all: np.ndarray,\n    A_prev: np.ndarray,                  # bool mask over pairs\n    C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray,\n    params: ASNParams\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns:\n      I_act, J_act: active pair indices (K,)\n      idx_act: indices into [0..m) paralleling I_act/J_act\n\
    \      face_idx: (n,) ints in {-1,0,1,2,3} for {none,left,right,down,up}\n      w_face: (n,) boundary proxy weights (zeros where face_idx=-1)\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef assemble_grad_hess(\n    C: np.ndarray,\n    I_act: np.ndarray, J_act: np.ndarray, idx_act: np.ndarray,\n    y_smooth: np.ndarray,\n    face_idx: np.ndarray, w_face: np.ndarray,\n    params: ASNParams\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns:\n      g: (n,2) gradient\n      H: (n,2,2) block-diagonal curvature with damping and parallel curvature\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef solve_per_circle(\n    H: np.ndarray, g: np.ndarray, params: ASNParams\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns: dC (n,2) with per-circle norm capped at δ_max\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef predicted_gain(\n    dC: np.ndarray,\n    C: np.ndarray,\n    I_act: np.ndarray, J_act: np.ndarray, idx_act: np.ndarray,\n    y_smooth: np.ndarray,\n    face_idx: np.ndarray, w_face: np.ndarray\n) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    ĝ = sum_{pairs} y_ij <u_ij, dC_i - dC_j> + sum_{faces}\
    \ w_face <v_face, dC_i>\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef adapt_hyperparams(\n    params: ASNParams,\n    rho: float,\n    accepted: bool,\n    A_sizes: dict[str,int] | None = None\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Mutates params in-place: adjust μ_g, α_list top, thresholds (τ_pair) slightly if needed.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef asn_refine(\n    C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, f: float,\n    exact_lp,                      # closure\n    y_pairs: np.ndarray | None,    # initial duals; if None, will be set after first LP\n    I_all: np.ndarray, J_all: np.ndarray,\n    steps: int,\n    params: ASNParams,\n    time_budget_s: float,\n    rng: np.random.Generator | None = None\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, float, dict]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns improved (C*, r*, f*) and stats dict: {'lp_calls': int, 'accepts': int, 'avg_rho': float, 'avg_pairs': float}\n    \"\"\"\n\nD) Code skeleton (Python-like, concise)\n\ndef asn_refine(...):\n    t0 = time.time()\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    if y_pairs is None:\n        r, f, ok,\
    \ y_pairs, (I_all, J_all) = exact_lp(C)\n        if not ok: return C, r, f, {'lp_calls':1, 'accepts':0}\n    y_smooth = np.clip(y_pairs, 0.0, None).astype(float)\n    rejects = 0\n    stats = {'lp_calls': 0, 'accepts': 0, 'avg_rho': 0.0, 'avg_pairs': 0.0}\n    A_prev = np.zeros_like(y_smooth, dtype=bool)\n    for t in range(steps):\n        if time.time() - t0 > time_budget_s: break\n        # Build active set\n        I_act, J_act, idx_act, face_idx, w_face = build_active_set(y_smooth, I_all, J_all, A_prev, C, r, params)\n        stats['avg_pairs'] = (stats['avg_pairs']*t + len(idx_act)) / (t+1)\n        # Assemble and solve per-circle blocks\n        g, H = assemble_grad_hess(C, I_act, J_act, idx_act, y_smooth, face_idx, w_face, params)\n        dC = solve_per_circle(H, g, params)\n        # Predicted gain\n        ghat = predicted_gain(dC, C, I_act, J_act, idx_act, y_smooth, face_idx, w_face)\n        accepted = False\n        rho_used = 0.0\n        for α in params.α_list:\n    \
    \        C_try = np.clip(C + α*dC, params.ε_box, 1.0 - params.ε_box)\n            r_try, f_try, ok, y_new, _ = exact_lp(C_try)\n            stats['lp_calls'] += 1\n            if ok and (f_try > f + params.ε_improve):\n                # Succeed\n                C, r, f = C_try, r_try, f_try\n                accepted = True\n                rho = (f_try - (f - (f_try - f))) / max(ghat, 1e-10)  # careful: use saved f_old\n                rho_used = rho\n                stats['accepts'] += 1\n                if y_new is not None:\n                    y_smooth = params.ema_beta*y_smooth + (1-params.ema_beta)*np.clip(y_new, 0.0, None)\n                adapt_hyperparams(params, rho, accepted=True, A_sizes={'pairs': len(idx_act)})\n                break\n        if not accepted:\n            adapt_hyperparams(params, rho=0.0, accepted=False, A_sizes={'pairs': len(idx_act)})\n            rejects += 1\n            if rejects >= params.max_rejects:\n                # Rescue move: clearance or\
    \ line-search (short)\n                C, r, f = rescue_clearance(C, r, f)  # or rescue_line_search(C, trials=20)\n                # Refresh duals\n                _, _, _, y_new, _ = exact_lp(C)\n                stats['lp_calls'] += 1\n                if y_new is not None:\n                    y_smooth = params.ema_beta*y_smooth + (1-params.ema_beta)*np.clip(y_new, 0.0, None)\n                rejects = 0\n        A_prev = np.zeros_like(y_smooth, dtype=bool); A_prev[idx_act] = True\n        # Update avg rho\n        stats['avg_rho'] = (stats['avg_rho']*t + rho_used) / (t+1) if accepted else stats['avg_rho']\n    return C, r, f, stats\n\nNotes:\n- The rho computation needs the old f before evaluating α; in code, save f_old before the α-loop to compute rho = (f_try−f_old)/max(ĝ,1e−10).\n- adapt_hyperparams:\n  - If accepted and rho > 0.8: params.μ_g *= 0.8 (not less than 5e−4); optionally augment α_list = [min(1.2*α_list[0],1.3)] + α_list (dedup).\n  - If rejected: params.μ_g *= 1.5 (cap\
    \ at maybe 1e−1); params.τ_pair *= 0.9 (slightly looser) only once per two rejects; maintain hysteresis.\n\nE) Integration hooks (pipeline)\n- After MM-LP for the top-2 seeds:\n  - C_mm, R_mm, O_mm = mm_lp_optimize(C0, iters=?, delta0=?)\n  - C_asn, R_asn, O_asn, asn_stats = asn_refine(C_mm, R_mm, O_mm, exact_lp, y_pairs, I_all, J_all, steps=params.steps_asn, params=params, time_budget_s=params.time_budget_s)\n  - Proceed to Block-Newton polish on (C_asn, R_asn).\n- Ensure the persistence discipline and loader remain unchanged.\n\nF) Metrics to log (minimal)\n- Per seed: {'seed_id': k, 'f_in': f0, 'f_asn': f1, 'accepts': A, 'avg_pairs': P, 'avg_rho': R, 'lp_calls': L, 'μ_end': μ_g}\n- Emit only when ASN returns or on early stop.\n\nG) Edge-case checklist\n- If |A_pair|=0 (all y≈0): skip ASN and go straight to BN.\n- If H_i produces NaN/Inf solve: increase μ_g and rebuild once; otherwise mark reject.\n- If predicted gain ĝ≤0 repeatedly: treat as reject and force rescue.\n\nH) Runtime\
    \ target and sanity tests\n- Target < 2–3 minutes per top seed; monitor LP calls (aim < ~25/seed for ASN).\n- Sanity test on a known configuration:\n  - Perturb C slightly; ASN should recover or modestly improve f in a few steps; predicted ρ within [0,2] typical.\n  - Ablation: turn off boundary proxies; ensure it still progresses (pairs dominate).\n\nNext (Tick 5): outline minimal unit-test stubs (pseudo) and precise first-implementation parameter values, plus a concrete step to wire ASN into our current best-performing script with a guarded flag to quickly toggle ASN on/off for comparisons."
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on design tasks**


  I need to focus on the reflective design for ASN since the user has multi-tick reflection. I should outline elements like function signatures, code skeleton, and implementation plans. Metrics and risk mitigation are important, along with test plans and runtime complexity. I’m considering edge cases and how to handle them, as well as storage and parallelization aspects. Since this is reflective, I’ll provide structured, pseudo-code and avoid YAML formatting. Let''s keep it clear and organized for the user!**Outlining ASN parameters and functions**


  I’m preparing to present the parameter dataclass ASNParams and several key functions such as build_active_set, assemble_grad_hess, and solve_per_circle. Each function serves its purpose in our plan, like predicted_gain and adapt_hyperparams. I’ll also mention how exact_lp computes radii and pairs, and highlight the performance metrics—around 240 Kpairs and minimal memory use for operations. Integration steps into existing pipelines will be outlined as well to ensure coherence. Let''s keep this organized and clear for the user!**Providing plug-in details for MM-LP**


  I need to explain how to plug in after the MM-LP function call, focusing on passing the closure for LP.


  Metrics to log include step index, previous and new function values, delta, alpha, rho, and more. I should have unit tests for synthetic rings and ensure gradient sanity. For a fail-safe, if solve_per_circle returns NaN, I''ll increase μ, and if predicted gain is less than or equal to zero, I''ll treat that as a rejection. I’ll provide a sample pseudo code block in Python with type hints and outline initial values and heuristics. Let''s keep this structured!'
