tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "Thoughts (Tick 5/5): Final ASN blueprint, concrete defaults, quick tests, and wiring plan\n\nA) Final parameter defaults (first implementation)\n- Pair selection\n  - τ_pair = 1.0e−3\n  - τ_keep = 0.6 × τ_pair = 6.0e−4\n  - τ_drop = 0.3 × τ_pair = 3.0e−4\n  - τ_min = 3.0e−4 (don’t go lower)\n  - K_pairs = 240 (cap); K_min = 60 (ensure a minimum)\n  - y_cap = 1.0e2 (cap dual magnitude)\n  - ema_beta = 0.5 (dual smoothing)\n- Boundary proxy\n  - τ_bound = 1.0e−4; keep if ≥ 0.5 τ_bound\n  - s_thresh = 1.0e−3; κ_b = 1.0e3 to build proxy w_face = max(0, κ_b (s_thresh − slack))\n- Newton/Trust-region\n  - μ_g start = 1.0e−3 (min 5.0e−4, max 1.0e−1), per-block raise locally if ill-conditioned\n  - γ_parallel = 0.05 (add small curvature along u_ij u_ij^T)\n  - α_list = [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]; on two strong accepts allow prepending 1.2 once (cap 1.3)\n  - δ_max = 0.05 (per-circle step cap)\n  - ε_improve = 1.0e−8; ε_box = 1.0e−6\n- Loop control\n  - steps_asn = 8 (per seed)\n  - max_rejects\
    \ = 3 → trigger rescue (clearance pass or 20-trial per-circle search)\n  - time_budget_s ≈ 120 per seed (top-2 seeds only)\n\nB) Minimal unit-test stubs (pseudo)\n1) Active set sizing and hysteresis\n- Setup: random y_smooth with a few large entries; A_prev marks a subset active.\n- Expect: build_active_set caps at K_pairs, retains A_prev entries above τ_drop, and enforces ≥K_min by relaxing τ_pair but not below τ_min.\n\n2) Grad/Hess assembly sanity\n- Construct a simple configuration with two strong contacts and one boundary face proxy; call assemble_grad_hess.\n- Expect: H[i] symmetric 2×2, det(H[i]) > 0 (with damping); ||g|| > 0; no NaN/Inf.\n\n3) Predicted gain monotonicity (micro check)\n- Single active pair (i,j) with unit u_ij; set dC_i = +u_ij, dC_j = −u_ij (others zero).\n- Expected ĝ ≈ 2 y_ij > 0 (up to small tolerances).\n\n4) Acceptance gate behavior\n- Craft C, then propose C_try = C + ε_nudge; run exact LP both sides.\n- Expect: accept only when f_try > f + ε_improve;\
    \ otherwise reject and μ_g increases.\n\n5) Rescue move hook\n- Force repeated rejects by zeroing dC; ensure rescue is called on the 3rd reject; verify it returns a new C with LP succeeding (ok=True).\n\nC) Adaptation logic (precise)\n- On accept:\n  - ρ = (f’ − f_old) / max(ĝ, 1.0e−10)\n  - If ρ > 0.8: μ_g ← 0.8 μ_g (floor 5e−4); if α_list[0] < 1.3 and not recently expanded, set α_list = [min(1.2α_0, 1.3)] + α_list.\n  - If 0.25 ≤ ρ ≤ 0.8: keep μ_g, α_list.\n  - If ρ < 0.25: μ_g ← 1.2 μ_g; consider shrinking α_list top to 0.8 for the next step (temporary).\n- On reject:\n  - μ_g ← 1.5 μ_g (cap 1e−1).\n  - Optionally relax τ_pair × 0.9 once per two rejects; rebuild active set next iteration.\n\nD) Edge-case safeguards (strict)\n- Degenerate pairs: d_ij ← max(d_ij, 1e−9), y_use ← min(y_smooth, y_cap).\n- If |A_pair|=0: skip ASN → BN.\n- If per-circle solve yields ||δc_i|| < 1e−9 for all i while ||g|| > 1e−6: raise μ_g, rebuild A with larger K_pairs (to 300) and lower τ_pair slightly (×0.9)\
    \ once.\n- If predicted ĝ ≤ 0 repeatedly: treat as reject, trigger rescue earlier.\n\nE) Integration checklist\n- Place asn_refine after mm_lp_optimize for the top-2 seeds by MM-LP objective; call with steps_asn=8, time_budget_s=120.\n- Use exact_lp from our current code: returns r, f, ok, y_pairs, (I_all, J_all). If duals not exposed, rebuild y_smooth from slack heuristic ỹ = 1 / (ε + slack).\n- After ASN, pass (C_asn, R_asn, O_asn) to block_newton_polish. Keep optional SOCP polish as a final “accept-if-improves” step.\n- Persistence discipline unchanged; loader stays as production default.\n\nF) Logging (low volume, useful)\n- Per seed after ASN: {'f_in': f0, 'f_out': f1, 'accepts': A, 'avg_pairs': P, 'avg_rho': R, 'lp_calls': L, 'mu_end': μ_g}\n- Only print when running ASN; skip in loader/production submissions.\n\nG) Runtime budgeting\n- Expect ~3 LPs per ASN step (line-search attempts). At 8 steps, ~24 LPs/seed; for 2 seeds, ~48 LPs.\n- Combined with MM-LP and BN LP usage, stays\
    \ within the 20-minute limit given our past runs. Time-box to 120–150s for ASN per seed; early-stop if marginal Δf over last 10 LPs < 1e−6.\n\nH) Expected gains target and stop criteria\n- Target ΔΣr ≈ 2–5e−3 beyond current 2.9292366 (aspirational); immediate success is any consistent improvement ≥ 5e−4 after ASN+BN.\n- Stop early if:\n  - ASN marginal gain < 1e−6 over last 10 LPs,\n  - Two seeds processed and global best unchanged,\n  - Time budget near 3–4 minutes used on ASN total.\n\nI) Implementation roadmap next turn\n- Add ASNParams and implement:\n  - get_boundary_proxies(C, r)\n  - build_active_set(y_smooth, I_all, J_all, A_prev, C, r, params)\n  - assemble_grad_hess(C, I_act, J_act, idx_act, y_smooth, face_idx, w_face, params)\n  - solve_per_circle(H, g, params)\n  - predicted_gain(...)\n  - adapt_hyperparams(params, rho, accepted, A_sizes)\n  - asn_refine(...)\n- Wire asn_refine into the best multi-start submission (toggle via flag USE_ASN=True).\n- Guard: if exact_lp doesn’t\
    \ return duals, create y_smooth from 1/(ε + slack) with exponent p≈1 and normalize to match scale of typical duals for thresholds to behave.\n\nJ) Validation plan (quick smoke tests)\n- Run ASN on a persisted-best C with steps_asn=3 (quick mode) and check f increases or stays neutral; confirm strict feasibility after final shrink and no double-shrink.\n- Run full pipeline on the top-2 seeds with ASN enabled and log stats; if no improvement over baseline, adjust τ_pair ladder or μ_g schedule and retry short runs.\n\nWith this, we can implement the ASN module next, integrate cleanly, and probe for the remaining headroom beyond 2.9292366 while staying robust and within budget."
