parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 57\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol (Verity I)\n- Goal: push Circle Packing sum(r) > 2.9292366 with strict validity and reproducibility.\n- Always: exact LP finalize (HiGHS), strict safety-shrink, validate, persist only on strict improvement.\n- Time: keep submission < 20 min; target < 3–5 min.\n- Seeds: persisted-best, rotated-hex, farthest-point. Deterministic RNG.\n- Search: pseudo-dual “stress” equilibration + backtracked Newton-like step; rescue move = worst-circle clearance relocation; accept only if LP-improves.\n- Token mgmt: prune when usage > 75%; maintain concise, complete summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 52,164 / 270,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 57 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message\
    \ 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 124**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Laplacian Newton steps from slack-weighted stresses + worst-circle clearance; exact LP finalize\n**ID:** 124\n**Tags:** circle packing, linear programming, laplacian newton, clearance, local search\n**Abstract:** Starting from persisted-best and structured seeds, we compute slack-weighted pairwise stresses and solve Laplacian linear systems to obtain Newton-like center displacements. Backtracked steps are accepted only if the exact LP (HiGHS) improves ∑r. A rescue relocation of the worst circle via a clearance map is used when stalled. Final strict feasibility with safety-shrink; persist if improved.\n**Score:** 1.5999999999999999\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 1.600000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport time, os\nfrom math import sqrt\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n\
    \    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\nN = 32\n\n# ---------- Geometry and LP ----------\ndef _pairwise_distances(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n    np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n    d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n    return d\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _solve_lp_for_radii(C: np.ndarray):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        r = 0.75 * np.minimum(b, np.median(b))\n        r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n        return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    rows, rhs = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n            row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n            rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows)\
    \ if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rows else None\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)  # maximize sum r -> minimize -sum r\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    if C.shape != (N, 2) or r.shape != (N,): return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0): return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1): return False\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    if np.any(D < Rsum - 1e-12): return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    rr = np.array(r, dtype=float) *\
    \ 0.999\n    rr = np.maximum(rr, 1e-12)\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, rr): break\n        rr *= 0.96\n    return rr\n\ndef _clip_to_box(C: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-4) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n# ---------- Seeds ----------\ndef _load_persisted_best():\n    try:\n        data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n        C = data['centers']; r = data['radii']\n        if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape == (N,):\n            r2 = _safety_shrink(C, r)\n            if _validate(C, r2):\n                return C.copy()\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return None\n\ndef _rotated_hex_seed(n: int, angle_deg: float = 13.5, spacing: float = 0.17, margin: float = 0.02) -> np.ndarray:\n    theta = np.deg2rad(angle_deg)\n    R = np.array([[np.cos(theta), -np.sin(theta)],\n                  [np.sin(theta),  np.cos(theta)]], dtype=float)\n    xs = np.arange(-6, 7) * spacing\n    ys = np.arange(-6, 7) * (spacing * sqrt(3)/2.0)\n\
    \    pts = []\n    for j, y in enumerate(ys):\n        xoff = (0.5 * spacing) if (j % 2) else 0.0\n        for x in xs:\n            p = (R @ np.array([x + xoff, y])) + np.array([0.5, 0.5])\n            if margin <= p[0] <= 1.0 - margin and margin <= p[1] <= 1.0 - margin:\n                pts.append(p)\n    pts = np.array(pts, dtype=float)\n    # Greedy farthest selection\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(123)\n    chosen = [pts[rng.integers(0, len(pts))]]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        diff = pts[:, None, :] - np.array(chosen)[None, :, :]\n        d = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n        idx = int(np.argmax(np.min(d, axis=1)))\n        chosen.append(pts[idx])\n    return np.array(chosen, dtype=float)\n\ndef _farthest_point_sampling(n: int, rng, margin=0.02, candidates=350) -> np.ndarray:\n    pts = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        cand = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(candidates, 2))\n        exist = np.array(pts)\n     \
    \   d = np.sqrt(np.sum((cand[:, None, :] - exist[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n        min_to_pts = np.min(d, axis=1)\n        b = np.minimum(np.minimum(cand[:, 0], 1.0 - cand[:, 0]),\n                       np.minimum(cand[:, 1], 1.0 - cand[:, 1]))\n        score = np.minimum(min_to_pts, 2.0 * b)\n        pts.append(cand[int(np.argmax(score))])\n    return np.array(pts, dtype=float)\n\n# ---------- Laplacian Newton step ----------\ndef _build_weights(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-4):\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    S = D - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])  # pairwise slack\n    W = 1.0 / (eps + np.maximum(S, 0.0))\n    np.fill_diagonal(W, 0.0)\n    return W, D, S\n\ndef _grad_and_laplacian(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, W: np.ndarray, D: np.ndarray, boundary_scale=0.5, lam=1e-3):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    g = np.zeros_like(C)\n    # Pair contributions\n    with np.errstate(invalid='ignore', divide='ignore'):\n        U = (C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]) / (D[:, :, None] + 1e-12)\n\
    \    U[np.isnan(U)] = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # g_i += sum_j w_ij * u_ij  - sum_j w_ji * u_ji (W symmetric -> simplifies)\n        g[i] += np.sum(W[i, :, None] * U[i], axis=0)\n        g[i] -= np.sum(W[:, i, None] * U[:, i], axis=0)\n\n    # Boundary contributions (push away from near-active faces)\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    sl = x - r; sr = (1.0 - x) - r; sd = y - r; su = (1.0 - y) - r\n    wl = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(sl, 0.0))\n    wr = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(sr, 0.0))\n    wd = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(sd, 0.0))\n    wu = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(su, 0.0))\n    g[:, 0] += boundary_scale * (wl - wr)\n    g[:, 1] += boundary_scale * (wd - wu)\n\n    # Laplacians for x and y\n    deg = np.sum(W, axis=1)\n    L = np.diag(deg) - W\n    Lx = L.copy(); Ly = L.copy()\n    # Add boundary diagonal weights\n    Lx += np.diag(boundary_scale * (wl + wr))\n    Ly += np.diag(boundary_scale * (wd + wu))\n    # Damping\n    Lx += lam * np.eye(n); Ly += lam * np.eye(n)\n\n\
    \    return g, Lx, Ly\n\ndef _laplacian_newton_step(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, alpha: float, lam=1e-3, boundary_scale=0.5):\n    W, D, S = _build_weights(C, r)\n    g, Lx, Ly = _grad_and_laplacian(C, r, W, D, boundary_scale=boundary_scale, lam=lam)\n    try:\n        dx = np.linalg.solve(Lx, g[:, 0])\n        dy = np.linalg.solve(Ly, g[:, 1])\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        # Robust fallback\n        dx = np.linalg.lstsq(Lx, g[:, 0], rcond=None)[0]\n        dy = np.linalg.lstsq(Ly, g[:, 1], rcond=None)[0]\n    step = np.stack([dx, dy], axis=1)\n    Ctr = _clip_to_box(C + alpha * step, margin=1e-4)\n    return Ctr\n\n# ---------- Rescue move ----------\ndef _clearance_at_point(p: np.ndarray, C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    bx = min(p[0], 1.0 - p[0]); by = min(p[1], 1.0 - p[1])\n    cb = min(bx, by)\n    if C.size == 0:\n        return cb\n    d = np.sqrt(np.sum((C - p[None, :])**2, axis=1))\n    return float(min(cb, np.min(d - r)))\n\ndef _worst_circle_relocation(C:\
    \ np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, rng, samples=250, margin=0.01):\n    i = int(np.argmin(r))\n    cand = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(samples, 2))\n    others = np.delete(C, i, axis=0)\n    r_oth = np.delete(r, i, axis=0)\n    scores = np.array([_clearance_at_point(p, others, r_oth) for p in cand])\n    p_best = cand[int(np.argmax(scores))]\n    Ct = C.copy(); Ct[i] = p_best\n    return Ct\n\n# ---------- Main ----------\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    np.random.seed(11)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(11)\n    time_budget = 15.0\n    t0 = time.time()\n\n    seeds = []\n    C0 = _load_persisted_best()\n    if C0 is not None:\n        seeds.append(C0)\n    seeds.append(_rotated_hex_seed(N, angle_deg=13.5, spacing=0.17, margin=0.02))\n    seeds.append(_farthest_point_sampling(N, rng, margin=0.02, candidates=350))\n\n    bestC = None; bestR = None; bestObj = -1.0\n\n    for seed in seeds:\n        if time.time() - t0 > time_budget * 0.9: break\n        C = _clip_to_box(np.array(seed,\
    \ dtype=float), margin=1e-4)\n        r, obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(C)\n        if not ok: continue\n        if obj > bestObj + 1e-12:\n            bestC, bestR, bestObj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n\n        no_improve = 0\n        for it in range(100):\n            if time.time() - t0 > time_budget: break\n            improved = False\n            for alpha in (0.25, 0.16, 0.10, 0.06, 0.04, 0.025, 0.015, 0.01):\n                Ct = _laplacian_newton_step(C, r, alpha=alpha, lam=1e-3, boundary_scale=0.6)\n                rt, objt, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(Ct)\n                if ok and objt > obj + 1e-10:\n                    C, r, obj = Ct, rt, objt\n                    improved = True\n                    break\n            if improved:\n                no_improve = 0\n                if obj > bestObj + 1e-12:\n                    bestC, bestR, bestObj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n            else:\n                no_improve += 1\n                if no_improve >= 6:\n            \
    \        Ct = _worst_circle_relocation(C, r, rng, samples=200, margin=0.01)\n                    Ct = _clip_to_box(Ct, 1e-4)\n                    rt, objt, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(Ct)\n                    if ok and objt > obj + 1e-10:\n                        C, r, obj = Ct, rt, objt\n                        no_improve = 0\n                        if obj > bestObj + 1e-12:\n                            bestC, bestR, bestObj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n                    else:\n                        j = rng.integers(0, N)\n                        C[j] = _clip_to_box(C[j] + rng.normal(0.0, 0.01, size=2), 1e-4)\n\n    if bestC is None:\n        # Conservative fallback grid\n        xs = np.linspace(1.0/(8+1), 1.0-1.0/(8+1), 8)\n        ys = np.linspace(1.0/(4+1), 1.0-1.0/(4+1), 4)\n        G = np.array([(x, y) for y in ys for x in xs], dtype=float)[:N]\n        b = _boundary_margins(G)\n        rr = np.minimum(b, 0.45 * min((xs[1]-xs[0]), (ys[1]-ys[0])) * np.ones(N))\n        return G,\
    \ rr\n\n    final_r = _safety_shrink(bestC, bestR)\n    if not _validate(bestC, final_r):\n        xs = np.linspace(1.0/(8+1), 1.0-1.0/(8+1), 8)\n        ys = np.linspace(1.0/(4+1), 1.0-1.0/(4+1), 4)\n        G = np.array([(x, y) for y in ys for x in xs], dtype=float)[:N]\n        b = _boundary_margins(G)\n        rr = np.minimum(b, 0.45 * min((xs[1]-xs[0]), (ys[1]-ys[0])) * np.ones(N))\n        return G, rr\n\n    try:\n        os.makedirs('storage/verity', exist_ok=True)\n        np.savez('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz', centers=bestC, radii=final_r, obj=np.sum(final_r))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return bestC, final_r\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Safe loader v2: return\
    \ persisted best as-is; robust 6×6-minus-corners fallback (r=1/12)' (ID: 128) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6639999999999997\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.664000\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 124` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 124 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Safe loader v2: return persisted best as-is; robust 6×6-minus-corners fallback (r=1/12)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 128.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle\
    \ Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 93 | 1 | Diverse multi-start MM-LP + block-Newton (rows + rotated-hex + farthest) with persistence | Verity I | 35 | 2.9292366 |\n| 97 | 1 | Basin-hopping MM-LP with clearance relocations, per-circle line search, and block-Newton polish (... | Verity I | 36 | 2.9292366 |\n| 99 | 1 | Aggressive diverse multi-start: MM-LP + two-worst clearance relocation + per-circle line-search +... | Verity I | 37 | 2.9292366 |\n| 102 | 1 | SOCP-refined aggressive multi-start: MM-LP + relocations + line-search + block-Newton, then cvxpy... | Verity I | 38 | 2.9292366 |\n| 109 | 1 | Persisted-best exact return (no double-shrink); rebuild radii via exact LP if needed; robust fall... | Verity I | 40 | 2.9292366 |\n| 118 | 1 |\
    \ Active-Set Newton (ASN) refinement + exact LP finalize (strict feasibility, persist-if-improved) | Verity I | 46 | 2.9292366 |\n| 105 | 1 | Fast loader: return persisted best packing with strict feasibility guard (fallback to quick grid) | Verity I | 39 | 2.9263074 |\n| 50 | 1 | SLSQP with New Perturbation Seed | Praxis I | 20 | 2.9155878 |\n| 66 | 1 | Pure SLSQP with Increased Iterations (maxiter=1000) | Praxis I | 25 | 2.9155878 |\n| 88 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Ensemble (Corrected) | Praxis I | 33 | 2.9155878 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
    \ room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
