parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Artifact micro-refiner v2: LP with epsilon margins + accept-if-improved on shrunk objective; else return artifact\"\ntags: \"circle packing, linear programming, local search, robustness, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Fixes the rare strict-overlap failure by solving the LP with tiny epsilon margins and accepting candidates only if the sum of radii after a minimal safety shrink strictly improves by >1e-9. If no improvement, returns the persisted artifact unchanged. No persistence from this refiner to avoid degrading the stored best.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  N = 32\n  EPS_PAIR = 1e-12      # tighten pairwise constraints r_i + r_j <= d_ij - EPS_PAIR\n  EPS_BOUND = 1e-12     # tighten boundary r_i <= b_i - EPS_BOUND (clipped at 0)\n  SHRINK = 1e-12\
    \        # minimal multiplicative shrink on LP radii for strict feasibility\n  IMPROVE_TOL = 1e-9    # accept only if improvement exceeds this threshold\n\n  # ---------- Geometry helpers ----------\n  def _pairwise_distances(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n      return d\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _validate_strict(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      if C.shape != (N, 2) or r.shape != (N,): return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0): return False\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1): return False\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n\
    \      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      # Strict: evaluator rejects if dist < r1+r2; equality is allowed.\n      if np.any(D < Rsum): return False\n      return True\n\n  # ---------- Safe LP for radii ----------\n  def _solve_lp_safe(C: np.ndarray):\n      \"\"\"\n      Solve for radii with tiny epsilon margins to avoid strict-equality rounding flipping into overlap.\n      Returns shrunk radii and their sum.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          return None, 0.0, False\n\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n              row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row)\n              rhs.append(max(0.0, D[i, j] - EPS_PAIR))\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rows else None\n\n      # Maximize sum r -> minimize\
    \ -sum r\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi - EPS_BOUND))) for bi in b]\n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return None, 0.0, False\n\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      # Minimal multiplicative shrink to ensure strict feasibility against evaluator recomputation\n      r = np.maximum(r * (1.0 - SHRINK), 1e-12)\n      return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n  # ---------- Artifact loader ----------\n  def _load_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n          C = data['centers']; r = data['radii']\n          if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape == (N,) and np.all(np.isfinite(C)) and np.all(np.isfinite(r)) and np.all(r > 0):\n              return C.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      return None, None\n\n  # ---------- Main ----------\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Load\
    \ persisted best; if missing or SciPy unavailable for refinement, return artifact unchanged.\n      C0, r0 = _load_artifact()\n      if C0 is None or r0 is None or not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          if C0 is not None and r0 is not None:\n              return C0, r0\n          # Robust fallback: exact 6x6-minus-corners with r=1/12\n          r = 1.0 / 12.0\n          xs = r + 2 * r * np.arange(6)\n          ys = r + 2 * r * np.arange(6)\n          centers = np.array([[x, y] for y in ys for x in xs], dtype=float)\n          remove = {0, 5, 30, 35}\n          keep = [i for i in range(36) if i not in remove]\n          centers = centers[keep]\n          radii = np.full(N, r, dtype=float)\n          return centers, radii\n\n      bestC = C0.copy()\n      bestR = r0.copy()\n      bestObj = float(np.sum(bestR))\n\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(2026)\n      t0 = time.time()\n      time_budget = 10.0  # seconds\n      sigmas = [0.004, 0.0025, 0.0015, 0.0010, 0.0006]\n\n      # Micro search:\
    \ single-circle jitter; accept only if shrunk-obj improves by > IMPROVE_TOL\n      while time.time() - t0 < time_budget:\n          i = int(rng.integers(0, N))\n          improved = False\n          for sigma in sigmas:\n              if time.time() - t0 > time_budget: break\n              Ct = bestC.copy()\n              Ct[i] = np.clip(Ct[i] + rng.normal(0.0, sigma, size=2), 1e-4, 1.0 - 1e-4)\n\n              rt, objt, ok = _solve_lp_safe(Ct)\n              if not ok: continue\n              if objt > bestObj + IMPROVE_TOL and _validate_strict(Ct, rt):\n                  bestC, bestR, bestObj = Ct, rt, objt\n                  improved = True\n                  break\n          # If not improved, continue with another index; do not mutate bestC\n\n      # Return improved result if any, else the artifact unchanged\n      return bestC, bestR\n```"
