    \ bounded runtime (< 5–10 min typical).\n- Token mgmt: prune when usage > 75%; keep concise, complete summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,965 / 270,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #1: LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs**\nAuthor: Verity I, Created at Tick: 53\nAbstract: We report a reproducible 32-circle packing achieving sum of radii 2.9292366. Centers are optimized via MM-LP trust-region steps, LP-dual–informed active-set refinements, and targeted relocations; radii are always finalized exactly via LP (HiGHS). This paper lists all key experiments with Evaluation IDs and scores to satisfy verifiability.\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #2: A Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem**\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 59\nAbstract: This paper presents a multi-start constrained optimization method\
    \ for the 32-circle packing problem. The algorithm utilizes `scipy.optimize.SLSQP` seeded with randomly perturbed grid initializations. The method is shown to be effective and robust, achieving a score of 2.9155. This paper provides a detailed description of the algorithm and presents the results of five verifiable experiments, including baseline comparisons and ablation studies, to support its efficacy.\n\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #3: Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing**\nAuthor: Cognito I, Created at Tick: 69\nAbstract: This paper provides a rigorous, evidence-based characterization of a highly stable local optimum in the 32-circle packing problem, yielding a score of 2.8658500. We demonstrate that a specific methodology—combining a 4x8 grid initialization with the Adam optimizer in a JAX framework (Evaluation ID 43)—robustly converges to this point. We present verifiable evidence showing that numerous sophisticated initializers,\
    \ including global search heuristics, converge to this same optimum. Furthermore, we demonstrate that substituting the Adam optimizer with SGD results in complete failure, proving the entire methodological pipeline is critical. This work establishes a well-defined, reproducible benchmark and offers a detailed portrait of a significant attractor basin that traps general-purpose optimizers.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `preview all` (in Archive Room);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Archive Room);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Preview command processed for all capsules. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 609 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | A Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 59 | 744 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 1319 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #3 ('Handoff notes: SOTA 2.9292366, safe loader policy, and next research directions'). Full ID: Verity_private_3\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Handoff notes: SOTA 2.9292366, safe loader policy, and next research directions | Verity I | Tick 72 | 326 | 1 |\
    \ (All Read) |\n| 2 | Circle Packing status @tick 42: 2.9292366 best, method recap, and next steps | Verity I | Tick 42 | 499 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Progress to 2.87826 and next steps: exact convex solve (SOCP/NLP) and robustness plan | Verity I | Tick 29 | 376 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
