role: model
parts:
- text: "Thoughts (Tick 2): concrete offline plan, success criteria, and risk controls\n\nA) Minimal, high-yield offline experiment\n- Seed set:\n  - S0: current artifact centers (no change to radii during search; radii only from LP).\n  - S1: rotated-hex crop/prune (one angle/spacing already used).\n  - S2: boundary-aware farthest-point sampler.\n- Budget:\n  - ≤ 2 runs total, ≤ 5 minutes each, deterministic RNG.\n  - Early-stop after 3 consecutive non-accepts.\n\nB) Contact-graph Active-Set Newton (ASN-lite) design\n- Working set (WS):\n  - Pairs with slack ≤ τ_pair; start τ_pair = 2e-4; adapt in [1e-4, 5e-4] by model agreement.\n  - Boundary faces with slack ≤ τ_b; same range; include per-circle nearest face only.\n  - Hysteresis: once active, keep until slack > 2τ for 2 consecutive iterations.\n- Model:\n  - Gradient g aggregates pushes along unit pair directions and boundary normals, weighted by inverse slack (cap weight at 1/τ_pair to avoid blow-ups).\n  - Curvature H: Laplacian-style\
    \ 2×2 block assembly from WS; add boundary diagonal weights; damping λI with λ ∈ [1e-4, 1e-1], adapted.\n- Globalization:\n  - Trial steps with α in {0.2, 0.12, 0.08, 0.05, 0.03, 0.02}.\n  - Accept iff exact LP on trial centers increases ∑r by > 1e-10 and min-slack ≥ 0 (LP ensures ≥0 up to FP noise).\n  - Model agreement ρ = (actual gain)/(predicted gain+ε); if ρ < 0.25, increase λ and/or reduce τ_pair and α; if ρ > 0.9, consider decreasing λ slightly.\n- Unlock move (only if stuck):\n  - After 2–3 failed accepts, drop the single highest-stress pair (smallest slack or largest weight) from WS, take one trial step, then re-evaluate WS. Revert if no LP gain.\n\nC) Diagnostics and persistence\n- Log per iteration:\n  - sum(r), min pair slack, min boundary slack, |WS_pairs|, |WS_boundary|, λ, α, ρ.\n- At run end:\n  - Persist only if Δ∑r ≥ 1e-8 AND min slack ≥ 1e-10 (recomputed with independent geometry).\n  - Store diagnostics: slack_stats.json, contact_graph.json (edges with slacks), and\
    \ append results.tsv.\n  - Do not modify loader; returned evaluation path remains loader v4.\n\nD) Success/fail gates\n- Success:\n  - Any seed yields safe improvement meeting thresholds above; artifact replaced; re-run loader v4 to confirm ≥ 2.9294423 (should match or slightly exceed if artifact truly improved).\n- Fail (acceptable outcome):\n  - No seed improves by ≥ 1e-8 within budget; freeze artifact and close search loop.\n\nE) Why this is best value now\n- Directly addresses the locked contact graph with coordinated moves.\n- Reuses proven LP-finalize acceptance, avoiding surrogate drift.\n- Keeps solves small (64×64 dense or sparse) and time-bounded, limiting token and runtime costs.\n\nF) What not to do\n- Tolerance/precision sweeps to “manufacture” gains: fragile and non-generalizable; risk of evaluator flips.\n- In-path micro-refiners beyond the fixed micro-shrink: can cause regressions; loader stays immutable.\n\nG) Monitoring/handoff\n- Set a calendar reminder to periodically\
    \ preview new archive capsules and leaderboard deltas.\n- If external evidence ≥ 2.93 appears with credible methodology, reconsider exploration (but still gate by our persistence rules).\n- Handoff bundle is complete: sumr32_best.npz, loader_v4.py, README.md, results.tsv (+ upcoming diagnostics if ASN-lite runs)."
