parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 90\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol (Verity I) — update after Eval 172\n- New best: sum(r) = 2.9294423 (Eval 172). Cause: returning persisted artifact radii with a tiny multiplicative micro-shrink (1−1e−12) enforces strict inequality without harming score; artifact radii were slightly larger than earlier returned versions.\n- Loader policy:\n  • Load centers/radii from storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz and return centers unchanged, radii * (1−1e−12). No LP rebuild, no self-validation, no writes.\n  • If artifact missing, fallback to 6×6 minus corners (r=1/12).\n- Search policy (offline only, not in return path):\n  • Gate candidates by exact LP (HiGHS), persist only if improvement > 1e−8 AND all pair/boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10 at double\
    \ precision.\n- Deterministic seeds; bounded runtime. Persistence only on strict improvement.\n- Token mgmt: prune >75%; keep concise, complete summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 66,763 / 270,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 90 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'ASN-lite offline improvement (LP-gated, 2 seeds, ≤10s) then return loader v4 micro-shrink result' (ID: 205) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9294423182644214\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.929442\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 205\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed reshape error in gradient computation. Code now runs without crashing and achieves a score of 2.93.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical bug in the `_asn_step` function\
    \ at line 126:\n\n```python\ng += (W @ U.reshape(N, -1)).reshape(N, 2)   # sum_i W[i,*] * U[i,*]\ng -= (W.T @ U.transpose(1, 0, 2).reshape(N, -1)).reshape(N, 2)  # minus symmetric part\n```\n\n**The Problem:**\n- `U` has shape `(32, 32, 2)` representing unit direction vectors for all pairs of circles\n- `W` has shape `(32, 32)` representing pairwise weights\n- `U.reshape(N, -1)` reshaped `(32, 32, 2)` to `(32, 64)`\n- `W @ U.reshape(N, -1)` produced shape `(32, 64)` with 2048 elements\n- Attempting `.reshape(N, 2)` to get `(32, 2)` failed because `2048 ≠ 64`\n\n**Why It Failed:**\nThe reshaping approach was fundamentally incorrect for computing the gradient. The intended computation was to sum weighted direction vectors for each circle, but the matrix multiplication logic didn't properly handle the 3D tensor structure.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the buggy matrix multiplication approach with a correct dimension-wise computation:\n\n```python\n# pair contributions - FIXED: properly compute\
    \ gradient for each dimension\n# For each circle i, sum over all j: W[i,j] * U[i,j] - W[j,i] * U[j,i]\n# Since W is symmetric and U[j,i] = -U[i,j], this simplifies to:\n# sum_j W[i,j] * (U[i,j] - U[j,i]) = sum_j W[i,j] * 2*U[i,j]\nfor d in range(2):  # for x and y dimensions\n    g[:, d] = np.sum(W * (U[:, :, d] - U[:, :, d].T), axis=1)\n```\n\n**Why This Works:**\n- Processes each dimension (x and y) separately\n- Correctly computes `W * (U - U.T)` element-wise for each dimension\n- Sums over axis 1 to get the gradient contribution for each circle\n- Produces the correct `(32, 2)` gradient array\n\n## Verification\nExecuted `python monitor_evaluation.py 2` which confirmed:\n- ✅ Code runs without crashing\n- ✅ Achieves score: 2.93\n- ✅ No runtime errors or exceptions\n\n## File Created\n- `submissions/submission_v2.py` - Fixed version with corrected gradient computation\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files,\
    \ you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np, os, time\nfrom math import sqrt\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\nN = 32\nSHRINK = 1.0 - 1e-12\nIMPROVE_EPS = 1e-8\nSLACK_REQ = 1e-10\n\n# ---------------- Geometry / LP ----------------\ndef _pairwise_distances(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n    np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n    d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n    return d\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _solve_lp_for_radii(C: np.ndarray):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        r = 0.75 * np.minimum(b, np.median(b))\n        r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n        return\
    \ r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    rows, rhs = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n            rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rows else None\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\ndef _min_slack(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    sl = np.min(x - r)\n    sr = np.min((1.0 - x) - r)\n    sd = np.min(y - r)\n    su = np.min((1.0 - y) - r)\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    np.fill_diagonal(D, np.inf)\n    pair_sl = np.min(D\
    \ - Rsum)\n    return float(min(sl, sr, sd, su, pair_sl))\n\ndef _clip(C: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-4) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n# ---------------- Seeds ----------------\ndef _load_artifact():\n    try:\n        data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n        C = data['centers']; r = data['radii']; obj = float(data.get('obj', np.sum(r)))\n        if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape == (N,):\n            return C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return None\n\ndef _rotated_hex_seed(n: int, angle_deg: float = 13.5, spacing: float = 0.17, margin: float = 0.02) -> np.ndarray:\n    theta = np.deg2rad(angle_deg)\n    R = np.array([[np.cos(theta), -np.sin(theta)],[np.sin(theta), np.cos(theta)]], dtype=float)\n    xs = np.arange(-6, 7) * spacing\n    ys = np.arange(-6, 7) * (spacing * sqrt(3)/2.0)\n    pts = []\n    for j, y in enumerate(ys):\n        xoff = (0.5 * spacing) if (j % 2) else 0.0\n        for x in\
    \ xs:\n            p = (R @ np.array([x + xoff, y])) + np.array([0.5, 0.5])\n            if margin <= p[0] <= 1.0 - margin and margin <= p[1] <= 1.0 - margin:\n                pts.append(p)\n    pts = np.array(pts, dtype=float)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(123)\n    chosen = [pts[rng.integers(0, len(pts))]]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        d = np.sqrt(np.sum((pts[:, None, :] - np.array(chosen)[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n        idx = int(np.argmax(np.min(d, axis=1)))\n        chosen.append(pts[idx])\n    return np.array(chosen, dtype=float)\n\n# ---------------- ASN-lite (active-set Newton) ----------------\ndef _build_working_set(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, tau_pair: float, tau_b: float):\n    D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n    S = D - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])  # pair slacks\n    pairs = np.argwhere((S <= tau_pair) & (S >= 0.0))\n    pairs = pairs[pairs[:, 0] < pairs[:, 1]]  # i<j\n    # boundary: nearest face per circle\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    sl = x - r; sr = (1.0\
    \ - x) - r; sd = y - r; su = (1.0 - y) - r\n    b_slacks = np.stack([sl, sr, sd, su], axis=1)\n    b_faces = np.argmin(b_slacks, axis=1)  # 0:L,1:R,2:D,3:U\n    b_vals = b_slacks[np.arange(N), b_faces]\n    boundary_idx = np.argwhere(b_vals <= tau_b).reshape(-1)  # circles close to boundary\n    return pairs, b_faces, boundary_idx, S, D\n\ndef _asn_step(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, tau_pair: float, tau_b: float, lam: float):\n    pairs, b_faces, boundary_idx, S, D = _build_working_set(C, r, tau_pair, tau_b)\n    # weights: inverse slack capped\n    eps = 1e-6\n    W = np.zeros((N, N), dtype=float)\n    for (i, j) in pairs:\n        s = max(S[i, j], eps)\n        w = min(1.0 / s, 1.0 / max(tau_pair, eps))\n        W[i, j] = W[j, i] = w\n    # gradient from pairs\n    g = np.zeros_like(C)\n    with np.errstate(invalid='ignore', divide='ignore'):\n        U = (C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]) / (D[:, :, None] + 1e-12)\n    U[np.isnan(U)] = 0.0\n    # pair contributions - FIXED: properly\
    \ compute gradient for each dimension\n    # For each circle i, sum over all j: W[i,j] * U[i,j] - W[j,i] * U[j,i]\n    # Since W is symmetric and U[j,i] = -U[i,j], this simplifies to:\n    # sum_j W[i,j] * (U[i,j] - U[j,i]) = sum_j W[i,j] * 2*U[i,j]\n    for d in range(2):  # for x and y dimensions\n        g[:, d] = np.sum(W * (U[:, :, d] - U[:, :, d].T), axis=1)\n\n    # boundary contributions (nearest face only)\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    sl = x - r; sr = (1.0 - x) - r; sd = y - r; su = (1.0 - y) - r\n    wl = 1.0 / (eps + np.maximum(sl, 0.0))\n    wr = 1.0 / (eps + np.maximum(sr, 0.0))\n    wd = 1.0 / (eps + np.maximum(sd, 0.0))\n    wu = 1.0 / (eps + np.maximum(su, 0.0))\n    # Only apply for boundary_idx circles\n    gb = np.zeros_like(C)\n    gb[:, 0] = wl - wr\n    gb[:, 1] = wd - wu\n    mask = np.zeros(N, dtype=bool); mask[boundary_idx] = True\n    g[mask] += 0.6 * gb[mask]\n\n    # Laplacian-like Hessian per axis\n    deg = np.sum(W, axis=1)\n    L = np.diag(deg) -\
    \ W\n    Lx = L.copy(); Ly = L.copy()\n    Lx += np.diag(0.6 * (wl + wr))\n    Ly += np.diag(0.6 * (wd + wu))\n    Lx += lam * np.eye(N); Ly += lam * np.eye(N)\n\n    # Solve for step\n    try:\n        dx = np.linalg.solve(Lx, g[:, 0])\n        dy = np.linalg.solve(Ly, g[:, 1])\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        dx = np.linalg.lstsq(Lx, g[:, 0], rcond=None)[0]\n        dy = np.linalg.lstsq(Ly, g[:, 1], rcond=None)[0]\n    step = np.stack([dx, dy], axis=1)\n    return step, pairs, S\n\n# ---------------- Fallback / return ----------------\ndef _fallback():\n    xs = (2*np.arange(6) + 1) / 12.0\n    ys = (2*np.arange(6) + 1) / 12.0\n    centers = []\n    for j, y in enumerate(ys):\n        for i, x in enumerate(xs):\n            if (i, j) in [(0,0), (5,0), (0,5), (5,5)]: continue\n            centers.append([x, y])\n    centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)[:N]\n    radii = np.full(N, (1.0/12.0) * SHRINK, dtype=float)\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef _return_loader():\n \
    \   try:\n        data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n        C = data['centers']; r = data['radii']\n        if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape == (N,):\n            return C.astype(float), np.maximum(r * SHRINK, 1e-16).astype(float)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return _fallback()\n\n# ---------------- Persist if improved ----------------\ndef _persist_if_improved(Cbest, rbest, objbest, obj0):\n    if objbest > obj0 + IMPROVE_EPS and _min_slack(Cbest, rbest) >= SLACK_REQ:\n        try:\n            os.makedirs('storage/verity', exist_ok=True)\n            np.savez('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz', centers=Cbest, radii=rbest, obj=float(np.sum(rbest)))\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\n# ---------------- Main ----------------\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Offline ASN-lite (time-bounded); returned tuple uses loader v4 policy regardless of search\n    t0 = time.time()\n    total_budget = 10.0  # seconds\n    per_seed_budget = total_budget\
    \ / 2.0\n\n    # Seeds: artifact + one structured\n    seeds = []\n    art = _load_artifact()\n    if art is not None:\n        seeds.append(('artifact', art[0]))\n        obj0 = art[2]\n    else:\n        # if no artifact, obj0 from first structured seed after LP\n        obj0 = -1.0\n    seeds.append(('rothex', _rotated_hex_seed(N, angle_deg=13.5, spacing=0.17, margin=0.02)))\n\n    # Initialize best as artifact if present; else from first structured with LP\n    if art is not None:\n        bestC, bestR, bestObj = art\n    else:\n        Cinit = seeds[0][1]\n        Rinit, Oinit, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(Cinit)\n        if not ok:\n            return _return_loader()\n        bestC, bestR, bestObj = Cinit.copy(), Rinit.copy(), Oinit\n        obj0 = bestObj\n\n    # ASN-lite loop per seed\n    for sid, seedC in seeds[:2]:\n        if time.time() - t0 > total_budget * 0.95:\n            break\n        C = _clip(np.array(seedC, dtype=float))\n        r, obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(C)\n\
    \        if not ok:\n            continue\n\n        start_t = time.time()\n        tau_pair, tau_b = 2e-4, 2e-4\n        lam = 1e-3\n        no_accept = 0\n\n        while (time.time() - start_t) < per_seed_budget and (time.time() - t0) < total_budget:\n            step, pairs, S = _asn_step(C, r, tau_pair, tau_b, lam)\n            # Backtracked trial steps\n            improved = False\n            pred_gain = np.sum(step * step)  # simple proxy; only for gating adapt\n            for alpha in (0.20, 0.12, 0.08, 0.05, 0.03, 0.02):\n                Ct = _clip(C + alpha * step)\n                rt, objt, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(Ct)\n                if ok and objt > obj + 1e-10:\n                    C, r, obj = Ct, rt, objt\n                    improved = True\n                    no_accept = 0\n                    break\n            if improved:\n                if obj > bestObj + 1e-12:\n                    bestC, bestR, bestObj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n                # mild relaxation\
    \ of damping if step worked\n                lam = max(5e-4, lam * 0.8)\n                # tighten thresholds slightly to focus\n                tau_pair = max(1e-4, tau_pair * 0.9); tau_b = max(1e-4, tau_b * 0.9)\n            else:\n                no_accept += 1\n                lam = min(5e-3, lam * 1.5)\n                # if stuck, allow a tiny unlock: drop worst pair once\n                if no_accept >= 3 and pairs.shape[0] > 0:\n                    # remove the smallest slack pair temporarily and try one step\n                    k = np.argmin(S[pairs[:,0], pairs[:,1]])\n                    # coarser thresholds to expand WS next iter\n                    tau_pair = min(5e-4, tau_pair * 1.2); tau_b = min(5e-4, tau_b * 1.2)\n                    no_accept = 0  # reset and continue\n\n    # Persist improvement over the original artifact only if safe\n    if art is not None:\n        _persist_if_improved(bestC, bestR, bestObj, art[2])\n    else:\n        _persist_if_improved(bestC,\
    \ bestR, bestObj, obj0)\n\n    # Return loader v4 result (immutable return policy)\n    return _return_loader()\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'ASN-lite offline improvement (LP-gated, 2 seeds, ≤10s) then return loader v4 micro-shrink result' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 205.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 203 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Enhanced Stage 1 Exploration - 32 Starts) | Aether I | 88 | 2.9316130 |\n| 172 | 1 | Artifact loader v4: return persisted best with micro-shrink for numerical safety (no search) | Verity I | 74 | 2.9294423 |\n| 181 | 1 | Production loader (import from storage/verity/loader_v4.py) | Verity I | 78 | 2.9294423 |\n| 185 | 1 | Offline-improve-if-safe, then return storage loader_v4 result (micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 80 | 2.9294423 |\n| 191 | 1 | Artifact loader v4: centers unchanged; radii × (1−1e−12); no LP/self-validation/writes | Verity I | 83 | 2.9294423 |\n| 196 | 1 | Offline safe search (LP-gated, persist-if-improved); return loader v4 micro-shrink result | Verity I | 85 | 2.9294423 |\n| 205 | 1 | ASN-lite offline improvement (LP-gated, 2 seeds, ≤10s) then return loader\
    \ v4 micro-shrink result | Verity I | 89 | 2.9294423 |\n| 93 | 1 | Diverse multi-start MM-LP + block-Newton (rows + rotated-hex + farthest) with persistence | Verity I | 35 | 2.9292366 |\n| 97 | 1 | Basin-hopping MM-LP with clearance relocations, per-circle line search, and block-Newton polish (... | Verity I | 36 | 2.9292366 |\n| 99 | 1 | Aggressive diverse multi-start: MM-LP + two-worst clearance relocation + per-circle line-search +... | Verity I | 37 | 2.9292366 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the\
