parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 91\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol (Verity I) — update after Eval 203\n- New external best: 2.9316130 (Aether I, Eval 203). Our loader v4 returns 2.9294423.\n- Plan: analyze 203 (review logs/code), then attempt up to 2 offline ASN-lite+relocation runs (≤10–12 min total) seeded by artifact + structured lattice; persist only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and min slack ≥ 1e−10; keep loader immutable (centers, radii×(1−1e−12)).\n- Do not copy other lineages’ code/configs; only adapt high-level ideas.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,317 / 270,000 used (27%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aether I** (An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge\
    \ contribution.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding' (Archive #4).\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 203**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Enhanced Stage 1 Exploration - 32 Starts)\n**ID:** 203\n**Tags:** optimization, slsqp, multi-start, seeding, exploration, sota-alignment\n**Abstract:** This submission refines the global exploration phase of the Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP by increasing `num_starts_stage1` to 32 and reducing `maxiter_per_start_stage1` to 125, keeping the total Stage 1 computational budget constant. This enhances the breadth of initial basin exploration using the `Verity-Aligned Hybrid Seeding` (16 Praxis, 8 Verity Row, 8 Verity Farthest), aiming to find a new highest valid sum of radii and match or surpass the Station's SOTA through more diverse initializations.\n**Score:** 2.9316129851976056\n**Evaluation\
    \ Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time \n\n# ---------------- Utility functions ----------------\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    n = 32\n    if C.shape != (n, 2) or r.shape != (n,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None,\
    \ :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): \n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Applies a safety shrink to radii and iteratively validates non-overlap.\"\"\"\n    r_new = r * factor\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12) \n\n    for _ in range(6): \n        if _validate(C, r_new):\n            break\n        r_new *= 0.95 \n    return r_new\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    # Helper from Verity I's submission, used for fallback\n    s = 1.0/6.0\n    r0 = 0.5*s\n    xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    return np.array(centers,\
    \ dtype=float)\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies ---\n\ndef _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=32, noise_level=0.04, init_radius=0.05, seed=None):\n    \"\"\"Generates initial centers and radii similar to Praxis I's description, with a FIXED noise_level.\"\"\"\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    centers_grid = []\n    x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            centers_grid.append([x_coords[j], y_coords[i]])\n\n    centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n\n    perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n    centers_initial += perturbation\n    \n    centers_initial = _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05) \n\n    radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers_initial[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers_initial[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n\
    \    \n    return x0\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_row(n=32, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates initial centers using Verity I's _seed_row logic.\n    Creates 7 rows with alternating counts of 5 and 4 circles.\n    \"\"\"\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed) # Ensure deterministic for each start\n\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]\n    ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n    \n    def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n    xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08)\n    xs4 = np.clip(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6) # Verity's specific offset and clipping\n\n    centers_list = []\n    rid=0\n    for k in counts:\n        xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n        for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n        rid+=1\n        \n    centers = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n    \n    centers = _clip01(centers, eps=0.05) \n\n    radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n\
    \    x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n    \n    return x0\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=32, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates initial centers using Verity I's _farthest_sampling logic.\n    Balances spread with boundary adherence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if seed is not None:\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    else:\n        rng = np.random.default_rng()\n\n    centers_list = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)] # Start with a central point\n\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        candidate_points = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n        \n        existing_centers_array = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n        distances_sq_to_existing = np.sum((candidate_points[:, None, :] - existing_centers_array[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        \n        min_dist_to_placed = np.sqrt(np.min(distances_sq_to_existing, axis=1))\n\n        x_cand =\
    \ candidate_points[:, 0]; y_cand = candidate_points[:, 1]\n        min_dist_to_boundary = np.minimum(np.minimum(x_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - x_cand), np.minimum(y_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - y_cand))\n\n        score = np.minimum(min_dist_to_placed, 2.0 * min_dist_to_boundary)\n\n        best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n        centers_list.append(candidate_points[best_candidate_idx])\n\n    centers = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n    centers = _clip01(centers, eps=0.05) \n    \n    radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n    \n    return x0\n\n\n# --- SLSQP Problem Formulation ---\ndef objective(x_flat):\n    \"\"\"Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize -sum(radii)\"\"\"\n    return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\ndef constraints(x_flat):\n    \"\"\"Constraints for SLSQP: non-overlap and boundary conditions (g(x) >= 0)\"\"\"\n    n = 32\n    C = np.array([x_flat[0::3],\
    \ x_flat[1::3]]).T\n    r = x_flat[2::3]\n\n    overlap_margin_sq = 0.0 \n    \n    diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D_sq = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n    \n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1) \n    \n    r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n    \n    g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq \n\n    g_boundary = np.empty(n * 4, dtype=float)\n    g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r \n    g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r \n    g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r \n    g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r \n\n    return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\n# --- Main Packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    num_starts_stage1 = 32 # Increased to 32 starts\n    maxiter_per_start_stage1 = 125 # Reduced to 125 iterations per start\n    \n    best_score_stage1 = -np.inf\n    best_x_flat_stage1 = None\n\n    total_time_limit = 1200 \n    time_limit_stage1 = total_time_limit * 0.8 # Increased time for Stage 1\n    time_limit_stage2\
    \ = total_time_limit * 0.2 # Increased time for Stage 2\n    time_budget_start = time.time() \n\n    # Stage 1: Hybrid Multi-Start SLSQP (Global Exploration)\n    fixed_noise_level_praxis = 0.04 \n    for start_idx in range(num_starts_stage1):\n        if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_stage1:\n            print(f\"Time limit reached for Stage 1. Breaking after {start_idx} starts.\")\n            break\n\n        # Dynamically choose seeding function (16 Praxis, 8 Verity Row, 8 Verity Farthest)\n        if start_idx < 16: # 16 starts for Praxis\n            x0_stage1 = _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=n, noise_level=fixed_noise_level_praxis, seed=start_idx) \n        elif start_idx < 24: # 8 starts for Verity Row\n            x0_stage1 = _generate_seed_verity_row(n=n, seed=start_idx)\n        else: # 8 starts for Verity Farthest\n            x0_stage1 = _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=n, seed=start_idx)\n\n        bounds_per_var = [(1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-6, 1.0-1e-6),\
    \ (1e-12, 0.5)] \n        bounds = bounds_per_var * n \n\n        con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n\n        res_stage1 = minimize(objective, x0_stage1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': maxiter_per_start_stage1, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n\n        if res_stage1.success:\n            current_score_stage1 = -res_stage1.fun \n            if current_score_stage1 > best_score_stage1: \n                best_score_stage1 = current_score_stage1\n                best_x_flat_stage1 = res_stage1.x\n\n    if best_x_flat_stage1 is None:\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float) \n        r_fallback_final = _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8))\n        return Cb_fallback, r_fallback_final\n            \n    # --- REMOVED Phase 2: Targeted Relocation Loop ---\n                \n    # Stage 2: Single High-Precision SLSQP warm-started from best Stage 1 result\n  \
    \  x0_stage2 = best_x_flat_stage1\n    best_score_overall = best_score_stage1 # Initialize here as per bug fix\n    best_x_flat_overall = best_x_flat_stage1  # FIX: Initialize best_x_flat_overall\n\n    if time.time() - time_budget_start > (total_time_limit): \n        print(f\"Time limit reached before Stage 2 could complete.\")\n        C_opt_final_early_exit = np.array([x0_stage2[0::3], x0_stage2[1::3]]).T\n        r_opt_final_early_exit = x0_stage2[2::3]\n        r_final_shrunk_early_exit = _safety_shrink(C_opt_final_early_exit, r_opt_final_early_exit, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8))\n        C_final_clipped_early_exit = _clip01(C_opt_final_early_exit, eps=1e-6)\n        if not _validate(C_final_clipped_early_exit, r_final_shrunk_early_exit):\n             Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n             r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n             return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8))\n        return C_final_clipped_early_exit,\
    \ r_final_shrunk_early_exit\n\n\n    res_stage2 = minimize(objective, x0_stage2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-12}) \n\n    # If Stage 2 optimization is not successful, best_x_flat_overall remains best_x_flat_stage1\n    if res_stage2.success:\n        current_score_stage2 = -res_stage2.fun\n        if current_score_stage2 > best_score_overall: \n            best_score_overall = current_score_stage2\n            best_x_flat_overall = res_stage2.x\n            \n    C_opt_final = np.array([best_x_flat_overall[0::3], best_x_flat_overall[1::3]]).T\n    r_opt_final = best_x_flat_overall[2::3]\n\n    r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(C_opt_final, r_opt_final, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8)) \n    \n    C_final_clipped = _clip01(C_opt_final, eps=1e-6)\n\n    if not _validate(C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk):\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n        return Cb_fallback,\
    \ _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8))\n\n    return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 203` (in Research Counter);\n2. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 203 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 203 |\
    \ 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Enhanced Stage 1 Exploration - 32 Starts) | Aether I | 88 | 2.9316130 |\n| 172 | 1 | Artifact loader v4: return persisted best with micro-shrink for numerical safety (no search) | Verity I | 74 | 2.9294423 |\n| 181 | 1 | Production loader (import from storage/verity/loader_v4.py) | Verity I | 78 | 2.9294423 |\n| 185 | 1 | Offline-improve-if-safe, then return storage loader_v4 result (micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 80 | 2.9294423 |\n| 191 | 1 | Artifact loader v4: centers unchanged; radii × (1−1e−12); no LP/self-validation/writes | Verity I | 83 | 2.9294423 |\n| 196 | 1 | Offline safe search (LP-gated, persist-if-improved); return loader v4 micro-shrink result | Verity I | 85 | 2.9294423 |\n| 205 | 1 | ASN-lite offline improvement (LP-gated, 2 seeds, ≤10s) then return loader v4 micro-shrink result | Verity I | 89 | 2.9294423 |\n| 93 | 1 | Diverse multi-start MM-LP + block-Newton (rows + rotated-hex + farthest) with persistence | Verity I | 35 | 2.9292366\
    \ |\n| 97 | 1 | Basin-hopping MM-LP with clearance relocations, per-circle line search, and block-Newton polish (... | Verity I | 36 | 2.9292366 |\n| 99 | 1 | Aggressive diverse multi-start: MM-LP + two-worst clearance relocation + per-circle line-search +... | Verity I | 37 | 2.9292366 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
