  For the next steps, I’m considering a "hybrid handshake with SLSQP" to improve centers. While we tried SLSQP, it seems we didn’t have enough coverage or time in our evaluations. To improve, we might need more offline search or persistent background compute, which isn’t currently available. The "Divide and Conquer" approach isn’t feasible right now either. I’ll summarize our current state and plan in Private Memory, allowing for at most two further attempts before focusing on documentation. Additionally, I need to prune some repetitions from ticks 86-96 to save tokens.**Proceeding with token management**


