parts:
- text: "Tick 2: Concrete parameters, screening metric, and acceptance logic\n\nSeed generation (deterministic, compact, diverse)\n- Rotated-hex mosaics (12 variants total):\n  - Angle deg ∈ {9, 11, 13, 15}\n  - Spacing s ∈ {0.168, 0.171, 0.174}\n  - Anisotropy ax/ay ∈ {1.00, 0.985} (apply to x before rotation)\n  - Build lattice, crop to box, greedily farthest-subselect to n=32.\n- Farthest-point seeds (6 variants):\n  - Boundary-penalty λ ∈ {0.7, 1.0, 1.3}\n  - Two tie-breaker streams per λ (fixed seeds), sample 400 candidates/placement, domain margin 0.02.\n- Total 18 seeds → pre-screen down to 6–8.\n\nPre-screening features (computed after LP on fixed centers)\n- f1: LP score (sum radii).\n- f2: Boundary-contact ratio: fraction of circles where r_i equals min{x_i,1−x_i,y_i,1−y_i} within 1e-8 (lower is better early).\n- f3: Near-active contact graph spectral gap λ2:\n  - Define near-active pairs where slack s_ij = d_ij − (r_i + r_j) ≤ τ_na with τ_na = 3e-4.\n  - Build unweighted Laplacian\
    \ L from these edges; λ2 = second-smallest eigenvalue (higher ⇒ better connectivity/escape potential).\n- f4: Degree entropy H of the near-active graph (favor moderate spread vs overly concentrated contacts).\n- f5: Min slack after micro-shrink r←r(1−1e−12): s_min = min(boundary slacks, pair slacks).\n- Diversity: embed centers by vectorizing the 32×32 distance matrix (or its top-10 PCA components); during selection, greedily pick seeds maximizing minimum embedding distance.\n\nComposite screening score (normalize each feature to [0,1] across the 18 seeds)\n- Maximize S = 0.50·norm(f1) + 0.25·norm(λ2) + 0.15·norm(H) − 0.30·norm(boundary ratio).\n- Hard filter: s_min ≥ 5e-11 (post micro-shrink) or drop.\n- Diversity selection: pick the best seed, then iteratively add the seed with the largest minimum distance to already chosen; stop at 6–8 seeds.\n\nRefiner schedule per kept seed (strictly offline, ≤1–1.5 min/seed)\n- SLSQP “centers-only” burst (30–45 s):\n  - Box bounds [m,1−m], m=1e-3\
    \ (keep away from edges).\n  - Surrogate objective: increase weighted near-active slacks (e.g., sum w_ij·s_ij with w_ij = 1/(ε+s_ij)) + boundary slack terms; exact LP used as accept gate, not inside the steps.\n  - Deterministic initial step sizes; 5–10 inner restarts if no progress.\n- ASN polish (20–30 s):\n  - Working set W = near-active pairs (s_ij ≤ τ_na) + boundary faces where slack ≤ τ_b = 5e-4.\n  - Damped Newton direction from dual-like weights; trust-region backtracking with α ∈ {0.25, 0.16, 0.10, 0.06, 0.04, 0.025, 0.015, 0.01}.\n  - Refresh W every accepted step or after 3 rejections.\n\nAcceptance and model-agreement checks\n- Exact LP gate: accept only if ΔLP = ∑r_new − ∑r_old > 1e-8 and s_min(new, micro-shrunk) ≥ 1e-10.\n- Predicted vs actual agreement:\n  - Build a simple predicted gain Δpred from the quadratic model on W (linearized slack increase with diagonal damping).\n  - Ratio ρ = ΔLP / max(Δpred, 1e-12).\n  - If ρ < 0.25: shrink trust region (halve α or increase\
    \ damping); if ρ > 0.7 for 3 consecutive accepts: cautiously expand α (×1.2).\n- Stagnation rules:\n  - If no accept in 10 attempts: perform one worst-circle clearance relocation (best-of-200 samples via clearance map), then resume; if still no accept after 20 total attempts, end the seed.\n\nPersistence discipline and validation\n- A candidate artifact must beat the current artifact by >1e-8 and s_min ≥ 1e-10 (micro-shrunk). Recompute slacks in double precision.\n- Repro check: improvement should appear on at least 2 distinct seeds (within 1e-6 of each other) to avoid one-off numeric artifacts before persisting.\n\nBudget and batch plan\n- Batch 1: 6 seeds × ~75 s = ~7.5–9 min + overhead; Batch 2 repeats if and only if any seed reaches ≥2.9305 (clear above current 2.92944).\n- If both batches fail to produce a safe improvement, terminate exploration per exit criteria and remain in maintenance mode.\n\nLogging (for later analysis and handoff)\n- For every seed: initial LP, boundary ratio,\
    \ λ2, H, s_min; per accept: ΔLP, ρ, new s_min, contact degrees. Record final best LP and metrics. Persist results.tsv entries only on accepted improvements; otherwise, log to a local scratch file to avoid token bloat.\n\nNext tick: exact thresholds sanity (τ_na, τ_b), surrogate objective weighting for SLSQP, and how to choose m (margin) adaptively based on boundary ratio to avoid early over-binding to walls."
