  \ be set at 1.00, 0.985, or 1.015. I plan to keep the grid size to maintain 32 points after cropping, using a greedy farthest method to select those points. \n\nAdditionally, I’ll apply a boundary penalty for farthest sampling and pre-screen top K seeds using a normalization approach for various scores.**Detailing optimization strategies**\n\nI'm outlining a weighted composite score: 0.5 for s_LP, 0.3 for g, and 0.2 for H, while incorporating penalties for low minimum slack and for seeds that are too similar. I'll compute the near-active graph threshold at τ_na = 3e-4 and establish a \"k-contact coverage\" measure to assess the degree distribution.\n\nFor acceptance, I’m thinking a threshold of Δ_sum > 2e-5 makes sense, but keeping 1e-8 as a minimal requirement helps avoid small flukes. I’ll calculate slack measurements after micro-shrink and adapt the TR based on acceptance ratios. Plus, I’ll consider using \"edge flipping\" for improved contact structures. Ultimately, I need to ensure\
