tick: 104
role: model
parts:
- text: "Tick 4: Minimal diagnostics, auto-tuning rules, and “quick-decision” success criteria\n\nCheap diagnostics to compute at each LP-evaluated state\n- Score and gains: ∑r, ΔLP since last accept, cumulative ΔLP for the seed.\n- Slack health (post micro-shrink): s_min; slack quantiles q10, q25 for pair slacks; boundary slack median.\n- Boundary-contact ratio (BCR): fraction with r_i equal to a face within 1e-8.\n- Near-active contact graph (thresholded):\n  - Edge count |E|; per-node degree stats (median, max).\n  - Spectral gap λ2 (unweighted Laplacian on edges where slack ≤ τ_na).\n- Model-agreement: predicted gain Δpred vs actual ΔLP; ratio ρ = ΔLP / max(Δpred, 1e-12).\n\nAuto-tuning τ_na, τ_b, and working-set size\n- Target near-active density: |E| in [2n, 4n] (≈64–128 for n=32), per-node degree median ≈4–6.\n  - If |E| > 5n or degree max > 9: shrink by setting τ_na to the 20th percentile of current near-active slack; also cap neighbors per node to k=5–6.\n  - If |E| < 1.5n or degree\
    \ median < 3: expand by setting τ_na to the 40th percentile; allow k up to 7.\n  - Hysteresis: only change τ_na if it would move by ≥1e-4, to avoid thrashing.\n- Boundary threshold τ_b (guide wall influence):\n  - If BCR > 0.35: τ_b = 8e-4 and β (boundary weight) = 0.7.\n  - If 0.20 < BCR ≤ 0.35: τ_b = 5e-4, β = 0.5.\n  - If BCR ≤ 0.20: τ_b = 3e-4, β = 0.35.\n  - Update at accept events only; never decrease τ_b if BCR is rising.\n- Damping and trust region via model-agreement:\n  - If ρ < 0.25 (over-optimistic model): λ ×= 2 or α ×= 0.5; keep τ_na, τ_b fixed.\n  - If 0.25 ≤ ρ ≤ 0.7: keep λ, α.\n  - If ρ > 0.7 for 3 accepts: α ×= 1.2 (capped), λ ×= 0.8 (floored).\n\nWhen to expand/shrink the working set W explicitly\n- Expand W if: λ2 < 0.06 AND |E| < 2n (graph too loose) OR Δpred ≈ 0 but ΔLP>0 appears after occasional tries (missing constraints).\n- Shrink W if: |E| > 5n OR frequent rejections with ρ << 0.25 (model too “stiff” due to weak edges); drop weakest 25% of edges (largest slacks)\
    \ and reassemble.\n- Per-node cap enforcement: after any expand, re-cap degrees to k to avoid ill-conditioning.\n\nSLSQP surrogate’s safety guards\n- Barrier parameters: δ_b = 5e-6; p = 1.0; w_max = 1e6; γ (L2 reg) start 1e-4, halve it when 3 consecutive accepts with ρ>0.7, double it after 5 rejections.\n- Adaptive bounds margin m:\n  - m = 0.004 if BCR>0.35; 0.002 if 0.20<BCR≤0.35; 0.001 otherwise. Update only on accept.\n\nQuick triage and early-stopping per seed (to protect the batch budget)\n- After initial LP on the seed:\n  - Drop immediately if ∑r < 2.90 AND BCR > 0.5 AND λ2 < 0.05 (bad basin).\n- During attempts:\n  - If 10 proposals yield cumulative ΔLP < 5e-9: attempt one worst-circle clearance relocation (best-of-250); if still no accept after 20 total proposals: stop the seed.\n  - If s_min ever falls below 5e-11 (post micro-shrink) on a candidate: reject candidate and increase λ or reduce α; do not persist.\n\nNumerical “success” criteria for persistence decisions\n- Must-be-true:\n\
    \  - ΔLP over current artifact > 1e-8 AND s_min ≥ 1e-10 (post micro-shrink) on the candidate.\n  - Repro plausibility: a second, distinct seed reaches within 1e-6 of the same ∑r (or better) under the same thresholds.\n- Strong-signals-to-continue (but not yet persist):\n  - Seed crosses 2.9305 with s_min ≥ 2e-10 and BCR ≤ 0.35; λ2 ≥ 0.08; degree median 4–6.\n  - Two accepts with total ΔLP ≥ 3e-8 and ρ median ≥ 0.5.\n- Stop conditions (batch-level):\n  - No seed exceeds 2.92946 (artifact + 2e-5) within 12–15 minutes → end batch.\n  - After two batches with no safe improvement, exit to maintenance mode.\n\nMinimal logs to keep decisions lightweight and auditable\n- Per seed: {seed_id, type, initial ∑r, BCR, λ2, s_min}.\n- Per accept: {ΔLP, new ∑r, s_min, BCR, |E|, degree median/max, λ2, ρ, α, λ}.\n- End-of-seed: {best ∑r, accepts, cumulative ΔLP, time}.\n- Persisted candidate (if any): artifact path, SHA256, metrics snapshot, and “repro across seeds” note.\n\nNext (Tick 5): a crisp 2-batch\
    \ execution checklist (what to run, in what order, with time caps), and explicit “go/no-go” gates after Batch 1 to decide whether Batch 2 is warranted."
thinking_content: "**Evaluating prediction adjustments**\n\nIf there's a predicted mismatch because of missing constraints, I should include the next tier pairs with slack in (τ_na, τ_na + Δ) or those near the threshold. Otherwise, I’ll shrink the selection by removing the lowest weights or pairs that show inconsistent alignment.\n\nFor step acceptance gating and trust regions, I’ll maintain the schedule for step sizes and adapt based on acceptance, ramping up damping λ. \n\nTo measure success for persistence, I’ll focus on improvements greater than 1e-8, ensuring reproducibility and stability across different runs and randomizations.**Examining deterministic re-runs**\n\nI can't re-run inside the station, but offline re-runs are quick while keeping determinism. I’ll calculate an aggregated improvement measure across the top-2 seeds and compare that to the baseline. \n\nAn additional metric I’ll track is the contact count, aiming for BCR to be less than 0.35, with a maximum per-node contact\
  \ of around 6.\n\nFor logging, I’ll record details per seed, including seed ID, metrics, gains, and a summary saved to results.tsv. I'll also address potential artifacts by dumping data to a new file.**Setting thresholds and parameters**\n\nI need to establish typical ranges since I didn't compute them earlier. For the λ2 minimum target, I’m suggesting 0.06 early on, increasing to over 0.12 later. \n\nThe target edges should be between 48-128, and I aim for a BCR of less than 0.3 after the initial steps. After micro-shrink thresholds, I want s_min to be at least 3e-10 for early accepted steps, ensuring it's more than 1e-10 by the end.\n\nI’ll suggest early triage: if f1 is low (<2.90) or BCR is over 0.5 with λ2 below 0.05, then we should drop it."
