role: model
parts:
- text: "Tick 5: Two-batch execution checklist, go/no-go gates, and close-out plan\n\nBatch 0 (pre-flight; ≤1 min)\n- Fix RNG seeds and wall-clock budget; confirm loader v4 remains frozen (return centers, radii ×(1−1e−12)).\n- Load current artifact metrics (∑r=2.9294423; s_min after micro-shrink; BCR; λ2).\n- Prepare lightweight logging (seed_id, metrics at start/accept/end) without touching return path.\n\nBatch 1 (curated breadth; target ≤12–15 min total)\n1) Seed bank construction (deterministic):\n   - 12 rotated-hex variants: angle ∈ {9°,11°,13°,15°} × spacing s ∈ {0.168,0.171,0.174} × anisotropy {1.00,0.985}; crop to box; farthest-subselect to n=32.\n   - 6 farthest-point variants: boundary penalty λ ∈ {0.7,1.0,1.3} × 2 deterministic draws; margin 0.02; 400 candidates/placement.\n   - Total 18 seeds.\n2) Pre-screen each seed with an exact LP (fixed centers):\n   - Compute features: LP score, s_min (post micro-shrink), BCR, near-active graph λ2 (slack ≤ τ_na initial 3e-4), degree stats,\
    \ H (degree entropy).\n   - Composite score S = 0.50·norm(LP) + 0.25·norm(λ2) + 0.15·norm(H) − 0.30·norm(BCR).\n   - Hard filter: s_min ≥ 5e-11; then diversity pick 6–8 seeds by greedy max-min distance in a PCA embedding of pairwise distances.\n3) Per kept seed (≤95 s/seed):\n   - SLSQP burst (centers-only; bounds [m,1−m], m adaptive by BCR: 0.004/0.002/0.001):\n     • Optimize smooth barrier surrogate on near-active slacks (δ_b=5e-6; β≈0.5; reg γ≈1e-4). Exact LP used only as accept gate.\n   - ASN polish (working set W from near-active pairs and boundary faces):\n     • Trust-region backtracking α ∈ {0.25,…,0.01}; damping λ start 1e-3; model-agreement ratio ρ guides α/λ.\n     • Auto-tune τ_na to keep |E| in [2n,4n] with degree cap k=5–6; τ_b by BCR (8e-4→3e-4).\n   - Rescue once if needed: worst-circle clearance relocation (best-of-250) then short ASN.\n   - Acceptance gate (strict): ΔLP > 1e-8 and s_min(new, micro-shrunk) ≥ 1e-10; log ΔLP, ρ, λ2, BCR.\n   - Early-stop per seed: if\
    \ 20 proposals yield <5e-9 cumulative ΔLP or metrics degenerate (e.g., λ2 < 0.05 and BCR > 0.5), stop seed.\n4) Batch 1 persistence decision (do not affect return tuple):\n   - Mark “candidate” if any seed beats artifact by >1e-8 and passes slack gate.\n   - Require reproducibility plausibility: a second, distinct seed within 1e-6 of the candidate score (or better) under same checks before persisting.\n   - If persisted, compute micro-shrunk metrics and revalidate s_min ≥ 1e-10 (double precision) immediately.\n\nGo/No-Go gate for Batch 2\n- Go to Batch 2 only if Batch 1 produced at least one seed with ∑r ≥ 2.9305 and s_min ≥ 2e-10 (post micro-shrink), or if two seeds beat 2.9294423 by ≥3e-8 each with stable ρ (median ≥0.5).\n- Otherwise, skip Batch 2 and proceed to maintenance.\n\nBatch 2 (focused depth; ≤12–15 min total)\n- Select top 3 seeds by LP score and λ2 (diverse by embedding); carry forward their tuned τ_na/τ_b/m.\n- Schedule per seed (≤4–5 min):\n  - Short SLSQP (20–30 s) only\
    \ if BCR still high (>0.3); otherwise go straight to ASN.\n  - ASN depth pass (40–60 s): tighter W (cap k=5), stronger damping control; enlarge α by ×1.2 only after three accepts with ρ>0.7.\n  - One optional rescue if completely stalled; else stop early.\n- Persistence rule unchanged (ΔLP > 1e-8; s_min ≥ 1e-10; reproducibility across ≥2 seeds within 1e-6).\n\nSuccess criteria (to justify artifact update)\n- Minimum: best candidate ∑r > 2.9294423 by >1e-8 with s_min ≥ 1e-10 (micro-shrunk), reproduced on a second seed within 1e-6.\n- Strong: cross 2.9305 with healthy metrics (λ2 ≥ 0.08; BCR ≤ 0.35).\n\nClose-out and maintenance\n- If neither batch meets success criteria, declare exploration complete; remain in maintenance mode with:\n  - Frozen loader v4; no in-return refiners.\n  - Documentation up to date (results.tsv entries for any accepted runs; shorthand notes for rejected attempts).\n  - Standing note: further progress likely requires broader exploration or a novel move beyond\
    \ current low-risk toolkit.\n\nRisk summary\n- Low operational risk: all search offline; return tuple unchanged and safe; strict accept gates and slack checks; deterministic seeds; bounded time.\n- Upside: moderate; curated seeds + better working-set control and boundary management could uncover a slightly denser basin. A leap to 2.9316 is ambitious but a measurable advance toward it is plausible; if absent, we stop quickly."
