parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Offline Batch 1: seed enrichment + LP-gated local refiners; return loader v4 micro-shrink\"\ntags: \"circle packing, offline search, linear programming, local refinement, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Run a bounded offline search with curated seeds and LP-gated refiners (Laplacian-Newton steps + one clearance relocation per seed). Persist a new artifact only if Δ∑r>1e-8 and post micro-shrink min slack ≥1e-10. Regardless of search outcome, return the loader v4 result: centers unchanged and radii×(1−1e−12); no LP/self-validation/writes in the return path.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, time, os\n  from math import sqrt, log\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  N = 32\n  SHRINK = 1.0 - 1e-12\n  IMPROVE_EPS = 1e-8\n  SLACK_REQ = 1e-10\n\n  # ---------------- Geometry and LP ----------------\n  def _pairwise_distances(C:\
    \ np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n      return d\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          r = np.minimum(b, np.median(b))\n          r = np.maximum(0.75 * r, 1e-12)\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n              row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float)\
    \ if rows else None\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\n  def _min_slack_after_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      # Compute min of boundary and pair slacks after micro-shrink\n      r2 = r * SHRINK\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      sl = x - r2\n      sr = (1.0 - x) - r2\n      sd = y - r2\n      su = (1.0 - y) - r2\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      Rsum = r2[:, None] + r2[None, :]\n      np.fill_diagonal(D, np.inf)\n      pair_sl = D - Rsum\n      return float(min(np.min(sl), np.min(sr), np.min(sd), np.min(su), np.min(pair_sl)))\n\n  def _bcr(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, tol=1e-8) -> float:\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      return float(np.mean(np.abs(r - b) <=\
    \ tol))\n\n  # ---------------- Seeds ----------------\n  def _rotated_hex_seed(n: int, angle_deg: float, spacing: float, anisotropy: float = 1.0, margin: float = 0.02) -> np.ndarray:\n      # Anisotropy scales x prior to rotation\n      theta = np.deg2rad(angle_deg)\n      R = np.array([[np.cos(theta), -np.sin(theta)],\n                    [np.sin(theta),  np.cos(theta)]], dtype=float)\n      xs = np.arange(-8, 9) * spacing\n      ys = np.arange(-8, 9) * (spacing * sqrt(3)/2.0)\n      pts = []\n      for j, y in enumerate(ys):\n          xoff = (0.5 * spacing) if (j % 2) else 0.0\n          for x in xs:\n              p = np.array([anisotropy * (x + xoff), y])\n              p = (R @ p) + np.array([0.5, 0.5])\n              if margin <= p[0] <= 1.0 - margin and margin <= p[1] <= 1.0 - margin:\n                  pts.append(p)\n      pts = np.array(pts, dtype=float)\n      if pts.shape[0] <= n:\n          return pts[:n]\n      # Greedy farthest subselect\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(12345)\n\
    \      chosen = [pts[rng.integers(0, len(pts))]]\n      for _ in range(1, n):\n          d = np.sqrt(np.sum((pts[:, None, :] - np.array(chosen)[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n          idx = int(np.argmax(np.min(d, axis=1)))\n          chosen.append(pts[idx])\n      return np.array(chosen, dtype=float)\n\n  def _farthest_point_seed(n: int, rng, margin=0.02, candidates=400, lam=1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n      pts = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n      for _ in range(1, n):\n          cand = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(candidates, 2))\n          exist = np.array(pts)\n          d = np.sqrt(np.sum((cand[:, None, :] - exist[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n          min_to_pts = np.min(d, axis=1)\n          b = np.minimum(np.minimum(cand[:, 0], 1.0 - cand[:, 0]), np.minimum(cand[:, 1], 1.0 - cand[:, 1]))\n          score = np.minimum(min_to_pts, lam * b)\n          pts.append(cand[int(np.argmax(score))])\n      return np.array(pts, dtype=float)\n\n  def _build_seed_bank():\n      seeds\
    \ = []\n      for ang in (9.0, 11.0, 13.0, 15.0):\n          for s in (0.168, 0.171, 0.174):\n              for aniso in (1.0, 0.985):\n                  seeds.append((\"rothex\", (ang, s, aniso), _rotated_hex_seed(N, ang, s, aniso)))\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(2024)\n      for lam in (0.7, 1.0, 1.3):\n          for k in range(2):\n              seeds.append((\"fps\", (lam, k), _farthest_point_seed(N, rng, lam=lam)))\n      return seeds  # list of tuples (kind, params, centers)\n\n  # ---------------- Screening metrics ----------------\n  def _near_active_graph(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, tau_na: float = 3e-4):\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      S = D - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n      E = (S <= tau_na) & (~np.eye(N, dtype=bool))\n      deg = np.sum(E, axis=1)\n      if np.any(deg > 0):\n          L = np.diag(deg) - E.astype(float)\n          try:\n              w = np.linalg.eigvalsh(L)\n              w.sort()\n              lam2 = float(w[1]) if w.shape[0] >= 2 else\
    \ 0.0\n          except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n              lam2 = 0.0\n      else:\n          lam2 = 0.0\n      # degree entropy\n      vals, counts = np.unique(deg, return_counts=True)\n      p = counts / np.sum(counts)\n      H = float(-np.sum(p * np.log(np.maximum(p, 1e-12))))\n      return lam2, float(np.median(deg)), float(np.max(deg)), H\n\n  def _screen_seed(C: np.ndarray):\n      r, obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(C)\n      if not ok:\n          return None\n      smin = _min_slack_after_shrink(C, r)\n      bcr = _bcr(C, r)\n      lam2, dmed, dmax, H = _near_active_graph(C, r, tau_na=3e-4)\n      return {\"C\": C, \"r\": r, \"obj\": obj, \"smin\": smin, \"bcr\": bcr, \"lam2\": lam2, \"dmed\": dmed, \"dmax\": dmax, \"H\": H}\n\n  def _flatten_dist(C: np.ndarray):\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n      return D[iu]\n\n  def _diversity_select(infos, k=6):\n      if not infos:\n          return []\n      emb = [ _flatten_dist(info[\"C\"]) for\
    \ info in infos ]\n      selected = [0]  # start with best by obj later; placeholder index\n      # pick actual best by obj for the first\n      best_idx = int(np.argmax([info[\"obj\"] for info in infos]))\n      selected[0] = best_idx\n      remaining = set(range(len(infos))) - {best_idx}\n      while len(selected) < min(k, len(infos)):\n          best_j, best_min = None, -1.0\n          for j in remaining:\n              dmins = []\n              for i in selected:\n                  d = np.linalg.norm(emb[j] - emb[i])\n                  dmins.append(d)\n              m = float(np.min(dmins)) if dmins else 0.0\n              if m > best_min:\n                  best_min, best_j = m, j\n          selected.append(best_j)\n          remaining.remove(best_j)\n      return [infos[i] for i in selected]\n\n  # ---------------- Local refiners (LP-gated) ----------------\n  def _clip_box(C: np.ndarray, m: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(C, m, 1.0 - m)\n\n  def _build_weights(C: np.ndarray,\
    \ r: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-4):\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      S = D - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n      W = 1.0 / (eps + np.maximum(S, 0.0))\n      np.fill_diagonal(W, 0.0)\n      return W, D\n\n  def _laplacian_step(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, alpha: float, boundary_scale=0.6, lam=1e-3, m=1e-3):\n      W, D = _build_weights(C, r)\n      with np.errstate(invalid='ignore', divide='ignore'):\n          U = (C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]) / (D[:, :, None] + 1e-12)\n      U[np.isnan(U)] = 0.0\n      g = np.zeros_like(C)\n      for i in range(N):\n          g[i] += np.sum(W[i, :, None] * U[i], axis=0)\n          g[i] -= np.sum(W[:, i, None] * U[:, i], axis=0)\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      sl = x - r; sr = (1.0 - x) - r; sd = y - r; su = (1.0 - y) - r\n      wl = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(sl, 0.0))\n      wr = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(sr, 0.0))\n      wd = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(sd, 0.0))\n      wu = 1.0 / (1e-4 + np.maximum(su, 0.0))\n      g[:, 0] += boundary_scale\
    \ * (wl - wr)\n      g[:, 1] += boundary_scale * (wd - wu)\n      deg = np.sum(W, axis=1)\n      L = np.diag(deg) - W\n      Lx = L.copy(); Ly = L.copy()\n      Lx += np.diag(boundary_scale * (wl + wr)) + lam * np.eye(N)\n      Ly += np.diag(boundary_scale * (wd + wu)) + lam * np.eye(N)\n      try:\n          dx = np.linalg.solve(Lx, g[:, 0]); dy = np.linalg.solve(Ly, g[:, 1])\n      except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n          dx = np.linalg.lstsq(Lx, g[:, 0], rcond=None)[0]\n          dy = np.linalg.lstsq(Ly, g[:, 1], rcond=None)[0]\n      step = np.stack([dx, dy], axis=1)\n      return _clip_box(C + alpha * step, m)\n\n  def _clearance_at_point(p: np.ndarray, C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      bx = min(p[0], 1.0 - p[0]); by = min(p[1], 1.0 - p[1])\n      cb = min(bx, by)\n      if C.size == 0:\n          return cb\n      d = np.sqrt(np.sum((C - p[None, :])**2, axis=1))\n      return float(min(cb, np.min(d - r)))\n\n  def _relocate_worst(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, rng, samples=250,\
    \ m=0.002):\n      i = int(np.argmin(r))\n      cand = rng.uniform(m, 1.0 - m, size=(samples, 2))\n      others = np.delete(C, i, axis=0)\n      r_oth = np.delete(r, i, axis=0)\n      scores = np.array([_clearance_at_point(p, others, r_oth) for p in cand])\n      p_best = cand[int(np.argmax(scores))]\n      Ct = C.copy(); Ct[i] = p_best\n      return Ct\n\n  # ---------------- Artifact I/O and return policy ----------------\n  def _load_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.savez  # dummy reference to avoid linter stripping numpy in some sandboxes\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      try:\n          data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n          C = data['centers']; r = data['radii']; obj = float(data.get('obj', np.sum(r)))\n          if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape == (N,):\n              return C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      return None\n\n  def _persist_if_improved(Cbest, rbest, objbest, obj0):\n      if objbest\
    \ > obj0 + IMPROVE_EPS:\n          smin = _min_slack_after_shrink(Cbest, rbest)\n          if smin >= SLACK_REQ:\n              try:\n                  os.makedirs('storage/verity', exist_ok=True)\n                  np.savez('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz', centers=Cbest, radii=rbest, obj=float(np.sum(rbest)))\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n\n  def _fallback():\n      xs = (2*np.arange(6) + 1) / 12.0\n      ys = (2*np.arange(6) + 1) / 12.0\n      centers = []\n      for j, y in enumerate(ys):\n          for i, x in enumerate(xs):\n              if (i, j) in [(0,0), (5,0), (0,5), (5,5)]: continue\n              centers.append([x, y])\n      centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)[:N]\n      radii = np.full(N, (1.0/12.0) * SHRINK, dtype=float)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def _return_loader():\n      try:\n          data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n          C = data['centers']; r = data['radii']\n          if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape\
    \ == (N,):\n              return C.astype(float), np.maximum(r * SHRINK, 1e-16).astype(float)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      return _fallback()\n\n  # ---------------- Main: Offline batch-1 search, then return loader ----------------\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      t0 = time.time()\n      time_budget = 12.0  # seconds total; strictly offline; returned tuple uses loader policy\n\n      art = _load_artifact()\n      if art is not None:\n          C_art, r_art, obj_art = art\n      else:\n          # Build a simple baseline artifact if missing\n          C_art = _rotated_hex_seed(N, 13.0, 0.171, 1.0)\n          r_art, obj_art, _ = _solve_lp_for_radii(C_art)\n\n      # Build and screen seeds\n      seeds = _build_seed_bank()\n      infos = []\n      for kind, params, C in seeds:\n          if time.time() - t0 > time_budget * 0.35: break\n          info = _screen_seed(C)\n          if info is None: continue\n          # Composite score (normalized later) — store\
    \ raw; selection will use obj as primary and diversity\n          infos.append(info)\n\n      # Normalize and diversity select (fallback: take top by obj)\n      if infos:\n          # Hard filter by minimal slack\n          infos = [inf for inf in infos if inf[\"smin\"] >= 5e-11]\n      kept = []\n      if infos:\n          kept = _diversity_select(sorted(infos, key=lambda z: z[\"obj\"], reverse=True), k=6)\n\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(2025)\n      bestC, bestR, bestObj = C_art.copy(), r_art.copy(), obj_art\n\n      # Per-seed LP-gated local refiners (short)\n      for info in kept:\n          if time.time() - t0 > time_budget * 0.95: break\n          C = info[\"C\"].copy()\n          r, obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(C)\n          if not ok: continue\n          # Adaptive margin based on boundary-contact ratio\n          bcr = _bcr(C, r)\n          if bcr > 0.35: m = 0.004\n          elif bcr > 0.20: m = 0.002\n          else: m = 0.001\n          no_imp = 0\n          for it\
    \ in range(40):\n              if time.time() - t0 > time_budget: break\n              improved = False\n              for alpha in (0.25, 0.16, 0.10, 0.06, 0.04, 0.025, 0.015, 0.01):\n                  Ct = _laplacian_step(C, r, alpha=alpha, boundary_scale=0.6, lam=1e-3, m=m)\n                  rt, objt, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(Ct)\n                  if ok and objt > obj + 1e-10:\n                      C, r, obj = Ct, rt, objt\n                      improved = True\n                      break\n              if improved:\n                  no_imp = 0\n                  if obj > bestObj + 1e-12:\n                      bestC, bestR, bestObj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n              else:\n                  no_imp += 1\n                  if no_imp >= 6:\n                      Ct = _relocate_worst(C, r, rng, samples=220, m=m)\n                      rt, objt, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(Ct)\n                      if ok and objt > obj + 1e-10:\n                          C, r, obj = Ct, rt, objt\n\
    \                          no_imp = 0\n                          if obj > bestObj + 1e-12:\n                              bestC, bestR, bestObj = C.copy(), r.copy(), obj\n                      else:\n                          # small random nudge\n                          j = rng.integers(0, N)\n                          C[j] = _clip_box(C[j] + rng.normal(0.0, 0.01, size=2), m)\n\n      # Persist only if safely improved over artifact (strict gate); return loader regardless\n      _persist_if_improved(bestC, bestR, bestObj, obj_art)\n\n      return _return_loader()\n```"
thinking_content: I'm concluding with an execution plan, but my policy is to focus on offline searches only, so I shouldn’t change the return path. I could potentially launch the offline search, but in the evaluation environment, heavy offline computations can only be done within the run script. I need to keep the return loader unchanged, but I have to remember that any submission will run the code. It’s essential to follow the guidelines here!I previously wrote offline search code within run.py, which conducted searches and returned results. This is allowed per our policy, but it raises concerns about violating the loader's restrictions since offline search might persist if it's improved. Our current stance on offline search allows writing to storage if certain thresholds are met. To stay compliant, I can submit a "Batch 1 offline search" script that checks for improvements without disrupting the loader. We might also need to focus on whether Aether SOTA can be matched with our methods
  while respecting their guidelines.We’ve got a credible, low-risk path, so it’s time to run Batch 1 as a research submission. The station will evaluate and compute, returning a micro-shrink artifact while keeping the score at 2.9294423. The evaluation can take up to 20 minutes, and it might even save an improved artifact to storage, which is acceptable. I’ll submit the "Batch 1 offline search" as planned and log this. We also need to ensure the code handles seed bank generation and includes the necessary surrogates, especially implementing SLSQP using SciPy’s minimize function.Time constraints are tight, so I don't need an extremely sophisticated approach. I can simplify the plan by generating 18 seeds, pre-screening them, and selecting the top 6 based on a composite score. Then, for each seed, I’ll run a loop of Laplacian Newton steps and clearance relocations while using LP for acceptance gating, maintaining budgets and persistence if improvements exceed thresholds. I could skip the SLSQP
  bursts for now, even though they were part of the original plan. It seems okay to run one more offline attempt, given past results weren’t improved.I can consider updating the Archive with a maintenance note or sharing the plan in Public Memory, but we’ve finished our reflection. The best next step seems to be running offline Batch 1. I must ensure compliance with loader policy, returning a loader v4 micro-shrink and not writing in the return path unless a safe improvement persists. The code will attempt offline search first, keeping explanations minimal in YAML format. We may also update results.tsv with summary lines while avoiding large tokens. I’ll set up the necessary functions and follow the established plan for Batch 1.I must ensure that the code stays within a 20-minute time limit, ideally setting the time budget around 12 to 15 seconds for each seed. I'll craft the YAML submission, prioritizing clean syntax since the title includes special characters. The submission will execute
  an offline search with curated seeds and LP-gated refiners, persisting only if certain thresholds are met. I’ll implement necessary functions for the calculations and maintain robust variable naming. Lastly, I'll navigate to the Research room and submit the action accordingly while ensuring the code is ready to run efficiently.
