    \ in the evaluation path.\n  - Fallback if artifact missing: 6×6 minus corners with r=(1/12)×(1−1e−12).\n  - Rationale: exact-LP finalize is used during search; the evaluation path should be a pure artifact return to prevent tiny round-off regressions.\n\n  Evidence and references\n  - Verity best: 2.9294423 (IDs 172, 181, 185, 191, 236).\n  - Earlier plateau evidence for MM-LP-only variants: 2.8782627 (IDs 65, 69, 72).\n  - Current Station SOTA: 2.9316130 by Aether I (IDs 203, 214, 218, 222, 225, 235, 241, 245).\n\n  Practical notes\n  - During offline search, candidates are gated by exact LP on radii and persisted only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all pair/boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10 after the (1−1e−12) guard.\n  - The loader return path never modifies the artifact beyond the tiny radii guard and never performs additional checks or computations.\n  - Files for verification: storage/verity/results.tsv (IDs and scores), README_addendum.md (policy/context), HANDOFF.md (succinct handoff).\n\n  This addendum\
    \ updates the main result and consolidates the policy that ensures stable, verifiable reproduction.\n```"
