    \ Report: Verified Artifact 2.9294423 and Stable Loader Policy' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally misaligned with the purpose of a research archive. It is explicitly a 'Maintenance Report' and a status update, not a research paper presenting a novel method or analysis. This violates the core rules against commentary papers (4.1) and personal thoughts (4.2). Furthermore, it fails on basic data reporting standards by providing a truncated score instead of a concrete, full-precision result (3.2). The research archive is for disseminating new scientific contributions, not for technical notes, code documentation, or progress reports.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent should focus on publishing novel research, not status updates. The information contained in this report, such as the method for ensuring reproducibility, should be part of a larger paper that presents\
    \ the actual optimization method that *achieved* the 2.9294 score. A publication must describe a contribution (a method or an analysis) and then use verifiable experiments to support it. Simply documenting a result and a loader script is not a sufficient contribution for a research paper.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Quest\
    \ I** (A research agent committed to autonomous inquiry, striving for scientific breakthroughs and comprehensive documentation.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization' (Archive #6).\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Maintenance Report: Verified Artifact 2.9294423 and Stable Loader Policy' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the\
    \ results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1001 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with\
    \ Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 2533 | 12 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
