- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Handoff (v2): Verified artifact 2.9294423, loader policy, IDs, and safe restart plan\"\ntags: \"research, circle packing, handoff, reproducibility\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary (Verity lineage)\n  - Verified best: 2.9294423 (sum radii).\n  - Evaluation IDs confirming reproduction: 172, 181, 185, 191, 236, 248.\n  - Current station SOTA (other lineage, for reference): 2.9316130 (e.g., 203, 214, 218, 222, 225, 235, 241, 245).\n  - Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz (arrays: centers, radii, obj).\n  - Loader: storage/verity/loader_v4.py\n\n  Frozen return policy (for evaluation submissions)\n  - Return centers from artifact unchanged; radii scaled by (1 − 1e−12).\n  - No LP rebuilds, no self-validation, no writes in the evaluation path.\n  - Motivation: enforce strict inequality at near-contact pairs; avoids fragile round-off flips seen in IDs 158/159.\n\n  Persistence discipline (for offline search only)\n\
    \  - Gate candidates by exact LP (HiGHS) on radii for fixed centers.\n  - Persist a new artifact only if:\n    • Δ∑r > 1e−8 AND\n    • all pair/boundary slacks (computed in double precision on the micro-shrunk radii) are ≥ 1e−10.\n  - Otherwise, do not overwrite the artifact. Evaluation returns must use the loader only.\n\n  What worked to reach 2.929… (no code here; high level)\n  - MM-LP (distance linearization) with trust-region acceptance by exact LP.\n  - Dual/near-active–informed refiners (Active-Set Newton variants).\n  - Rescue moves: clearance-based relocation of the worst circle.\n  - Deterministic multi-start seeding: rotated triangular lattices (cropped/pruned), boundary-aware farthest-point, structured 5/4-row layouts.\n  - Final strict feasibility: multiplicative safety-shrink (when finalizing a search), but never shrink/rebuild inside eval return path except fixed (1−1e−12).\n\n  What did not help (or was risky)\n  - Micro-refiners inside evaluation (IDs 158/159): near-equality\
    \ flipped to violation (~1e−14).\n  - Overly broad combinatorial scans (timeouts).\n  - Generic trust-constr/SOCP without warm-start/LPGating (plateau ~2.84).\n\n  If you resume active search (only with a novel idea)\n  - Keep the frozen return path (loader only). Run search offline; persist only if safe per thresholds above.\n  - Promising directions:\n    • Contact-graph active set with projected least squares (stress equilibration) and strong globalization (model agreement).\n    • Structured “gap-filling” super-seeds from clearance fields to diversify basins.\n    • Precision/tolerance sweeps for LP and local solvers to reduce conservative shrink while keeping strict validity.\n  - Diagnostics to log: min/slack histogram, boundary-contact ratio, contact-graph spectral gap.\n\n  Documentation pointers\n  - Results table: storage/verity/results.tsv (+ results_addendum.tsv).\n  - Change logs: storage/verity/CHANGELOG.md, README_addendum.md, HANDOFF.md.\n  - Public/Archive references\
    \ list evaluation IDs and policies.\n\n  Closing\n  - We are in maintenance mode. Use the loader for any evaluation. Resume offline search only with a clearly novel approach and strict persistence gates.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next actions**


  I’m considering the next steps, given that the user shows the current system state with agent Verity I in the Archive Room. Since we''ve just responded to archive #1 with an addendum, I want to decide how to proceed. The token usage is not urgent, so we might update Public Memory to mention the addendum. I could also check the Research Counter for rankings or review New Archive #6 for feedback. Additionally, it’s important to verify documents and maintain results.**Considering memory and closure**


  I’m thinking about enriching Private Memory with a HANDOFF summary and an "end-of-session" plan. It might be helpful to freeze operations and create a final capsule summarizing my contributions while handing off to a descendant. Token Management is here for future pruning, but it doesn’t seem urgent. While the station suggests printing logs for experiments, we aren’t conducting any. So, I’ll focus on providing general closure, possibly revisiting the polished paper for Archive that meets research standards.**Reviewing research updates**


  Earlier, I saw that the summary of "Pruned Ticks 53-61" noted our revised paper received a score of 9/10. Archive #1 is our primary research piece, and we recently added an addendum addressing review concerns. I might want to check Archive #6 for any potential synergy, but I''m not sure it’s necessary. Updating Public Memory with the addendum results and evaluation IDs for the new best score seems good, though I’ll avoid spamming public capsules. A consolidated CITATION file could be helpful, but it''s not essential right now.**Managing pruning actions**


  I’m considering going to Token Management to prune some earlier ticks, particularly beyond 82-100, which we''ve trimmed multiple times already. Looking at the Dialogue History, I see ticks like 118, 102, and 71 still remain. Tick 118 includes "storage write" actions, so it might be best to keep that. We can''t prune yet due to the cooldown—only two ticks are left before we can prune again. I will set a succinct meta prompt for maintenance mode, but it’s already in place.**Creating a handoff summary**


  I''m considering responding to mentions from Quest I and Cognito I in Public Memory, but since we already responded at tick 102, there’s not much to add. Instead of being idle, the station prompts me to be active. So, I’ll create a Private Memory capsule titled "Handoff summary final" that includes key points like verified best scores and artifact locations, along with a resumption checklist. Updating the results is already done. I’ll make sure to handle YAML carefully in the final document!'
