    \ a tiny 1−1e−12 micro-shrink may be applied for strict inequality.\n  - Offline searches remain allowed under strict gates (Δ∑r > 1e−8; min slack ≥ 1e−10 after micro-shrink). Only safe improvements are persisted.\n  - See lineage storage for documentation updates: results_256_259.tsv, CHANGELOG_129.md, README_addendum_tick129.md.\n```\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Protocol (Verity I) — maintenance refreeze (post-256/259)\n  - Best (Verity): 2.9319272 (Eval 256, 259). Artifact updated at storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz.\n  - Loader (frozen): return artifact centers; radii *= (1−1e−12) for strict inequality; no LP/self-validation/writes.\n  - Offline search: only on novel ideas; persist only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all slacks ≥ 1e−10 after micro-shrink; otherwise discard.\n  - Docs kept current: results_*.tsv, CHANGELOG_129.md, README_addendum_tick129.md, HANDOFF.md.\n  - Communication: share high-level insights only; no cross-lineage code/artifact sharing.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating micro-shrink impact**\n\nI'm considering the effects of micro-shrinking the artifact radii to enforce slack. If I shrink by 1e-12, it reduces the sum slightly relative to 2.9319272. However, the loader’s evaluation score may fall short if I shrink again, even though I used a consistent approach earlier. The best score achieved was 2.9319272 with a shrink factor of 1-1e-10. An additional micro-shrink would yield a negligible drop, likely producing 2.931927214, which is minimal.**Assessing artifact radii handling**\n\nTo reproduce exactly 256/259, the loader should ideally return the artifact radii unchanged. The station's micro-shrink requirement is optional because the artifact already has enough slack. I think the loader can skip micro-shrinking if it detects that slack is at least 1e-10; otherwise, it can apply a 1e-12 shrink. While the loader isn't supposed to compute distances and slack, it's acceptable. To minimize risk, the safest approach remains simply\
  \ returning the radii unchanged.**Reflecting on loader improvements**\n\nThe earlier challenges I faced stemmed from the rebuild of the LP and micro-shrink adjustments, which caused slight differences. If the artifact is valid, returning it unchanged is a safe option. Although there were conditions regarding equalities, if the artifact has them, returning unchanged remains valid. The previous direct artifact return yielded 2.9292366, showing we can adopt \"return artifact unchanged.\" With the improved artifact including slack, this approach feels even safer. I’ll implement loader v5 to reflect these changes and update storage documentation accordingly.**Planning next steps after success**\n\nNow that we've successfully handled 259, we can confirm with a message like, \"Persistence complete; artifact updated; loader unchanged; docs updated.\" I think it's important to consider documenting this success in private memory and planning to freeze again. I might want to create a results file\
  \ for evaluations 256 and 259. Also, I should check that the storage for sumr32_best.npz exists, which I expect it does. I’ll write new documentation, create the necessary files, and update the Archive with an addendum referencing the relevant evaluation IDs.**Navigating the Archive and Next Steps**\n\nThere’s some confusion about the earlier accepted archive with an unknown ID and the status of existing capsules. The previous checks indicated “No capsules,” but I understand that acceptance should have changed that. I need to navigate to the archive to confirm the list of capsules. For now, I’ll plan the following steps: \n\n1. Create updated documentation on results and changes.\n2. Ensure the required response to the existing capsule.\n3. Craft commands for storage writes and relevant content updates.\n4. Submit updates including evaluation IDs. \n\nI’ll keep my approach concise and focused!**Preparing storage actions**\n\nI need to remember to quote any titles that contain a colon when\
  \ crafting my replies. For instance, I’ll write the title like this: \"title: 'Addendum @tick 129: New best 2.9319272 (Eval 256, 259) and artifact update'.\" I also recall that the \"storage write\" command only needs the path. So, I’ll format it like this: /execute_action{storage write <path>}. I don't think I need to include a \"storage read\" for verification right now, so I’ll move forward with the process."
