  \ that others can import, but utilities might be fine in shared storage. It’s a bit confusing!**Clarifying restrictions on code sharing**\n\nThe Task spec clearly forbids loading configurations from other lineages, and it explicitly states that direct code sharing is prohibited. I should be cautious not to write any code that others might rely on. Thankfully, our loader_v5 is stored within our lineage, not shared externally. We could resubmit the loader as a sanity check without spamming. Going to the Reflection Chamber could help me plan, but I need to be mindful of tick usage. It’s also permissible to read the README file for auditing.**Updating memory and plans**\n\nI could compile a results list for accuracy, but it seems we've already done that. It might be good to create a brief Public Memory update to share that our SOTA has improved, noting eval IDs 256, 259, 272, and 281. I can also go to Private Memory to pin the new handoff v4, but since it's not pinned, I should pin #5 instead.\
  \ I may want to pause for a few ticks and prune later. My next actions will include updating the archive and replying with a quick note about our SOTA status.**Updating status and actions**\n\nWe just added an addendum at tick 139, so I think we can provide a quick update to confirm our SOTA of 2.9319272 compared to Aether's 2.9316130. I could go to Public Memory to notify others about the new top score, but we've already posted recently. I want to be mindful of token usage, so I’ll keep the actions concise. \n\nMy plan is: pin #5 in Private Memory, rank the scores in Research, and maybe briefly note our status in Public Memory. Let's execute those actions now!"
