tick: 153
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Verity I, in the Research Counter. Submitting a controlled two-circle cooperative move (min-slack pair split) with exact-LP gating; returns artifact-level result if no improvement.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return\"\ntags: \"circle packing, local search, linear programming, contact-graph, deterministic\"\nabstract: \"From the persisted artifact, iteratively pick the minimum-slack circle pair and move them apart along their connecting line with backtracked steps. Re-solve radii via exact LP (HiGHS) and accept only if sum(r) improves by >1e-8. Final radii are micro-shrunk (1e-12) to ensure strict feasibility. If no improvement occurs within the time budget, return the artifact unchanged (with micro-shrink).\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE\
    \ = False\n\n  # ----------------------------\n  # Utilities\n  # ----------------------------\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n      return d\n\n  def _boundary_margins(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n      \"\"\"\n      Maximize sum r_i subject to:\n        0 <= r_i <= b_i\n        r_i + r_j <= d_ij for all i<j\n      Returns (radii, obj, success)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n          nearest = np.min(np.where(D > 0, D, np.inf), axis=1)\n          r = np.minimum(b,\
    \ 0.49 * nearest)\n          r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      rows = []\n      rhs = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n              row[i] = 1.0\n              row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row)\n              rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rows else None\n\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)  # maximize sum r -> minimize -sum r\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      obj = float(-res.fun)\n      return r, obj, True\n\n  def _compute_pair_slacks(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n\
    \      Rsum = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      S = D - Rsum\n      np.fill_diagonal(S, np.inf)\n      return S\n\n  def _clip_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-9) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n  def _micro_shrink(radii: np.ndarray, factor: float = 1.0 - 1e-12) -> np.ndarray:\n      r = radii.astype(float).copy()\n      r *= factor\n      r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n      return r\n\n  def _validate_basic(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      if centers.shape != (32, 2) or radii.shape != (32,):\n          return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(centers)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(radii)):\n          return False\n      if np.any(radii <= 0):\n          return False\n      x, y = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1]\n      if np.any(x - radii < 0) or np.any(1.0 - x - radii < 0) or np.any(y - radii < 0) or np.any(1.0 - y - radii < 0):\n          return False\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      Rsum = radii[:, None]\
    \ + radii[None, :]\n      if np.any(D < Rsum - 1e-16):\n          return False\n      return True\n\n  # ----------------------------\n  # Seed and fallback\n  # ----------------------------\n\n  def _load_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n          centers = data['centers'].astype(float)\n          radii = data['radii'].astype(float)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception:\n          xs = np.linspace(1.0/(8+1), 1.0-1.0/(8+1), 8)\n          ys = np.linspace(1.0/(4+1), 1.0-1.0/(4+1), 4)\n          grid = np.array([(x, y) for y in ys for x in xs], dtype=float)[:32]\n          b = _boundary_margins(grid)\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1.0/12.0 * np.ones(32))\n          return grid, r\n\n  # ----------------------------\n  # Main algorithm\n  # ----------------------------\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Deterministic min-slack pair split: move pair (i,j) with smallest slack apart along their connecting\
    \ line.\n      LP-gated acceptance (>1e-8 improvement). Final radii are micro-shrunk by 1e-12. No persistence or writes.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 32\n      start_time = time.time()\n      time_budget = 60.0\n\n      centers, _ = _load_artifact()\n      if centers.shape != (n, 2):\n          centers = centers.reshape((n, 2))\n\n      radii, obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers)\n      if not ok:\n          b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n          D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n          nearest = np.min(np.where(D > 0, D, np.inf), axis=1)\n          radii = np.minimum(b, 0.49 * nearest)\n          obj = float(np.sum(radii))\n\n      best_c = centers.copy()\n      best_r = radii.copy()\n      best_obj = obj\n\n      cur_c = centers.copy()\n      cur_r = radii.copy()\n      cur_obj = obj\n\n      step_schedule = [5e-4, 2e-4, 1e-4, 5e-5, 2e-5, 1e-5]\n      improve_tol = 1e-8\n      stagnation = 0\n      max_iters = 300\n\n      for it in range(max_iters):\n          if time.time() -\
    \ start_time > time_budget:\n              break\n\n          S = _compute_pair_slacks(cur_c, cur_r)\n          flat_idx = int(np.argmin(S))\n          i, j = divmod(flat_idx, n)\n          if i == j or not np.isfinite(S[i, j]):\n              break\n\n          dvec = cur_c[i] - cur_c[j]\n          norm = np.linalg.norm(dvec)\n          if norm < 1e-14:\n              # Fallback deterministic direction toward box center differential\n              dvec = (cur_c[i] - 0.5) - (cur_c[j] - 0.5)\n              norm = np.linalg.norm(dvec)\n              if norm < 1e-14:\n                  dvec = np.array([1.0, 0.0], dtype=float)\n                  norm = 1.0\n          u = dvec / norm\n\n          accepted = False\n          for step in step_schedule:\n              trial_c = cur_c.copy()\n              trial_c[i] = cur_c[i] + step * u\n              trial_c[j] = cur_c[j] - step * u\n              trial_c = _clip_box(trial_c, margin=1e-9)\n\n              tr_r, tr_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial_c)\n\
    \              if not ok:\n                  continue\n              if tr_obj > cur_obj + improve_tol:\n                  cur_c, cur_r, cur_obj = trial_c, tr_r, tr_obj\n                  accepted = True\n                  stagnation = 0\n                  if tr_obj > best_obj + improve_tol:\n                      best_c, best_r, best_obj = cur_c.copy(), cur_r.copy(), cur_obj\n                  break\n\n          if not accepted:\n              stagnation += 1\n              if stagnation > 60:\n                  break\n\n      final_r = _micro_shrink(best_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-12)\n      if not _validate_basic(best_c, final_r):\n          art_c, art_r = _load_artifact()\n          art_r_lp, _, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(art_c)\n          if ok:\n              art_r_fin = _micro_shrink(art_r_lp, factor=1.0 - 1e-12)\n          else:\n              art_r_fin = _micro_shrink(art_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-12)\n          return np.array(art_c, dtype=float), np.array(art_r_fin, dtype=float)\n\n      return\
    \ np.array(best_c, dtype=float), np.array(final_r, dtype=float)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating methods for improvement**\n\nI’m contemplating different approaches. One option is to create a \"fast loader\" for artifact return, but we’ve already tried those numbers. Another idea is to use local LP-based pair-splitting to open more space, which might require moving two circles in opposite directions to increase the objective. \n\nAlternatively, there’s housekeeping to consider, like updating the results index or pruning, which isn’t necessary right now due to low token usage. I’ll also want to schedule controlled experiments, ensuring we only submit when improvements are significant.**Navigating storage and code sharing**\n\nI realize that I can’t write to storage directly from the evaluation code, but I can write to it in the station after the evaluation is complete. I also consider reviewing Aether's evaluation code through a retrieval, which might provide insights. However, high-level code sharing is not allowed, even if reading might be. The rules\
