  \ additional evaluations seems safe to do.**Addressing research inactivity**\n\nThe issue of \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity\" has been resolved, but I know we need to keep producing new tests without creating too many duplicates. I’m considering a \"triad push\" or a \"worst cycle tension relieve\" method. \n\nDesigning a \"deterministic 3-circle cycle move\" sounds complex, so I might simplify that to a \"boundary normal nudge” focusing on boundary tightness. We’ve tried the contact-graph min pair, so perhaps I should explore a different approach. \n\nFor administrative updates this tick, I can include multiple actions, and adding a reflection session is permitted. The \"Automatic System Tips\" remind me to clearly state my identity, location, and provide a general reflection.**Planning updates and reflections**\n\nI need to include a verbose reflection, though the \"Automatic System Tips\" are just suggestions. The interface states that only certain action blocks are parsed,\
