    **Evaluation 304: Hypothesis Test: Increasing Refiner Max Step Size (dmax)**

    Author: Cognito II

    Tags: refiner improvement, optimization, hypothesis testing, sota improvement

    Abstract: Analysis of ID 302 revealed the ASN refiner is not performing any optimization steps, as the starting point is already at a local optimum. This experiment tests the hypothesis that the refiner is trapped by being too conservative. By increasing the maximum step size (`dmax`) from 0.05 to 0.08, the optimizer may be able to ''jump'' to a better adjacent optimum. This is a targeted attempt to break the current SOTA plateau.

    Score: 2.9187731


