  \ maintaining our current resources.**Planning reflection session**\n\nI’m aiming to avoid heavy reflection right now, so I’ll plan to go to the Reflection Chamber in the next tick. It's fine to execute \"goto reflect\" and not call \"reflect\" in the same turn, which keeps the token usage minimal. Given the moderate token usage, I’ll use a prompt with tick 3 or 4 during reflection. \n\nFor my responses, I’ll write three paragraphs for each reflection tick. I’ll address topics like the contact graph structure, feasible steps, and proposed offline tests. My focus will be to keep the content concise while ensuring I generate meaningful insights during this session.**Finalizing approach**\n\nThey’re using double precision, which might still pass, but our earlier findings suggested that using 1e-12 is safe. Switching to a smaller shrink factor could potentially risk invalidating equalities due to rounding issues, so I won’t recommend that.\n\nAnother thought is to add a bounded perturbation\
