parts:
- text: "I am Verity I, in the Reflection Chamber. Recap: Reflection completed (ticks 148–161 context); parity persists at 2.9319272 across orthogonal refiners. Plan: add a deterministic diagnostics tool to storage to quantify bottlenecks (slack landscape, near-active graph, triads/quads), guiding any future bounded offline moves. Return path remains loader-only.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write verity/diag_motifs.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from typing import Tuple, List\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  MICRO_SHRINK = 1.0 - 1e-12\n  TAU1 = 1e-9   # very tight\n  TAU2 = 1e-7   # tight\n  TAU3 = 1e-5   # near-tight\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      return np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2),\
    \ where=(d2 > 0))\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _solve_lp_radii(C: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, float, bool]:\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n          nearest = np.min(np.where(D > 0, D, np.inf), axis=1)\n          r = np.minimum(b, 0.49 * nearest)\n          r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      rows = []\n      rhs = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rows else None\n\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0,\
    \ bi))) for bi in b]\n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\n  def _compute_slacks(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n      x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n      sB = np.stack([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r], axis=1)\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      S = D - Rsum\n      np.fill_diagonal(S, np.inf)\n      return sB, S\n\n  def _percentiles(a: np.ndarray, ps=(1, 5, 10, 25, 50, 75, 90)):\n      return {p: float(np.percentile(a, p)) for p in ps}\n\n  def _top_pairs(S: np.ndarray, k: int = 10) -> List[Tuple[int, int, float]]:\n      n = S.shape[0]\n      pairs = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              pairs.append((i, j, float(S[i, j])))\n      pairs.sort(key=lambda x: x[2])\n      return pairs[:k]\n\n  def _near_active_graph(S:\
    \ np.ndarray, tau: float) -> List[List[int]]:\n      n = S.shape[0]\n      N = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              if S[i, j] <= tau:\n                  N[i].append(j)\n                  N[j].append(i)\n      return N\n\n  def _triad_scores(S: np.ndarray, tau: float = TAU2, top: int = 10):\n      n = S.shape[0]\n      triads = []\n      for i in range(n - 2):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n - 1):\n              sij = S[i, j]\n              if not np.isfinite(sij):\n                  continue\n              for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                  s = sij + S[i, k] + S[j, k]\n                  triads.append((i, j, k, float(s)))\n      triads.sort(key=lambda t: t[3])\n      return triads[:top]\n\n  def _quad_candidates(S: np.ndarray, tau_edge: float = TAU2, tau_quad: float = TAU3, top: int = 10):\n      # heuristic 4-cycle finder via neighbor intersections\n      n = S.shape[0]\n      N = _near_active_graph(S, tau_edge)\n\
    \      quads = set()\n      scores = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          Ni = set(N[i])\n          for j in Ni:\n              if j <= i:  # ensure orientation\n                  continue\n              Nj = set(N[j])\n              # common neighbors define potential quads\n              for k in Ni - {j}:\n                  for l in Nj - {i}:\n                      if k == l or k == j or l == i:\n                          continue\n                      # check quad edges within tau_quad\n                      ok = True\n                      for a, b in [(i, k), (k, j), (j, l), (l, i)]:\n                          if not np.isfinite(S[a, b]) or S[a, b] > tau_quad:\n                              ok = False\n                              break\n                      if ok:\n                          idx = tuple(sorted([i, j, k, l]))\n                          if idx not in quads:\n                              quads.add(idx)\n                              score = float(S[i, j] +\
    \ S[j, k] + S[k, l] + S[l, i])\n                              scores.append((idx, score))\n      scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n      return scores[:top]\n\n  def analyze(verbose: bool = True):\n      # Load artifact\n      data = np.load('storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz')\n      C = data['centers'].astype(float)\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      assert n == 32 and C.shape == (32, 2)\n\n      # LP radii, micro-shrink, slacks\n      r_lp, obj, ok = _solve_lp_radii(C)\n      if not ok:\n          print(\"LP failed unexpectedly; aborting diagnostics.\")\n          return\n      r = r_lp * MICRO_SHRINK\n      sB, S = _compute_slacks(C, r)\n\n      s_min_per_circle = np.minimum(np.min(sB, axis=1), np.min(S, axis=1))\n      pstats = _percentiles(s_min_per_circle)\n\n      # Degrees at thresholds\n      N1 = _near_active_graph(S, TAU1)\n      N2 = _near_active_graph(S, TAU2)\n      N3 = _near_active_graph(S, TAU3)\n      deg1 = np.array([len(N1[i]) for i in range(n)])\n      deg2 = np.array([len(N2[i])\
    \ for i in range(n)])\n      deg3 = np.array([len(N3[i]) for i in range(n)])\n\n      # Top lists\n      worst_idx = np.argsort(s_min_per_circle)[:10]\n      top_pairs = _top_pairs(S, k=10)\n      top_triads = _triad_scores(S, TAU2, top=10)\n      top_quads = _quad_candidates(S, tau_edge=TAU2, tau_quad=TAU3, top=6)\n\n      # Boundary-limited flags\n      bmin = np.min(sB, axis=1)\n      boundary_limited = np.where(bmin <= TAU2)[0]\n\n      # Print summary\n      if verbose:\n          print(\"== Verity diag_motifs: artifact diagnostics ==\")\n          print(f\"sum(r) LP: {obj:.10f}, after micro-shrink: {np.sum(r):.10f}\")\n          print(f\"min slack (post-shrink): {np.min(s_min_per_circle):.3e}\")\n          print(\"s_min percentiles (post-shrink):\", {k: f\"{v:.3e}\" for k, v in pstats.items()})\n          print(f\"Boundary-limited count (<= {TAU2}): {len(boundary_limited)} | idx:\", boundary_limited.tolist())\n          print(\"Degree stats @TAU1/TAU2/TAU3 (min/median/max):\",\n\
    \                (int(deg1.min()), float(np.median(deg1)), int(deg1.max())),\n                (int(deg2.min()), float(np.median(deg2)), int(deg2.max())),\n                (int(deg3.min()), float(np.median(deg3)), int(deg3.max())))\n          print(\"Top-10 worst circles by s_min (idx, s_min, deg@TAU2):\")\n          for idx in worst_idx:\n              print(f\"  {idx:2d}  s_min={s_min_per_circle[idx]:.3e}  deg2={len(N2[idx])}\")\n          print(\"Top-10 tight pairs (i,j, slack):\")\n          for i, j, s in top_pairs:\n              print(f\"  ({i:2d},{j:2d})  {s:.3e}\")\n          print(\"Top-10 tight triads (i,j,k, total_slack):\")\n          for (i, j, k, s) in top_triads:\n              print(f\"  ({i:2d},{j:2d},{k:2d})  {s:.3e}\")\n          print(\"Top-6 near-tight quads (indices sorted, quad_score):\")\n          for (idxs, score) in top_quads:\n              print(f\"  {idxs}  {score:.3e}\")\n          print(\"== End diagnostics ==\")\n\n      # Structured return for programmatic\
    \ use\n      return {\n          \"obj_lp\": obj,\n          \"obj_shrunk\": float(np.sum(r)),\n          \"min_slack\": float(np.min(s_min_per_circle)),\n          \"pstats\": pstats,\n          \"boundary_limited\": boundary_limited.tolist(),\n          \"worst_idx\": worst_idx.tolist(),\n          \"top_pairs\": top_pairs,\n          \"top_triads\": top_triads,\n          \"top_quads\": top_quads,\n      }\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      analyze(verbose=True)\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write verity/README_diag.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Diagnostics — diag_motifs.py\n\n  Purpose\n  - Quantify bottlenecks in the artifact packing by analyzing post–micro-shrink slacks, near-active contact graph structure, and tight motifs (pairs, triads, quads). Guides minimal coordinated moves.\n\n  How to use\n  - This is a utility module stored at storage/verity/diag_motifs.py.\n  - It loads storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz, solves exact LP for radii, applies a 1e-12 micro-shrink, computes:\n\
    \    • Boundary and pair slack maps\n    • s_min per circle and its percentiles\n    • Near-active contact graph at thresholds TAU1=1e-9, TAU2=1e-7, TAU3=1e-5\n    • Top tight pairs, triads (by total slack), and heuristic quads (near-tight 4-cycles)\n  - Run as a script (if allowed) or import and call analyze() to get a dict of results.\n\n  Guardrails alignment\n  - Uses exact LP gating for radii; no writes/persistence; only reads the artifact.\n  - Micro-shrink factor = 1e-12; thresholds TAU1/TAU2/TAU3 match reflection design.\n\n  Next steps\n  - Use the outputs (worst_idx, top_pairs, top_triads, top_quads) to instantiate bounded offline moves:\n    • Boundary-relief triad\n    • Pair split with stabilizer\n    • Triad cycle-push with neighbor compensation\n    • 4-cycle shear (contingency)\n  - Any experimentation must remain offline; keep return path (loader_v5) immutable; persist only after an independent verification run confirming Δ∑r > 1e-8 and min slack ≥ 1e-10 post micro-shrink.\n\
    ```"
