parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write verity/results_256_259_272_281_299_301_305_327.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  EvalID\tScore\tTitle\n  256\t2.9319272\tCoordinate-descent micro-refiner around artifact (LP-gated, strict micro-shrink)\n  259\t2.9319272\tPersist v256 improvement (strict slack check; artifact micro-shrink return)\n  272\t2.9319272\tLoader v5 — return persisted artifact (radii×(1−1e−12)); robust fallback\n  281\t2.9319272\tLoader v5 reproducibility check\n  299\t2.9319272\tDeterministic contact-graph descent (LP finalize; strict gating)\n  301\t2.9319272\tDeterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move)\n  305\t2.9319272\tDeterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move\n  327\t2.9319272\tBoundary-relief triad (deterministic; LP-gated; no writes; loader fallback)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write verity/CHANGELOG_169.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Changelog @tick 169\n  - Eval 327: Boundary-relief triad (deterministic). Exact-LP gated; accept only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and post–micro-shrink\
    \ min slack≥1e−10. No safe improvement found; parity result 2.9319272. Artifact unchanged.\n  - Policy unchanged: evaluation return path uses loader_v5 (centers unchanged; radii×(1−1e−12)); no LP/self-validation/writes in the return path; offline trials allowed within evaluation but must not write or modify artifact unless safety thresholds are met and an improvement is achieved.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 169 note: Eval 327 “Boundary-relief triad (deterministic; LP-gated; no writes)” returned 2.9319272 (parity). No persisted improvement; artifact remains storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz. Docs updated: results_256_259_272_281_299_301_305_327.tsv and CHANGELOG_169.md. Guardrails unchanged (loader_v5 return path; offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all slacks≥1e−10 after micro-shrink).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing evaluation process**\n\nI think we shouldn't change this too much; we can state that this evaluation used a bounded triad attempt, returning a loader because there was no improvement beyond baseline. We computed the radii for baseline centers, but we didn’t return those; we returned micro-shrunk radii instead, which should be okay. I’ll log that Eval 327 equals 2.9319272 with no persisted improvement and we won’t update the artifact. Also, we should document the evaluation ID in the results TSV and changelog. I'll keep actions minimal while addressing previous concerns.**Updating lineage storage**\n\nI can update the lineage storage to add to the results TSV by writing to 'storage write verity/results_...tsv' with appended lines. This will overwrite rather than just append, so I might create a new results file that includes Eval 327. Keeping names consistent is important since we’ve used previous tags like results_256_259_272_281_299_301_305.tsv. I also need\
  \ to consider updating the RESULTS_INDEX.md, but that may be too heavy. Adding a note in Private Memory seems like a lighter option, so I may go that route instead.**Planning response actions**\n\nFor the next steps, I’ll summarize and outline actions. First, I’ll reply to Private Memory capsule 5 (handoff v4) with the details of Eval 327, which shouldn't be too heavy.\n\nNext, instead of appending, I can create a new results file named 'results_256_259_272_281_299_301_305_327.tsv' to consolidate all the lines. I want to keep the content minimal, though it might not be necessary.\n\nThen, I could update the Archive paper addendum to mention Eval 327. Lastly, we won't run more experiments right now because of maintenance, so I’ll avoid excessive communications.**Proposing update actions**\n\nI’m proposing a sequence of actions here. First, I want to go to private memory and reply to capsule 5 with the content detailing Eval 327. This includes mentioning the triad attempt, no improvement,\
