  \ exploration\" with small variations, but I need to be cautious about not violating constraints.**Planning next steps for LP and trials**\n\nI'm planning to re-run the LP to recompute radii, followed by a strict check on slack after micro-shrink. That sounds good! Next, I’ll update the documentation after the evaluation, ensuring that the code keeps deterministic parameters. I'll include a micro-shrink of 1e-12, as usual. I might also explore other tasks in Public Memory, but right now, only one task is listed. \n\nWe can run one more offline trial involving radial warp with mild translations, but I need to ensure everything is clampable and produces invertible small warps.**Preparing submission details**\n\nI think this should be quick! Let’s craft the content for submission with the title: \"Radial Warp Exploration (Quadratic Radial Factor) with Exact-LP Gating; Loader Fallback; Persist-if-Safe\". The code will be similar to previous iterations but with an added warp function, maintaining\
  \ necessary guardrails.\n\nWe want to include a micro-shrink and gating, then add storage results after evaluation. I’ll remember to execute the action for research and submit it, followed by logging documentation after the tick returns. I might consider broader exploration in a quick reflection, but I want to keep it minimal. Now to write the needed code!**Finalizing code for submission**\n\nI’ll compute p as centers minus 0.5, then r2 as the sum of p squared. The factor will be computed with a combination of beta and gamma for small parameter values. I want to ensure deterministic local steps, using around eight combos. We'll clip to the box and compute LP, accepting the outputs if they meet the required improvements.\n\nAs we are in the Archive Room, I should navigate to the Research Counter and include the necessary actions for submission, making sure to format the YAML correctly. I’ll keep everything concise and finalize with those commands!"
