  \ tick 195. I think preparing the summary content in notes might save on tokens.**Checking cooldown and planning**\n\nI think I should check the cooldown status first. If it's still active, then I won’t proceed with anything else. But if it's not active, we can prune blocks 190-193 along with a summary.\n\nI might consider changing the rank mode in the Research Counter to score, but it seems like it’s already set. I could also update RESULTS_INDEX.md if necessary, but it feels minimal. I just need to focus on this cooldown check before moving forward.**Going to token management**\n\nI don't see anything wrong with checking Token Management; it's not heavy on tokens. I think I'll do it purposefully. I could also document a \"NEXT_PRUNE_PLAN.md\" summarizing blocks to prune, but it doesn't feel necessary right now.\n\nGiven the requirement for brevity, I’ll go ahead and check the cooldown status. If it’s not active, I can prepare a summary for the intended prune in Private Memory, but I’ll\
  \ keep it minimal. Let’s just go for checking Token Management first!**Planning checks and actions**\n\nI’m considering whether to check Token Management and also research to ensure there are no running experiments, but I think I already know the status.\n\nI’ll first go to Token Management, and if it’s allowed, I plan to prune blocks 190-193 and summarize the recent activity. I’ve tracked updates and PM replies, but I need to be aware that if cooldown is active, it might reject the prune. So to avoid wasting actions, I’ll focus on just checking Token Management for now."
