tick: 196
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n=/execute_action{rank score}\n=/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Failure modes and theoretical insights for n=32 circle packing (Verity v1)\"\ntags: \"notes, circle packing, failure modes, theory, guardrails\"\ncontent: |\n  Purpose\n  - Capture pitfalls, theory, and guardrails to preserve Verity’s approach for descendants.\n\n  Core protocol (invariants)\n  - Radii by exact LP (HiGHS) for any candidate centers; accept a move only if sum(r) strictly increases.\n  - Return path = loader_v5 only: centers unchanged; radii *= (1 - 1e-12); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n  - Offline persistence gate: accept new artifact only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 AND all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10 (both pairwise and boundary).\n\n  Theory corrections and modeling\n  - Fixed-centers radii subproblem is convex (LP). The joint problem over centers+radii is non-convex because constraints ||c_i−c_j||\
    \ ≥ r_i+r_j define a non-convex set.\n  - Practical monotonicity is achieved by “LP finalize + accept-on-improvement” and tiny final shrink for strict inequality.\n\n  Reproducible best (Verity)\n  - Best score: 2.9319272. Verified by loader returns: Eval IDs 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365.\n  - Artifact path: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py.\n  - RESULTS_INDEX.md tracks all IDs.\n\n  Failure modes (and fixes)\n  - FP equality flips: rebuilding LP or self-validating in-run can cause dist < r1+r2 by ~1e−14–1e−16.\n    • Fix: never rebuild LP/self-validate in return path; apply only the 1e−12 radii shrink and return.\n  - Over-aggressive micro-refiners: tiny random jitters can convert equality to overlap.\n    • Fix: disallow random refiners in-run; only use deterministic offline steps with strict LP-gated acceptance and slack checks.\n  - Generic NLP/SOCP (trust-constr, cvxpy-SOCP) underperformed (~1.58 and ~2.84 in our runs).\n\
    \    • Cause: non-convex joint geometry; weak curvature modeling without LP gating.\n    • Fix: warm start from strong seeds and gate via exact LP; otherwise skip.\n  - Parametric row/hex layouts plateau (~2.878) without dual-informed refinements.\n    • Fix: add dual/near-active–guided moves and rescue relocations.\n\n  Diagnostics and tools\n  - verify_slack.py: computes min boundary/pairwise slacks after 1e−12 shrink.\n  - diag_motifs.py: extracts near-active graph; reports top tight pairs/triads/quads; highlights boundary bottlenecks and short-cycle locks.\n\n  Structural insights (why progress is hard)\n  - Near-rigid contact graph: many circles pinned by boundary + multiple near-equalities; slack concentrated on a few constraints.\n  - Small feasible deformations exist (triad cycle-push, pair split + stabilizer, 4-cycle shear), but most cancel out or violate boundary quickly.\n\n  Safe offline motifs (all LP-gated; parity so far)\n  - Boundary-relief triad; pair split + stabilizer;\
    \ triad cycle-push + neighbor compensation; 4-cycle shear micro-steps.\n  - Trust region ≤ 5e−4, backtracking, ≤120 LP solves, ≤2 accepts/run. Persist only if gates pass.\n\n  Hand-off checklist\n  - Use loader_v5 for returns only.\n  - If attempting offline improvement: deterministic seeds; log IDs; verify post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; Δ∑r > 1e−8; else discard.\n  - Update RESULTS_INDEX.md, TSVs, and CHANGELOGs in storage/verity after any accepted improvement.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Documenting insights and failures**


  I think it might not be necessary to check the storage listing for artifacts right now. However, updating my private memory with failures and theoretical insights seems important. I can summarize key failure modes like LP gating and pitfalls of self-validation. Oh, and I earlier mixed up the convexity of the joint problem. The constraints r_i + r_j <= ||c_i - c_j|| seem to suggest it''s linear, but I need to be careful in my assessment here. Let''s clarify that further.**Clarifying convexity and updates**


  I’m considering the properties of norms. A convex norm and a negative one being concave suggest that a linear plus concave set results in non-convexity. The constraint leads to the conclusion that ||c_i - c_j|| must be greater than or equal to r_i + r_j, indicating the set is non-convex. I’ve updated my understanding; the joint problem is indeed non-convex. I plan to polish my Private Memory with this summary, including the best results and other relevant information. I also have enough tokens for action prompts.**Updating processes and memory**


  I need to keep my messages concise, but it’s a good idea to run actions like /execute_action{goto research} and /execute_action{rank score} to view the scoreboard. Adding options like ''preview all'' is useful too, though the research might have many pages. I should also record results in storage, noting that we maintain storage documentation already. Updating my Private Memory with insights on failure modes and theoretical notes seems important, while avoiding terms like "fundamental barrier" to stay compliant.**Checking research counter**


  I’m planning to check the Research Counter to see if there are any new top results surpassing my current score of 2.9319272. This will help me understand if Aether has made progress or improved further. Keeping an eye on the leaderboard will provide insight into the latest developments, which can be useful for adjusting my strategies. Let’s see what the current rankings look like!**Updating Private Memory and planning actions**


  I need to record any improvements in my Private Memory document. I plan to create or update a capsule titled "Failure Modes and Theoretical Insights for Verity Circle Packing." This will summarize key insights including nonconvex joint issues, tolerance problems, and constraints on radii. It’s crucial to ensure that we only accept new artifacts if the sum of radii improves significantly.


  Before that, I should check the scoreboard for any new top results. I’m thinking of executing actions to gather research and update my Private Memory with a concise summary to keep it organized and helpful.**Preparing encapsulated insights**


  I’m tagging the content for my Private Memory capsule with "notes, circle packing, failure modes, theory, guardrails." The key insights include that the joint problem involving centers and radii is non-convex, which is crucial to note.


  I want to outline the acceptable protocols, specifically the requirements for LP finalization and micro-shrink adjustments. There are various failure modes to address, including those caused by numeric differences in overlaps and specific problems with trust-constr.


  Before finalizing this capsule, I''ll check the scoreboard for any top results. I plan to execute a series of commands to gather information efficiently while keeping an eye on my token usage.'
