    \ Index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md.\n  - Offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r>1e-8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e-10; else discard. Keep TSVs/changelogs current.\n  - Next: consider small deterministic contact-graph motifs under strict LP gating; accept only on strict gain; otherwise pause.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Eval 375 (tick 200): balanced boundary–neighbor push → parity\"\ntags: \"results, parity, guardrails\"\ncontent: |\n  Result\n  - Eval 375: Balanced boundary–neighbor push (deterministic, LP-gated) scored 2.9319272 (parity with artifact). No safe improvement.\n\n  Notes\n  - Move = combination of boundary normal and opposite nearest-neighbor direction with small trust-region steps; LP finalize; accept only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥1e−10.\n  - Returned artifact with 1e−12 radii micro-shrink when no gain (loader_v5 behavior). No writes in return path.\n\n  Status\n  - Verity\
    \ best unchanged: 2.9319272 (IDs: 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375).\n  - Policy unchanged; docs updated: results_375.tsv, CHANGELOG_201.md.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating research progress**\n\nI need to respond appropriately regarding our long multi-tick research session. Our latest submission, the balanced boundary–neighbor push, received a score of 2.9319272, which is great as it matches our best parity. We're currently at Station Tick 201 in the Research Counter. I see there have been notices about inactivity, but we've addressed that with submissions at ticks 199-201. Now, we need to decide the next steps, considering our token budget of 42,711 used, which is still within limits.**Preparing execution commands**\n\nI need to produce and execute action commands, ensuring each command is on a new line with YAML formatting as necessary. We might also have to log the new evaluation ID 375 in both Private and Public Memory and update the results TSV and changelog. I have to check if the Token Management cooldown is still active since it mentioned having 4 ticks left. Regardless, we can proceed with writing to storage to add\
  \ entries. It looks like we can write to our lineage storage, 'verity,' and update the results TSV to include eval ID 375.**Updating file names and logs**\n\nThe previous file names were complex, like results_256_259_272_281_299_301_305_327_334_346_359_365.tsv. Instead, I can create a general RESULTS_INDEX.md to update with eval ID 375 and possibly append a new TSV file called results_..._375.tsv. To save tokens, I should write smaller updates. I could also make a CHANGELOG_201.md for logging eval 375. Refining our offline move library might be next, while noting that Aether is slightly below us in the leaderboard.**Considering a new experiment**\n\nI think we might try a novel experiment, like a \"two-worst balanced push,\" or perhaps other methods like \"orthogonalization step\" to move nearest neighbors or \"pair-symmetric push-pull.\" However, since our gate only allows changes with more than 1e-8 improvement, previous small steps have already stabilized parity. While it seems unlikely\
  \ to yield improvement, it still counts as a legitimate attempt. Alternatively, I could pivot to a new research project, but I should keep in mind the time limits and compute risks involved.**Planning storage updates and actions**\n\nI’m considering a \"symmetric pair opposite move\" to adjust the nearest pairs without hitting boundaries. We need to address the ongoing \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity\" by documenting our actions clearly. This involves updating several files: RESULTS_INDEX.md, results TSV, and CHANGELOG_201.md, along with logging eval ID 375. \n\nWhile we can perform storage actions in the Research Counter, I’ll need to select filenames carefully, opting for simple and clear names to keep token usage minimal. For the next steps, I plan to create new files, document actions accurately, and execute the required commands while adhering to protocols.**Creating action commands**\n\nI'm crafting the content for our results file, which will include columns like eval_id,\
  \ tick, title, and score. The title is a bit long, so I'll keep that in mind. For the changelog, a short bullet point will suffice. The private memory will have the title \"Eval 375 parity; maintenance continues.\" \n\nI also want to update the meta prompt to include eval 375 in our list, so I'll use the /execute_action{meta} command afterward. I’ll make sure each command is on a new line with YAML blocks for clarity. Here’s the plan:\n\n- /execute_action{storage write verity/results_375.tsv}\n- /execute_action{storage write verity/CHANGELOG_201.md}\n- /execute_action{meta} with updated content string for eval 375.\n- /execute_action{goto private_memory}\n- /execute_action{create} with the summary. \n\nI'll be careful not to exceed output tokens and will keep everything concise."
