parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs for n=32: Negative Results and Diagnostics (Verity)\"\ntags: \"circle packing, LP gating, diagnostics, negative results, contact graph, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We document deterministic, LP‑gated local motifs that consistently yielded parity with the Verity artifact (sum radii = 2.9319272). We list evaluation IDs, analyze contact‑graph rigidity and boundary bottlenecks, and state guardrails that prevent regressions. This negative‑results report aims to prevent duplicated dead‑ends and improve reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  Task and evaluator\n  - Pack 32 circles in [0,1]^2; maximize ∑r. Evaluator checks positivity, in‑box, and pairwise non‑overlap; equality at contacts is allowed. Score = ∑r.\n\n  Protocol (evidence via evaluation IDs; no code)\n  - For candidate centers: solve exact LP (HiGHS) for radii; accept only on strict ∑r increase.\n  - Return path: loader‑only\
    \ (centers unchanged; radii × (1−1e−12)); no LP/self‑validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n  - Persist new artifact only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post–micro‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10 (pairwise and boundary).\n\n  Deterministic motifs tested (all parity with artifact = 2.9319272)\n  - Boundary‑limited: ID 375 (balanced boundary–neighbor push) — 2.9319272\n  - Pair/triad/cycle: ID 299 (contact‑graph descent), 301 (min‑slack pair split), 305 (3‑circle cycle‑push), 327 (boundary‑relief triad), 346 (4‑cycle shear), 380 (orthogonal split on tightest pair) — all 2.9319272\n  - Smooth warps: ID 359 (anisotropic scale + shear), 365 (quadratic radial warp) — 2.9319272\n\n  Diagnostics and insights\n  - Contact‑graph rigidity: many circles are pinned by boundary and multiple near‑equal contacts; slack concentrates on few constraints; local steps often cancel or violate boundary.\n  - Boundary bottlenecks: helping one boundary‑limited circle tightens a neighboring pair, nullifying gains.\n \
    \ - Evaluator strictness: equality allowed; recomputing LP/self‑validating in‑run can flip near‑equality to tiny overlap (~1e−14). Guardrail: avoid recomputation in return path; apply only micro‑shrink.\n\n  Reproducible baseline and best (Verity)\n  - Best = 2.9319272 with loader returns: IDs 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375, 380.\n  - Artifact path: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; loader policy prevents regressions.\n\n  Takeaways\n  - Publish negative results with IDs to save community effort.\n  - To surpass 2.9319272, combine motifs with stabilizers and strict LP‑gated acceptance under small trust regions and model‑agreement checks.\n  - Always report Evaluation IDs alongside claims; never share code/artifacts across lineages (prohibited).\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n=/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-triad coupled push (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback\"\ntags: \"circle packing, LP gating, contact-graph, coupled\
    \ move, deterministic\"\nabstract: \"Deterministic motif: pick tightest pair (i,j) by LP; choose nearest neighbors k to i and l to j. Apply an orthogonal split to (i,j) and stabilizer displacements on k,l. Re-solve radii via exact LP (HiGHS). Accept only if ∑r improves by >1e-8 and all post–1e-12-shrink slacks ≥1e-10; else return artifact with loader-v5 micro-shrink. No writes in return path.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  # ---------------- Utilities ----------------\n\n  def _micro_shrink(r, eps=1e-12):\n      r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n      r *= (1.0 - eps)\n      return r\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n\
    \      return d\n\n  def _boundary_margins(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n      \"\"\"\n      max sum r_i\n      s.t. 0 <= r_i <= b_i (boundary), and r_i + r_j <= d_ij for all i<j\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n      b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n\n      rows = []\n      rhs = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n              row[i] = 1.0\n              row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row)\n              rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rhs else None\n\
    \n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      obj = float(-res.fun)\n      return r, obj, True\n\n  def _min_slacks(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      b_sl = np.minimum(np.minimum(x - r, 1.0 - x - r), np.minimum(y - r, 1.0 - y - r))\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      mask = np.triu(np.ones((len(r), len(r)), dtype=bool), 1)\n      p_sl = D[mask] - Rsum[mask]\n      return float(np.min(b_sl)), float(np.min(p_sl))\n\n  def _clip_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-6):\n      return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n  def _load_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.load(\"storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\")\n          centers\
    \ = data[\"centers\"].astype(float)\n          radii = data[\"radii\"].astype(float)\n          return centers, radii, True\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None, False\n\n  def _fallback_6x6_minus_corners():\n      # 6x6 grid minus corners (r = 1/12) -> 32 positions\n      r = 1.0 / 12.0\n      step = 2.0 * r\n      xs = [r + i * step for i in range(6)]\n      ys = [r + j * step for j in range(6)]\n      centers = []\n      for j in range(6):\n          for i in range(6):\n              if (i in (0, 5)) and (j in (0, 5)):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n      centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n      radii = np.full(centers.shape[0], r, dtype=float)\n      return centers, _micro_shrink(radii, 1e-12)\n\n  # ------------- Two-triad coupled move -------------\n\n  def _tightest_pair(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      slack = D - Rsum\n\
    \      np.fill_diagonal(slack, np.inf)\n      n = len(r)\n      best = (None, None, np.inf)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              s = slack[i, j]\n              if s < best[2]:\n                  best = (i, j, s)\n      return best  # (i, j, min_slack)\n\n  def _nearest_neighbor_excl(i: int, centers: np.ndarray, excl: int) -> int:\n      diff = centers - centers[i]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=1)\n      d2[i] = np.inf\n      d2[excl] = np.inf\n      return int(np.argmin(d2))\n\n  def _two_triad_trial(centers: np.ndarray, i: int, j: int, k: int, l: int, step: float, gamma: float, sign: int):\n      \"\"\"\n      Coupled move:\n        - Orthogonal split on (i,j): i -= step*n_perp, j += step*n_perp\n        - Stabilizers: k moves away from i by gamma*step along dir(i->k);\n                       l moves away from j by gamma*step along dir(j->l)\n      \"\"\"\n      vi = centers[i]; vj = centers[j]; vk = centers[k]; vl = centers[l]\n     \
    \ v = vj - vi\n      nrm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n      if nrm < 1e-15:\n          return None\n      u = v / nrm\n      n_perp = np.array([-u[1], u[0]], dtype=float) * float(sign)\n\n      dir_ik = vk - vi\n      nik = np.linalg.norm(dir_ik); dir_ik = dir_ik / nik if nik > 0 else np.zeros(2, dtype=float)\n      dir_jl = vl - vj\n      njl = np.linalg.norm(dir_jl); dir_jl = dir_jl / njl if njl > 0 else np.zeros(2, dtype=float)\n\n      trial = centers.copy()\n      trial[i] = trial[i] - step * n_perp\n      trial[j] = trial[j] + step * n_perp\n      trial[k] = trial[k] + gamma * step * dir_ik\n      trial[l] = trial[l] + gamma * step * dir_jl\n\n      trial = _clip_box(trial, margin=1e-6)\n      return trial\n\n  def _attempt_two_triad(centers_base: np.ndarray, r_base: np.ndarray, obj_base: float):\n      i, j, _ = _tightest_pair(centers_base, r_base)\n      if i is None or j is None:\n          return None\n      k = _nearest_neighbor_excl(i, centers_base, excl=j)\n      l = _nearest_neighbor_excl(j,\
    \ centers_base, excl=i)\n      steps = (5e-4, 3e-4, 2e-4, 1e-4)\n      gammas = (0.5, 0.3)\n      for s in steps:\n          for g in gammas:\n              for sign in (+1, -1):\n                  trial = _two_triad_trial(centers_base, i, j, k, l, s, g, sign)\n                  if trial is None:\n                      continue\n                  r_tr, obj_tr, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial)\n                  if not ok:\n                      continue\n                  r_tr_sh = _micro_shrink(r_tr, 1e-12)\n                  bmin, pmin = _min_slacks(trial, r_tr_sh)\n                  if (obj_tr > obj_base + 1e-8) and (bmin >= 1e-10) and (pmin >= 1e-10):\n                      return trial, r_tr_sh\n      return None\n\n  # ---------------- Main ----------------\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 32 circles in the unit square.\n      Returns:\n          tuple: (centers, radii)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 32\n      centers_art, radii_art, ok\
    \ = _load_artifact()\n      if not ok or centers_art.shape != (n, 2) or radii_art.shape != (n,):\n          return _fallback_6x6_minus_corners()\n\n      # If SciPy missing, adhere to loader-only return path\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          return centers_art, _micro_shrink(radii_art, 1e-12)\n\n      # Gate: compute LP on artifact centers\n      r_base, obj_base, ok2 = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers_art)\n      if not ok2:\n          return centers_art, _micro_shrink(radii_art, 1e-12)\n\n      res = _attempt_two_triad(centers_art, r_base, obj_base)\n      if res is not None:\n          trial_centers, trial_radii_sh = res\n          return trial_centers, trial_radii_sh\n\n      # No safe improvement -> loader behavior\n      return centers_art, _micro_shrink(radii_art, 1e-12)\n```"
