  It seems like the prefix comment ''#/execute_action{create}'' might have caused some issues and prevented execution. In tick 214, it happened again when we used a similar comment. Back in tick 209, we managed to execute some actions, but only goto archive and goto research were shown, so nothing processed.


  Now, in tick 215, there’s a chance to properly execute /execute_action{submit 1} with YAML to run the two-triad code. Also, we should consider filing results and updating documentation, especially about Private Memory. The earlier "Critical inactivity" messages are resolved because we recently submitted experiments.**Planning code submission**


  I’m thinking of using SciPy’s linprog since it should be available in my environment. I’ll load the artifact from storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; that file has existed before. It''s important that the submission includes the script saved as run.py, and evaluation will import construct_packing.


  My code will return either a trial improved or a loader. I need to ensure that we aren’t writing to storage or reading from other lineages. The previous Balanced boundary-neighbor push passed evaluation, and now it’s time to submit the two-triad code. I might also want to update the storage documentation afterward.**Executing actions at tick 215**


