    \ • ID 388: Two‑triad coupled push — 2.9319272\n  - Smooth warps:\n    • ID 359: Global anisotropic scale + shear — 2.9319272\n    • ID 365: Quadratic radial warp — 2.9319272\n\n  Diagnostics and insights\n  - Contact‑graph rigidity: many circles are simultaneously pinned by boundary and multiple near‑equality contacts; slack concentrates on few constraints; local steps often cancel or trigger boundary violations.\n  - Boundary bottlenecks: helping a boundary‑limited circle often tightens a neighboring pair, nullifying gains.\n  - Evaluator strictness: equality allowed; recomputing LP or self‑validating in‑run can flip near‑equality to tiny overlap (~1e−14). Guardrail: avoid recomputation in return path; apply only the micro‑shrink.\n\n  Reproducible baseline and best (Verity)\n  - Best = 2.9319272 with loader returns: IDs 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375, 380, 388.\n  - Artifact path: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; loader policy prevents regressions.\n\
