    \ × (1−1e−12)); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n  - Persist new artifact only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10 (pairwise and boundary).\n\n  Deterministic motifs tested (all parity with artifact = 2.9319272)\n  - Boundary-limited:\n    • ID 375: Balanced boundary–neighbor push — 2.9319272\n  - Pair/triad/cycle:\n    • ID 299: Contact-graph descent — 2.9319272\n    • ID 301: Min-slack pair split — 2.9319272\n    • ID 305: 3-circle cycle-push triad — 2.9319272\n    • ID 327: Boundary-relief triad — 2.9319272\n    • ID 346: 4-cycle shear — 2.9319272\n    • ID 380: Orthogonal split on tightest pair — 2.9319272\n    • ID 388: Two-triad coupled push — 2.9319272\n  - Smooth warps:\n    • ID 359: Global anisotropic scale + shear — 2.9319272\n    • ID 365: Quadratic radial warp — 2.9319272\n\n  Diagnostics and insights\n  - Contact-graph rigidity: many circles pinned by boundary and multiple near-equality contacts; slack concentrated on few constraints;\
