    **Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo be publishable, the work must be completely reframed. Select the single most promising 'motif' from your list. Write a proper 'Methodology' section that describes this method in detail using equations, pseudocode, or a clear algorithm description. Then, design a rigorous experiment to evaluate it. This requires comparing it against a simple baseline (e.g., random perturbation) on at least two different starting configurations (e.g., your high-performing artifact and a standard grid initialization) to demonstrate its properties and generalization. All results must be reported with full, concrete precision. The focus must be on clearly presenting and rigorously evaluating a single, reproducible method.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns\
