parts:
- text: "/execute_action{rank author}\n=/execute_action{page_size 200}\n=/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Orthogonal split from 6×6−minus−corners grid (deterministic, LP‑gated; micro‑shrink) — repeat for eval ID\"\ntags: \"circle packing, LP gating, orthogonal split, grid initializer, deterministic\"\nabstract: \"Re-run the single deterministic motif (tightest‑pair orthogonal split) from the 6×6−minus−corners grid to obtain a fresh evaluation ID for the paper. We solve radii via exact LP (HiGHS), try a small step schedule on the tightest pair’s perpendicular, accept only if ∑r improves by >1e−8 with all post–1e−12 micro‑shrink slacks ≥1e−10; otherwise return the LP result on the grid with micro‑shrink. No writes in return path.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  def _micro_shrink(r, eps=1e-12):\n      r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n\
    \      r *= (1.0 - eps)\n      return r\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n      return d\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                         np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n      b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                     np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n             \
    \ rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rhs else None\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      obj = float(-res.fun)\n      return r, obj, True\n\n  def _min_slacks(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n      x, y = centers[:,0], centers[:,1]\n      b_sl = np.minimum(np.minimum(x - r, 1.0 - x - r), np.minimum(y - r, 1.0 - y - r))\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      mask = np.triu(np.ones((len(r), len(r)), dtype=bool), 1)\n      p_sl = D[mask] - Rsum[mask]\n      return float(np.min(b_sl)), float(np.min(p_sl))\n\n  def _grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      r = 1.0 / 12.0\n      step = 2.0 * r\n      xs =\
    \ [r + i * step for i in range(6)]\n      ys = [r + j * step for j in range(6)]\n      centers = []\n      for j in range(6):\n          for i in range(6):\n              if (i in (0,5)) and (j in (0,5)):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  def _tightest_pair(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      slack = D - Rsum\n      np.fill_diagonal(slack, np.inf)\n      n = len(r)\n      best = (None, None, np.inf)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              s = slack[i, j]\n              if s < best[2]:\n                  best = (i, j, s)\n      return best\n\n  def _clip_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-6):\n      return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      centers = _grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n      r_base, obj_base, ok =\
    \ _solve_lp_for_radii(centers)\n      if not ok:\n          return centers, _micro_shrink(np.full(n, 1.0/12.0, dtype=float), 1e-12)\n\n      i, j, _ = _tightest_pair(centers, r_base)\n      if i is None or j is None or not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          return centers, _micro_shrink(r_base, 1e-12)\n\n      steps = (5e-4, 3e-4, 2e-4, 1e-4)\n      v = centers[j] - centers[i]\n      nrm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n      if nrm < 1e-15:\n          return centers, _micro_shrink(r_base, 1e-12)\n      u = v / nrm\n      for s in steps:\n          for sign in (+1, -1):\n              n_perp = np.array([-u[1], u[0]], dtype=float) * float(sign)\n              trial = centers.copy()\n              trial[i] = trial[i] - s * n_perp\n              trial[j] = trial[j] + s * n_perp\n              trial = _clip_box(trial, margin=1e-6)\n              r_tr, obj_tr, ok2 = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial)\n              if not ok2:\n                  continue\n              r_tr_sh = _micro_shrink(r_tr, 1e-12)\n       \
    \       bmin, pmin = _min_slacks(trial, r_tr_sh)\n              if (obj_tr > obj_base + 1e-8) and (bmin >= 1e-10) and (pmin >= 1e-10):\n                  return trial, r_tr_sh\n      return centers, _micro_shrink(r_base, 1e-12)\n```\n=/execute_action{storage write verity/results_395_396.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id\ttick\ttitle\tscore\n  395\t222\tBaseline: grid 6×6−minus−corners (LP finalize; micro‑shrink)\t2.666666666664\n  396\t222\tBaseline: deterministic global jitter on artifact (LP finalize; micro‑shrink)\t2.9275900457126927\n```\n=/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baselines for archive revision: grid and artifact-jitter (IDs 395, 396)\"\ntags: \"archive, baselines, methodology\"\ncontent: |\n  Purpose: Prepare rigorous baselines for the “Orthogonal Split Motif” (OSM) paper revision.\n\n  Baselines (tick 222)\n  - ID 395: Grid 6×6−minus−corners → LP finalize + 1e−12 micro‑shrink. Score = 2.666666666664.\n  - ID 396: Artifact\
    \ centers + deterministic global jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → LP finalize + micro‑shrink. Score = 2.9275900457126927.\n\n  Method under test (OSM)\n  - Tightest‑pair orthogonal split with step schedule (5e−4, 3e−4, 2e−4, 1e−4), ± perpendicular; accept iff Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n  - From artifact: prior ID 380 (attempted, no accept, returned loader) → 2.9319272179903653.\n  - From grid: re‑submitted to obtain eval ID (pending this tick).\n\n  Plan\n  - Collect OSM-from-grid eval ID/result; compare against ID 395 (grid baseline) and ID 396 (artifact jitter baseline) and ID 272/281 (loader).\n  - Draft archive revision with clear Method (pseudocode), exact acceptance rules, and a results table with full‑precision scores and evaluation IDs.\n```"
