tick: 225
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write verity/results_osm.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id\ttick\tinit\tmethod\tscore\n  272\t133\tartifact\tLoader v5 (artifact return, micro-shrink)\t2.9319272\n  281\t138\tartifact\tLoader v5 reproducibility (micro-shrink)\t2.9319272\n  380\t205\tartifact\tOSM (orthogonal split, LP-gated; no accept)\t2.9319272179903653\n  395\t221\tgrid\t\"Grid 6×6−corners → LP finalize + 1e−12 micro-shrink\"\t2.666666666664\n  396\t221\tartifact\t\"Deterministic global jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → LP + micro-shrink\"\t2.9275900457126927\n  399\t223\tgrid\tOSM (orthogonal split from grid, LP-gated; no accept)\t2.666666666664\n```\n/execute_action{storage write verity/README_OSM.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) — Method and Results (Verity)\n\n  Goal\n  - Evaluate a single, deterministic local move (OSM) under exact LP gating and strict feasibility to test whether it can improve ∑r on two initializations: (a) grid\
    \ 6×6−corners, (b) strong artifact.\n\n  Method (deterministic)\n  1) Given centers C (32×2), solve exact LP (HiGHS) for radii r (maximize ∑r subject to boundary and pairwise constraints).\n  2) Find tightest pair (i*, j*) minimizing slack s_ij = ||C_i−C_j|| − (r_i + r_j).\n  3) Step schedule S = {5e−4, 3e−4, 2e−4, 1e−4}; orientations T = {+1, −1}.\n     - u = (C_j*−C_i*) / ||C_j*−C_i*||; n_perp = t · (−u_y, u_x).\n     - Try C' with symmetric ±s·n_perp on i*, j*, clipped to [1e−6, 1−1e−6]; re-solve LP for r'; micro-shrink r'' = (1−1e−12)·r'.\n     - Accept iff Δ∑r > 1e−8 and min boundary/pairwise slacks on (C', r'') ≥ 1e−10.\n  4) If none accepted, return base (C, micro-shrunk r). Deterministic: no randomness.\n\n  Results (eval IDs; full precision where available)\n  - Baselines:\n    - 272 (tick 133): Loader v5 — 2.9319272\n    - 281 (tick 138): Loader v5 reproducibility — 2.9319272\n    - 395 (tick 221): Grid 6×6−corners → LP + micro-shrink — 2.666666666664\n    - 396 (tick 221):\
    \ Artifact + deterministic global jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → LP + micro-shrink — 2.9275900457126927\n  - OSM (this method):\n    - 380 (tick 205): OSM from artifact — 2.9319272179903653 (no accepted step)\n    - 399 (tick 223): OSM from grid — 2.666666666664 (no accepted step)\n\n  Conclusion\n  - Under strict LP-gated acceptance and safety thresholds, OSM does not improve either from the grid or the strong artifact. The near-rigid contact structure likely requires coupled/stabilized multi-circle moves.\n\n  Reproducibility\n  - Deterministic algorithm with explicit thresholds; evaluator permits equality; micro-shrink ensures numerical robustness. No cross-lineage code/artifact use.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write verity/RESULTS_INDEX_addendum_225.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # RESULTS_INDEX addendum (tick 225)\n  Added OSM baselines and results:\n  - 395: Grid 6×6−corners → LP + micro-shrink = 2.666666666664\n  - 396: Artifact + deterministic global jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → LP +\
    \ micro-shrink = 2.9275900457126927\n  - 399: OSM (orthogonal split) from grid → 2.666666666664 (no accepted step)\n  References: 272/281 (artifact loader), 380 (OSM from artifact = 2.9319272179903653).\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"OSM paper: method + baselines logged; awaiting review (IDs 395, 396, 399, 380, 272, 281)\"\ntags: \"archive, OSM, methodology, baselines\"\ncontent: |\n  OSM method (orthogonal split, deterministic, LP-gated) formalized and submitted with clear pseudocode and acceptance rules. Baselines included:\n  - Grid baseline: ID 395 = 2.666666666664\n  - Artifact jitter baseline (σ=2e−4, seed=1): ID 396 = 2.9275900457126927\n  - Loader references: ID 272 = 2.9319272, ID 281 = 2.9319272\n  Method results:\n  - OSM from artifact: ID 380 = 2.9319272179903653 (no accept)\n  - OSM from grid: ID 399 = 2.666666666664 (no accept)\n  Storage updated: results_osm.tsv, README_OSM.md, RESULTS_INDEX_addendum_225.md.\n  Next:\
    \ if reviewers request, add “grid jitter” baseline (σ=2e−4, seed=2) and a short ablation on step schedule; otherwise maintain.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline: deterministic global jitter from grid (LP finalize; micro‑shrink)\"\ntags: \"circle packing, baseline, grid, jitter, LP finalize, deterministic\"\nabstract: \"Deterministic baseline from grid 6×6−corners: apply small Gaussian jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=2) to all centers, clip to [0,1]^2, solve radii via exact LP (HiGHS), and apply a 1e−12 micro‑shrink. Complements artifact‑jitter baseline and grid baseline for the OSM paper.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  def _micro_shrink(r, eps=1e-12):\n      r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n      r *= (1.0 - eps)\n      return r\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n\
    \      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n      return d\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                         np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n      b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                     np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n      D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs,\
    \ dtype=float) if rhs else None\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      obj = float(-res.fun)\n      return r, obj, True\n\n  def _grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      r = 1.0 / 12.0\n      step = 2.0 * r\n      xs = [r + i * step for i in range(6)]\n      ys = [r + j * step for j in range(6)]\n      centers = []\n      for j in range(6):\n          for i in range(6):\n              if (i in (0,5)) and (j in (0,5)):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      centers = _grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(2)\n      centers = centers + rng.normal(0.0, 2e-4, size=centers.shape)\n      centers = np.clip(centers,\
    \ 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n      r, obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers)\n      if not ok:\n          b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                         np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n      return centers, _micro_shrink(r, 1e-12)\n```"
