tick: 230
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write verity/results_osm.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id\ttick\tinit\tmethod\tscore\n  272\t133\tartifact\tLoader v5 (artifact return, micro-shrink)\t2.9319272\n  281\t138\tartifact\tLoader v5 reproducibility (micro-shrink)\t2.9319272\n  380\t205\tartifact\tOSM (orthogonal split, LP-gated; no accept)\t2.9319272179903653\n  395\t221\tgrid\t\"Grid 6×6−corners → LP finalize + 1e−12 micro-shrink\"\t2.666666666664\n  396\t221\tartifact\t\"Deterministic global jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → LP + micro-shrink\"\t2.9275900457126927\n  399\t223\tgrid\tOSM (orthogonal split from grid, LP-gated; no accept)\t2.666666666664\n  401\t225\tgrid\t\"Deterministic global jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=2) → LP + micro-shrink\"\t2.6623220384439765\n  406\t229\tartifact\tTriad motif (tightest pair orthogonal split + nearest-third stabilizer; LP-gated; loader fallback)\t2.9319272179903653\n  407\t229\tgrid\tTriad motif (tightest pair orthogonal split + nearest-third stabilizer; LP-gated;\
    \ grid fallback)\t2.666666666664\n```\n/execute_action{storage write verity/README_OSM.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Local Motif Studies (Verity): OSM and Triad (deterministic, LP-gated)\n\n  Goal\n  - Evaluate simple, deterministic local motifs under exact LP gating and strict feasibility to test whether they improve ∑r on two inits: (a) grid 6×6−corners, (b) strong artifact.\n\n  Shared protocol (deterministic)\n  - r := LP(C) via HiGHS; acceptance only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and min boundary/pairwise slacks (after 1e−12 micro-shrink) ≥ 1e−10. Otherwise return base (grid LP or artifact loader-style).\n\n  Motif A: OSM (Orthogonal Split on tightest pair)\n  - Pick tightest pair (i,j) by LP slacks; try step schedule {5e−4,3e−4,2e−4,1e−4} along ± perpendicular; LP-gate and accept if thresholds pass.\n\n  Motif B: Triad (tightest pair + nearest third stabilizer)\n  - As OSM for i,j plus a third circle k chosen as the nearest to pair midpoint. Move k outward from the midpoint by γ·step with γ ∈\
    \ {0.5, 0.3}. LP-gate and accept if thresholds pass.\n\n  Results (evaluation IDs; full precision in results_osm.tsv)\n  - Baselines:\n    - 272, 281: Artifact loader v5 → 2.9319272\n    - 395: Grid 6×6−corners → 2.666666666664\n    - 401: Grid jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=2) → 2.6623220384439765\n    - 396: Artifact jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → 2.9275900457126927\n  - OSM (no accepted step):\n    - 380 (artifact) → 2.9319272179903653\n    - 399 (grid) → 2.666666666664\n  - Triad (no accepted step):\n    - 406 (artifact) → 2.9319272179903653\n    - 407 (grid) → 2.666666666664\n\n  Conclusion\n  - Under conservative LP-gated thresholds, both OSM and Triad produce parity from grid and artifact initializations. The contact graph appears near rigid; future work should test richer coupled/stabilized operators with the same rigorous template.\n\n  Files\n  - results_osm.tsv — consolidated ID table\n  - CHANGELOG_OSM_226.md, RESULTS_INDEX_addendum_225.md — updates over time\n```\n/execute_action{storage\
