- text: "/execute_action{goto reflect}\n=/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Deep reflection: What core assumption should I challenge to unlock progress beyond parity?\n  - Hypothesis H1: Single- or one-stabilizer motifs are too weak for the near-rigid contact graph. Need “two-stabilizer” or cycle-compensated moves that explicitly preserve feasibility while redistributing slack.\n  - Hypothesis H2: Trust region must be guided by model-agreement using LP duals: predict Δ∑r from linearized distance changes and compare to exact LP improvement; adapt step/γ accordingly.\n  - Hypothesis H3: Motif selection should be stress-driven: choose motifs from edges with highest duals and include at least one boundary-relief direction.\n  - Sketch next operator: Pair split (i,j) orthogonal ±; two stabilizers k,l selected by (a) nearest to pair midpoint and (b) max dual “stress” among neighbors; k moves outward from midpoint; l shifts along its strongest boundary-relief normal or along a dual-informed\
    \ direction. Step s∈{5e−4,…}, γk,γl∈{0.5,0.3,0.2}. Accept only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–1e−12 slacks ≥1e−10 and model-agreement ratio in [0.4, 1.5].\ntick: 3\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Plan: Dual-guided two-stabilizer motif with model-agreement gating\"\ntags: \"plan, motif, LP duals, model-agreement, reproducibility\"\ncontent: |\n  Rationale\n  - OSM and simple triad are parity under strict gates. Contact graph appears near-rigid; single stabilizer is insufficient. Next step: dual-guided, two-stabilizer coupled move + model-agreement gating.\n\n  Operator (deterministic template)\n  1) LP(C) → radii r and duals λ_ij for active/tight edges; compute boundary duals β_i from r_i = boundary(C_i) cases.\n  2) Pick tightest or highest-dual pair (i,j). Define midpoint m = (C_i + C_j)/2 and unit perpendicular n⊥ to (C_j−C_i).\n  3) Select two stabilizers:\n     - k: nearest to m\n     - l: argmax neighbor of {i,j} by dual “stress”\
    \ (λ or boundary β)\n  4) Move:\n     - i,j: ±s n⊥ (orthogonal split)\n     - k: +γ_k s dir_k (dir_k = normalized (C_k−m))\n     - l: +γ_l s dir_l (dir_l = boundary-relief normal if boundary-tight; else weighted sum of high-dual neighbor directions)\n  5) Model-agreement gating:\n     - Predict Δ∑r̂ from LP-dual linearization of pairwise distances and boundary terms; accept only if:\n       • Exact LP Δ∑r > 1e−8\n       • min slacks (post 1e−12 shrink) ≥ 1e−10\n       • Agreement ratio Δ∑r / Δ∑r̂ ∈ [0.4, 1.5]\n  6) Deterministic schedules: s ∈ {5e−4, 3e−4, 2e−4, 1e−4}; γ_k,γ_l ∈ {0.5, 0.3, 0.2}; fixed order.\n\n  Evaluation protocol\n  - Inits: grid 6×6−corners; artifact.\n  - Baselines: grid, grid-jitter (σ=2e−4), artifact-jitter (σ=2e−4), loader refs.\n  - Evidence: full-precision scores + IDs. No writes in return path; artifact-only loader if no accept.\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep guardrails: exact LP finalize, micro-shrink, strict slacks, deterministic RNG, no cross-lineage use.\n  - Only\
    \ proceed to implementation if this plan remains sound after one more short reflection; otherwise maintain documentation and pause.\n```"
