- text: "/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"200-234\"\n    summary: |\n      Consolidated motif study and documentation (ticks 200–234). Focus: rigorous, deterministic local-move evaluations under exact LP gating with strict feasibility thresholds; best score unchanged at 2.9319272 (loader v5).\n\n      Methods and key results (full-precision, with Eval IDs):\n      - Balanced boundary–neighbor push (artifact): ID 375 = 2.9319272 (parity).\n      - Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM):\n        • From artifact: ID 380 = 2.9319272179903653 (no accepted step; parity).\n        • From grid 6×6−corners: ID 399 = 2.666666666664 (no accepted step; equals grid baseline).\n      - Baselines for paper:\n        • Grid 6×6−corners → LP + 1e−12 micro‑shrink: ID 395 = 2.666666666664.\n        • Grid jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=2) → LP + micro‑shrink: ID 401 = 2.6623220384439765.\n        • Artifact jitter (σ=2e−4, seed=1) → LP + micro‑shrink: ID 396 = 2.9275900457126927.\n      -\
    \ Coupled Triad motif (orthogonal split on tightest pair + nearest‑third stabilizer):\n        • From artifact: ID 406 = 2.9319272179903653 (parity).\n        • From grid: ID 407 = 2.666666666664 (parity).\n\n      Publications and reviews:\n      - Archive #9 “Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM)…” accepted (6/10). Contains method pseudocode, exact acceptance rules, baselines, and IDs. Addendum added (triad results: IDs 406, 407).\n\n      Engineering and storage:\n      - Added/updated: verity/results_osm.tsv; README_OSM.md; CHANGELOG_OSM_226.md; CHANGELOG_OSM_230.md; RESULTS_INDEX_addendum_225.md. Private memory notes for archive preparation and baselines.\n\n      Policy/guardrails (unchanged):\n      - Loader‑only return path (centers unchanged; radii×(1−1e−12)); no LP/self‑validation/writes during return.\n      - Offline improvements must pass exact LP gating with Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post‑micro‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10 before persistence.\n      - Deterministic schedules; no cross‑lineage\
    \ code/artifact use.\n\n      Reflection and next plan:\n      - Single/one‑stabilizer motifs are too weak for the near‑rigid contact graph. Planned a deterministic two‑stabilizer motif and model‑agreement gating (dual‑guided) and submitted initial variants from artifact/grid (results pending at submission time within this window)."
thinking_content: "**Summarizing evaluation results**\n\nI’m thinking about summarizing key evaluation IDs and baseline results for the range of 200-233, including various metrics. I need to include details like triad evaluations from ticks 406 and 407, and mention the OSM paper acceptance with a score of 6/10. I should emphasize that we haven't seen results for the two-stabilizer motifs submitted at ticks 233 and 234, and consider our token budget as well. I may need to draft a YAML outline for pruning and summarizing these findings.**Considering pruning actions**\n\nI'm noticing the station indicates \"Cooldown Active,\" so typically I would think we need to wait, but now it states \"Pruning Actions Available\" with no cooldown. This lets me perform a prune response. I’m planning to combine the range 200-233 into a single block for summarization since they’re consecutive. However, I need to make sure I include necessary details without exceeding the YAML specifications and remember to\
  \ quote any single-line text with colons. I'll also add \"ticks: 234\" for the latest pruning.**Evaluating prune options**\n\nI need to consider whether we should prune the last tick, 234, since it doesn't seem to have significant content, just research. It's fine to prune 234, as it's not protected. I can consolidate that tick with 200-234 since they are all consecutive. In the summary, I'll include the deterministic triad evaluation results and planned two-stabilizer motifs, plus notes on updated storage files. I may adjust meta, but it doesn’t seem necessary right now. I’ll prepare for the command to execute the prune action.**Crafting a concise summary**\n\nI’m considering how to include IDs like 395, 396, 399, 401, 406, and 407 while affirming important values like \"2.9319272 unchanged\" and that the loader v5 policy remains unchanged. I want to keep the summary concise but fully informative, avoiding a detailed per-tick breakdown. \n\nI'll highlight the theme of rigorous evaluation\
  \ of local motifs, mention the published negative results, and reference the baselines from various IDs, including OSM and triad artifact parities. Time to put this together!**Providing results summary**\n\nI need to provide the latest results, starting with storage updates for files like results_osm.tsv, README_OSM.md, and CHANGELOG. I've also posted archive addenda. \n\nReflecting on new plans, I've submitted the two-stabilizer motif and model-agreement gating, with results pending after submission at tick 233. \n\nI’ll maintain the loader policy and ensure proper YAML quoting for any special characters. Since the user hasn't requested anything specific beyond pruning, I'll proceed with the prune action while confirming the overall structure. Let's finalize this!"
