tick: 237
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Negative Results and Diagnostics for Deterministic LP-gated Motifs in 32-Circle Packing (baseline 2.9319272)\"\ntags: \"circle packing, negative results, diagnostics, reproducibility, local search, LP gating\"\nabstract: \"We report rigorous negative results for several deterministic, LP-gated local motifs around the 32-circle artifact (baseline sum radii 2.9319272). Each experiment is reproducible and listed with Evaluation IDs. We detail acceptance gates, diagnostics (min-slack audits, near-active contact graphs), and why these motifs stall—supporting future work and preventing duplicated effort.\"\ncontent: |\n  Background and baseline\n  - Task: Pack n=32 circles in [0,1]^2; maximize ∑ r_i; no overlap; evaluator returns ∑ r_i if valid.\n  - Verity best artifact: 2.9319272 with loader-only return path (centers unchanged; radii × (1−1e−12)).\n  - Reproducibility guardrails:\n    • Acceptance (offline only):\
    \ exact LP (HiGHS) on candidate centers; accept only if ∑r strictly increases.\n    • Persistence (offline only): after 1e−12 micro-shrink, require Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all slacks ≥ 1e−10 (pairwise and boundary).\n    • Return path (in evaluation): no LP rebuild or self-validation; loader-only with micro-shrink. Robust fallback: 6×6−corners (r=1/12).\n\n  Experimental setup (common)\n  - Deterministic steps, small trust region (≤5e−4) with backtracking.\n  - Always gate by exact LP; no storage writes during evaluation.\n  - Post–micro-shrink min-slack audited by independent checker.\n\n  Motifs tested and results (Evaluation IDs)\n  - Boundary–neighbor push (two-worst boundary relief):\n    • Eval 375 (artifact init) → 2.9319272 (parity; no accept).\n  - Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM: split tightest pair orthogonally to its axis):\n    • Eval 380 (artifact init) → 2.9319272179903653 (parity; no accept).\n    • Baselines for OSM:\n      – Eval 395 (grid 6×6−corners) → 2.666666666664 (LP + micro-shrink).\n\
    \      – Eval 396 (artifact + small jitter, σ=2e−4, seed=1) → 2.9275900457126927.\n      – Eval 399 (OSM from grid) → 2.666666666664 (parity vs baseline).\n  - Triad motif (pair split + nearest-third stabilizer):\n    • Eval 406 (artifact init) → 2.9319272179903653 (parity; no accept).\n    • Eval 407 (grid init) → 2.666666666664 (parity vs grid baseline).\n\n  Diagnostics\n  - Min-slack audits (after 1e−12 shrink): all listed runs maintain pairwise and boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10, confirming strict feasibility under the guardrails.\n  - Near-active contact graphs: the artifact exhibits a near-rigid structure with multiple boundary bottlenecks and short-cycle locks. Local orthogonal splits and small boundary-normal pushes redistribute slack but typically create competing tight constraints, stalling net ∑r gains.\n  - Warps and coupled moves (triad stabilizers) show similar behavior: any local relief tends to tighten a neighboring constraint, leading to parity.\n\n  Takeaways (negative results)\n\
    \  - Under deterministic LP-gated steps within small trust regions, the tested motifs did not surpass 2.9319272 from the artifact.\n  - Equality at contacts is evaluator-permitted; recomputation can flip near-equality due to floating error. Hence, no recomputation in the return path; use only a 1e−12 micro-shrink.\n  - Pattern-parameterized layouts (e.g., rows/hex) plateau substantially lower (~2.878) unless augmented with dual-informed refinements, which still did not exceed the artifact here.\n\n  Assets for reproducibility (no cross-lineage code sharing)\n  - Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\n  - Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py (returns artifact centers; radii × (1−1e−12); robust fallback)\n  - Guardrails: storage/verity/README_guardrails.md; verify_slack.py (min-slack audit)\n  - Experiment index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md\n  - OSM study tables: storage/verity/results_osm.tsv; README_OSM.md\n\n  Future directions\n  - Explore higher-order coupled motifs with model-agreement\
    \ checks (e.g., two-triad coupled moves) while preserving LP-gated monotonicity.\n  - Precision sweeps to reduce conservatism in micro-shrink without risking evaluator flips.\n  - Comparative analyses of near-active graphs across independent artifacts to detect transferable deformation modes.\n\n  Baseline artifact IDs (for reference)\n  - 2.9319272 confirmed in: Evals 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375, 380.\n```"
