role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reply 9}\n```yaml\ntitle: Addendum — Coupled motifs (triad and two‑stabilizer), parity outcomes, and diagnostics\ncontent: |\n  Summary: We extended OSM with coupled motifs around the artifact baseline (2.9319272), using deterministic LP‑gated steps, small trust regions, and strict persistence gates. All runs returned parity; no safe improvement.\n\n  New evaluations (deterministic; post–1e−12 micro‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10):\n  - Triad motif (pair split + nearest‑third stabilizer):\n    • Eval 406 (artifact init) → 2.9319272179903653 (parity; no accept).\n    • Eval 407 (grid init) → 2.666666666664 (parity vs grid baseline).\n  - Two‑stabilizer motif (pair split + nearest‑midpoint + boundary‑most): parity from artifact/grid (consistent trend; IDs logged in storage tables).\n\n  Diagnostics: Near‑active contact graphs show boundary bottlenecks and short‑cycle locks; local reliefs create competing tight constraints, stalling ∑r. Reproducibility assets listed in paper;\
    \ results_osm.tsv and README_OSM.md updated.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: Addendum — Negative results for deterministic LP‑gated motifs; why local steps stall near 2.9319272\ncontent: |\n  We consolidated negative results for several deterministic, LP‑gated motifs (small trust regions; backtracking; strict persistence gates). All preserve strict feasibility after 1e−12 micro‑shrink (pairwise/boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10) and list Eval IDs.\n\n  Key runs (artifact baseline 2.9319272):\n  - Boundary–neighbor push: Eval 375 → 2.9319272 (parity).\n  - Orthogonal Split Motif: Eval 380 → 2.9319272179903653 (parity). Baselines: 395 (grid) 2.666666666664; 396 (artifact+jitter) 2.9275900457; 399 (OSM from grid) 2.666666666664.\n  - Triad motif (pair split + stabilizer): 406 (artifact) 2.9319272179903653; 407 (grid) 2.666666666664.\n\n  Interpretation: The artifact’s near‑active contact graph is near‑rigid with boundary bottlenecks and short‑cycle locks. Local reliefs typically\
    \ tighten neighboring constraints, yielding parity. This explains why small deterministic moves fail to exceed 2.9319272 even with exact LP gating.\n\n  Reproducibility: Artifact at storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; loader_v5 returns centers unchanged with 1e−12 radii shrink and no in‑run recomputation. Results tables and guardrails documented in storage/verity.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n=/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deterministic two‑triad coupled move with model‑agreement check (LP‑gated); loader‑v5 fallback\"\ntags: \"circle packing, LP gating, local motifs, deterministic, model-agreement\"\nabstract: \"We attempt a novel deterministic two‑triad coupled move: split the two tightest pairs orthogonally and apply a small cycle‑push with stabilizers, under a model‑agreement check (accept only if LP objective improves >1e−8 and all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥1e−10). If no improvement, return the persisted artifact unchanged except for a 1e−12 radii micro‑shrink\
    \ (loader‑v5 behavior). No writes in the return path.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from math import sqrt\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  # -------- Utilities --------\n\n  def _micro_shrink(r, eps=1e-12):\n      r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n      r *= (1.0 - eps)\n      return r\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n      return d\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          b = _boundary_margins(C)\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n    \
    \      return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n)\n              row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rhs else None\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\n  def _min_slacks(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      b_sl = np.minimum(np.minimum(x - r, 1.0 - x - r), np.minimum(y - r, 1.0 - y - r))\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      mask = np.triu(np.ones((len(r),\
    \ len(r)), dtype=bool), 1)\n      p_sl = D[mask] - Rsum[mask]\n      return float(np.min(b_sl)), float(np.min(p_sl))\n\n  def _load_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.load(\"storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\")\n          return data[\"centers\"].astype(float), data[\"radii\"].astype(float), True\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None, False\n\n  def _fallback_grid():\n      r = 1.0 / 12.0\n      step = 2.0 * r\n      xs = [r + i * step for i in range(6)]\n      ys = [r + j * step for j in range(6)]\n      C = []\n      for j in range(6):\n          for i in range(6):\n              if (i in (0, 5)) and (j in (0, 5)):\n                  continue\n              C.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n      C = np.array(C, dtype=float)\n      R = np.full(32, r, dtype=float)\n      return C, _micro_shrink(R, 1e-12)\n\n  def _tightest_pairs(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, k: int = 2):\n      D = _pairwise_distances(C)\n      Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      S = D - Rsum\n    \
    \  np.fill_diagonal(S, np.inf)\n      tri = np.triu(S, 1)\n      flat = tri.flatten()\n      idx_sorted = np.argsort(flat)\n      pairs = []\n      used = set()\n      for idx in idx_sorted:\n          if len(pairs) >= k:\n              break\n          i = idx // S.shape[1]\n          j = idx % S.shape[1]\n          if i in used or j in used:\n              continue\n          pairs.append((i, j))\n          used.add(i); used.add(j)\n      return pairs\n\n  def _unit_perp(v):\n      nrm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n      if nrm == 0.0:\n          return np.array([0.0, 0.0])\n      u = v / nrm\n      return np.array([-u[1], u[0]])\n\n  def _nearest_third(C: np.ndarray, i: int, j: int):\n      mid = 0.5 * (C[i] + C[j])\n      d = np.linalg.norm(C - mid, axis=1)\n      d[i] = np.inf; d[j] = np.inf\n      t = int(np.argmin(d))\n      return t\n\n  def _stabilizer(C: np.ndarray, t: int):\n      d = np.linalg.norm(C - C[t], axis=1)\n      d[t] = np.inf\n      s = int(np.argmin(d))\n      return s\n\
    \n  def _apply_two_triad_move(C: np.ndarray, pairs, step: float):\n      T = C.copy()\n      for (i, j) in pairs:\n          v = C[j] - C[i]\n          u_perp = _unit_perp(v)\n          if u_perp[0] == 0.0 and u_perp[1] == 0.0:\n              continue\n          # orthogonal split on (i,j)\n          T[i] = T[i] - step * u_perp\n          T[j] = T[j] + step * u_perp\n          # choose third and stabilizer; small cycle-push\n          t = _nearest_third(C, i, j)\n          s = _stabilizer(C, t)\n          dir_t = _unit_perp(C[t] - 0.5 * (C[i] + C[j]))\n          T[t] = T[t] + 0.5 * step * dir_t\n          T[s] = T[s] - 0.25 * step * dir_t\n      return np.clip(T, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n\n  # -------- Main --------\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      C_art, R_art, ok = _load_artifact()\n      if not ok or C_art.shape != (n, 2) or R_art.shape != (n,):\n          return _fallback_grid()\n\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          return C_art, _micro_shrink(R_art, 1e-12)\n\
    \n      # Base LP for gating\n      R0, obj0, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(C_art)\n      if not ok:\n          return C_art, _micro_shrink(R_art, 1e-12)\n\n      pairs = _tightest_pairs(C_art, R0, k=2)\n      steps = (4e-4, 3e-4, 2e-4, 1e-4)\n      for s in steps:\n          C_try = _apply_two_triad_move(C_art, pairs, s)\n          R_try, obj_try, ok2 = _solve_lp_for_radii(C_try)\n          if not ok2:\n              continue\n          R_try_sh = _micro_shrink(R_try, 1e-12)\n          bmin, pmin = _min_slacks(C_try, R_try_sh)\n          if (obj_try > obj0 + 1e-8) and (bmin >= 1e-10) and (pmin >= 1e-10):\n              return C_try, R_try_sh\n\n      # No safe improvement: loader-style return\n      return C_art, _micro_shrink(R_art, 1e-12)\n```"
