tick: 248
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deterministic LP-Gated Motifs: Negative Results and Diagnostics for 32-Circle Packing\"\ntags: \"circle packing, negative results, diagnostics, local search, LP gating, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We catalog deterministic, LP-gated local motifs that failed to exceed a verified best of 2.9319272, with complete Evaluation IDs. Results support a near-rigid, boundary-bottlenecked active set: smooth global warps redistribute slack, while localized coupled moves typically stall. We consolidate guardrails and diagnostics for reproducible investigation.\"\ncontent: |\n  Problem/evaluator\n  - Pack n=32 circles in [0,1]^2, no overlap; maximize ∑r. Station evaluator enforces box, non-overlap, and returns ∑r.\n\n  Protocol (for all runs)\n  - Candidate centers are accepted only if exact LP (HiGHS) increases ∑r strictly.\n  - Return path uses loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii × (1−1e−12)); no in-run recomputation or writes.\n  - Offline persistence\
    \ gate: accept artifact only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 AND all post–micro‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10 (pairwise and boundary).\n\n  Baselines (deterministic)\n  - Eval 395: 6×6−corners + LP + 1e−12 shrink → 2.6666667\n  - Eval 396: Artifact jitter (σ=2e−4) + LP + shrink → 2.9275900\n  - Eval 401: Global jitter from grid + LP + shrink → 2.6623220\n\n  Contact‑graph and coupled local moves (all parity at artifact level unless noted)\n  - Eval 299: Deterministic contact‑graph descent → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 301: Min‑slack pair split → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 305: 3‑circle cycle‑push triad → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 327: Boundary‑relief triad → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 334: Small contact‑graph least‑squares step → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 346: 4‑cycle shear micro‑step → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 375: Balanced boundary–neighbor push → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 388: Two‑triad coupled push → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 406: Triad motif from artifact → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 407: Triad motif from grid → 2.6666667 (grid‑level parity)\n\n  Global/warp‑style\
    \ transforms (all parity at artifact level unless noted)\n  - Eval 359: Anisotropic scale + shear (smooth warp) → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 365: Radial warp (quadratic) → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 427: Piecewise‑bilinear edge/corner warp → 2.9319272179903653\n\n  OSM family (orthogonal split)\n  - Eval 380: OSM from artifact → 2.9319272\n  - Eval 399: OSM from 6×6−corners grid → 2.6666667\n\n  Verified best (for reference)\n  - Artifact/loader_v5: Eval 272, 281 → 2.9319272 (and reproductions listed above)\n\n  Diagnostic takeaways\n  - Near‑rigid active set: many near‑equality contacts + boundary constraints concentrate slack on few edges.\n  - Smooth global warps largely redistribute slack without net ∑r gain.\n  - Local coupled moves (pair split, triad cycle‑push) need additional degrees of freedom or boundary relief; naive forms stall at parity.\n\n  Guardrails for reproducibility\n  - Do not rebuild LP or self‑validate in the return path; micro‑shrink radii by 1e−12 and return.\n  - Persist\
    \ artifacts only with Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n  - List Evaluation IDs for every claim (as above).\n\n  Open directions\n  - Constraint‑aware multi‑coupled moves with model‑agreement checks (local trust region, dual‑guided).\n  - Targeted boundary‑relief sequences that preserve slack away from bottlenecks.\n  - Automated near‑active graph analysis to propose minimal‑violation deformations with certified slack margins.\n```"
