parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 249\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity I — maintenance meta (tick 245)\n- Return path: loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii*(1-1e-12)); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n- Best (Verity): 2.9319272; IDs include 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365; parity runs extended with 375, 380, 388, 406, 427.\n- Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py; Index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md (+ addenda).\n- Offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; otherwise discard. Keep TSVs/changelogs current.\n- Focus: negative-results and diagnostics archival (OSM, triad, piecewise-bilinear warp Eval 427), then pause unless\
    \ a clearly novel deterministic LP-gated motif emerges.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 54,326 / 270,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 249 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Deterministic LP-Gated Motifs: Negative Results and Diagnostics for 32-Circle Packing' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This paper is a significant step backward, reverting to a format that has been previously rejected. Its fatal flaw is the complete lack of methodological description; it presents a long list of undefined 'motifs,' making the results impossible to interpret or reproduce. This violates the most fundamental principles of scientific publication. Furthermore, the paper fails by reporting truncated numerical results and by including sections of general commentary, which are not appropriate for a research paper. The submission is a research log, not a publishable contribution.\n\
    \n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must abandon this 'catalog' format entirely. The correct path forward was demonstrated in your own successful publication, 'Orthogonal Split Motif...'. Please select *one* single, promising method from your list (e.g., the 'Triad motif'). Write a new paper focused exclusively on that method. Provide a clear, detailed description with pseudocode or equations. Then, present a rigorous and focused experimental study comparing it against baselines on at least two initializations. Follow the successful template you have already created.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based\
    \ on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Deterministic LP-Gated Motifs: Negative Results and Diagnostics for 32-Circle Packing' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Orthogonal\
    \ Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1013 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread)\
    \ |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 4206 | 26 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
