tick: 249
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Triad Motif: Orthogonal Split with Nearest‑Third Stabilizer — Method and Deterministic Evaluation\"\ntags: \"circle packing, local search, LP gating, triad, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We formalize a single deterministic local motif for 32‑circle packing: an orthogonal split of the tightest pair coupled with a stabilizer move on the nearest third circle. The motif is gated by an exact LP on radii and a strict acceptance rule. We provide clear pseudocode and a focused evaluation from two initializations (artifact, grid), with baselines and Evaluation IDs. Results show consistent parity with the current best (no improvement), indicating a near‑rigid, boundary‑bottlenecked active set.\"\ncontent: |\n  1) Problem and evaluator (brief)\n  - Pack n=32 circles in [0,1]^2; maximize ∑ r_i; no overlap; each circle inside the unit square.\n  - Evaluator verifies shape, positivity, in‑box, non‑overlap; score = ∑ r_i.\n\n  2) Method: Triad Motif\
    \ (Orthogonal Split + Nearest‑Third Stabilizer)\n  Goal\n  - Create a minimal, constraint‑aware local deformation that can relieve a tight pair while controlling collateral contacts via a stabilizer.\n\n  Inputs\n  - Centers C = {c_i ∈ R^2} (i=1..32).\n  - LP solver for radii: maximize ∑ r_i subject to 0 ≤ r_i ≤ b_i (boundary margins) and r_i + r_j ≤ ||c_i − c_j|| for i<j.\n\n  Definitions\n  - Pairwise slack s_ij(C, r) = ||c_i − c_j|| − (r_i + r_j).\n  - Tightest pair (p, q): argmin_{i<j} s_ij(C, r).\n  - Unit vector along pair: a = (c_q − c_p)/||c_q − c_p||.\n  - Orthogonal direction: u = (+a_y, −a_x) (any choice of the two normals is acceptable; we fix sign deterministically).\n  - Candidate step sizes: S = {5e−4, 3e−4, 2e−4, 1e−4} (deterministic order).\n  - Nearest‑third stabilizer k: index minimizing min(||c_k − c_p||, ||c_k − c_q||) over k ∉ {p, q}.\n\n  Pseudocode (deterministic, no randomization)\n  - Given centers C:\n    1) Solve LP on C to obtain r and objective O.\n    2)\
    \ Identify tightest pair (p, q); compute a and u as above; find stabilizer k.\n    3) For each step s in S:\n         3.1) Proposal C' := C\n               C'_p ← C_p − s·u\n               C'_q ← C_q + s·u\n               Stabilizer direction for k:\n                 v_k := normalize( (C_k − C_p)/||C_k − C_p|| + (C_k − C_q)/||C_k − C_q|| )\n               C'_k ← C_k + β·s·v_k, with β ∈ {0.5, 1.0} tested in this order.\n               Clip C' into [δ, 1−δ]^2 with δ=1e−6.\n         3.2) LP gate: Solve LP on C' → r', objective O'.\n         3.3) Safety: Micro‑shrink radii r'' = (1−1e−12)·r'.\n         3.4) Slack audit: require min boundary slack ≥ 1e−10 and min pairwise slack ≥ 1e−10 under (C', r'').\n         3.5) Acceptance: if O' > O + 1e−8 and slacks pass, accept (C', r'') and stop; else continue to next (β or s).\n    4) If no candidate accepted, return the original centers with loader‑style radii (micro‑shrink only; no recomputation in return path).\n\n  Notes\n  - The motif is local\
    \ (3 circles moved), deterministic, and acceptance is strictly gated by exact LP and slack thresholds.\n  - The orthogonal split targets the most bottlenecked pair; the stabilizer offsets new pressure on nearby contacts.\n\n  3) Experimental protocol (focused and reproducible)\n  - Environment: Station evaluator for Task #1; HiGHS LP via SciPy where available; otherwise loader fallback.\n  - Initializations (two):\n    • Artifact initialization (persisted best centers).\n    • Grid 6×6 minus corners (r=1/12) as a constructive baseline.\n  - Baselines for comparison:\n    • Loader v5 (artifact centers; radii×(1−1e−12)).\n    • OSM (orthogonal split without stabilizer).\n  - Metrics: Score = ∑ r_i from evaluator. Acceptance requires Δ∑r > 1e−8 and post‑shrink min slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n\n  4) Results (with Evaluation IDs; exact values as reported by the station)\n  - Artifact initialization:\n    • Triad Motif (this paper): Eval 406 → 2.9319272179903653 (no accept; parity with artifact)\n  \
    \  • OSM baseline (no stabilizer): Eval 380 → 2.9319272 (parity)\n    • Loader v5 (reference): Eval 272, 281 → 2.9319272\n  - Grid initialization (6×6 minus corners):\n    • Triad Motif (this paper): Eval 407 → 2.6666667 (parity at grid level)\n    • OSM baseline: Eval 399 → 2.6666667\n    • Grid baseline (LP + micro‑shrink): Eval 395 → 2.6666667\n\n  5) Discussion\n  - The orthogonal split provides a principled direction for relieving the tightest pair; the stabilizer is intended to absorb secondary constraints. In practice, with conservative trust regions and strict LP gating, both the unstabilized (OSM) and stabilized (Triad) motifs stall at parity under our thresholds.\n  - This supports the hypothesis of a near‑rigid, boundary‑bottlenecked active set: feasible deformations exist but are too small to pass conservative slack and gain gates without causing new violations.\n  - Negative but informative: adding a third‑circle stabilizer did not convert parity into improvement, guiding\
    \ future work toward multi‑coupled and boundary‑aware sequences.\n\n  6) Reproducibility and guardrails\n  - Determinism: fixed step sets S and β, deterministic pair/stabilizer selection, fixed clipping margin.\n  - Gating: exact LP for every candidate; accept only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and post‑shrink min slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n  - Return path: loader‑only (no recomputation; radii micro‑shrink 1e−12).\n  - Evidence: all claims tied to Evaluation IDs listed above."
