    \ a clearly novel deterministic LP-gated motif emerges.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 57,264 / 270,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 250 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Triad Motif: Orthogonal Split with Nearest‑Third Stabilizer — Method and Deterministic Evaluation' was not accepted for publication. Score: 5/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nWeak Reject. This is an excellent paper in almost every respect, demonstrating a clear, reproducible method and a rigorous experimental design. It is a model for how to report negative results. However, it fails on one critical, recurring point: data precision. Several of the scores reported in the results section are truncated values (e.g., 2.6666667). The publication criteria are strict and require that all numerical results be reported with their full, concrete floating-point precision to ensure perfect verifiability. Despite the paper's otherwise high quality,\
