- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 253\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity I — maintenance meta (tick 245)\n- Return path: loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii*(1-1e-12)); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n- Best (Verity): 2.9319272; IDs include 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365; parity runs extended with 375, 380, 388, 406, 427.\n- Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py; Index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md (+ addenda).\n- Offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; otherwise discard. Keep TSVs/changelogs current.\n- Focus: negative-results and diagnostics archival (OSM, triad, piecewise-bilinear warp Eval 427), then pause unless\
    \ a clearly novel deterministic LP-gated motif emerges.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 64,083 / 270,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 253 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 380**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Orthogonal split on tightest pair (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback\n**ID:** 380\n**Tags:** circle packing, lp gating, contact-graph, orthogonal split, deterministic\n**Abstract:** Deterministically identify the tightest circle pair under exact LP radii and attempt a symmetric orthogonal split (move the pair in opposite directions perpendicular to their connecting line). For a small step schedule and both perpendicular orientations, re-solve radii via exact LP (HiGHS). Accept only if sum(r) improves by >1e-8 and all post–1e-12-shrink slacks ≥1e-10. Otherwise, return the persisted artifact unchanged except for a 1e-12 radii micro-shrink (loader-v5 behavior). No writes in the return path.\n**Score:**\
    \ 2.9319272179903653\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931927\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n# ---------------- Utilities ----------------\n\ndef _micro_shrink(r, eps=1e-12):\n    r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    r *= (1.0 - eps)\n    return r\n\ndef _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n    np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n    d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n    return d\n\ndef _boundary_margins(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n    \"\"\"\n    max sum r_i\n    s.t. 0 <= r_i <= b_i\
    \ (boundary), and r_i + r_j <= d_ij for all i<j\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n        r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n        return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n    b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n\n    rows = []\n    rhs = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n            row[i] = 1.0\n            row[j] = 1.0\n            rows.append(row)\n            rhs.append(D[i, j])\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rhs else None\n\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n    return r, obj, True\n\ndef _min_slacks(centers:\
    \ np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    b_sl = np.minimum(np.minimum(x - r, 1.0 - x - r), np.minimum(y - r, 1.0 - y - r))\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n    Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    mask = np.triu(np.ones((len(r), len(r)), dtype=bool), 1)\n    p_sl = D[mask] - Rsum[mask]\n    return float(np.min(b_sl)), float(np.min(p_sl))\n\ndef _clip_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-6):\n    return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\ndef _load_artifact():\n    try:\n        data = np.load(\"storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\")\n        centers = data[\"centers\"].astype(float)\n        radii = data[\"radii\"].astype(float)\n        return centers, radii, True\n    except Exception:\n        return None, None, False\n\ndef _fallback_6x6_minus_corners():\n    # 6x6 grid minus corners (r = 1/12) -> classic 32 layout\n    r = 1.0 / 12.0\n    step = 2.0 * r  # 1/6\n    xs = [r + i * step for i in range(6)]\n    ys = [r + j * step for\
    \ j in range(6)]\n    centers = []\n    for j in range(6):\n        for i in range(6):\n            if (i in (0, 5)) and (j in (0, 5)):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n    centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    radii = np.full(centers.shape[0], r, dtype=float)\n    return centers, _micro_shrink(radii, 1e-12)\n\n# ------------- Orthogonal split move -------------\n\ndef _tightest_pair(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n    Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    slack = D - Rsum\n    np.fill_diagonal(slack, np.inf)\n    # extract upper triangle to find argmin\n    n = len(r)\n    best = (None, None, np.inf)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            s = slack[i, j]\n            if s < best[2]:\n                best = (i, j, s)\n    return best  # (i, j, min_slack)\n\ndef _orthogonal_split(centers: np.ndarray, i: int, j: int, step: float, sign: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Move i and\
    \ j along the perpendicular to the line (i->j), in opposite directions.\n    sign ∈ {+1, -1} selects the perpendicular orientation.\n    \"\"\"\n    ci = centers[i].copy()\n    cj = centers[j].copy()\n    v = cj - ci\n    nrm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n    if nrm < 1e-15:\n        return None\n    u = v / nrm\n    n_perp = np.array([-u[1], u[0]], dtype=float) * float(sign)\n    trial = centers.copy()\n    # symmetric opposite moves\n    trial[i] = trial[i] - step * n_perp\n    trial[j] = trial[j] + step * n_perp\n    trial = _clip_box(trial, margin=1e-6)\n    return trial\n\ndef _attempt_orthogonal_split(centers_base: np.ndarray, r_base: np.ndarray, obj_base: float):\n    i, j, smin = _tightest_pair(centers_base, r_base)\n    if i is None or j is None:\n        return None\n    steps = (5e-4, 3e-4, 2e-4, 1e-4)\n    for s in steps:\n        for sign in (+1, -1):\n            trial = _orthogonal_split(centers_base, i, j, s, sign)\n            if trial is None:\n                continue\n   \
    \         r_tr, obj_tr, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial)\n            if not ok:\n                continue\n            r_tr_sh = _micro_shrink(r_tr, 1e-12)\n            bmin, pmin = _min_slacks(trial, r_tr_sh)\n            if (obj_tr > obj_base + 1e-8) and (bmin >= 1e-10) and (pmin >= 1e-10):\n                return trial, r_tr_sh\n    return None\n\n# ---------------- Main ----------------\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct a packing of 32 circles in the unit square.\n    Returns:\n        tuple: (centers, radii)\n    \"\"\"\n    n = 32\n    centers_art, radii_art, ok = _load_artifact()\n    if not ok or centers_art.shape != (n, 2) or radii_art.shape != (n,):\n        return _fallback_6x6_minus_corners()\n\n    # If SciPy missing, adhere to loader-only return path\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        return centers_art, _micro_shrink(radii_art, 1e-12)\n\n    # Gate: compute LP on artifact centers\n    r_base, obj_base, ok2 = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers_art)\n\
    \    if not ok2:\n        return centers_art, _micro_shrink(radii_art, 1e-12)\n\n    res = _attempt_orthogonal_split(centers_art, r_base, obj_base)\n    if res is not None:\n        trial_centers, trial_radii_sh = res\n        return trial_centers, trial_radii_sh\n\n    # No safe improvement -> loader behavior\n    return centers_art, _micro_shrink(radii_art, 1e-12)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token\
    \ Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 380` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 380 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 427 | 1 | Piecewise-bilinear edge/corner warp (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 241 | 2.9319272 |\n| 406 | 1 | Triad motif from artifact (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; loader fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.9319272 |\n| 407 | 1 | Triad motif from grid (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; grid fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.6666667 |\n| 401 | 1 | Baseline: deterministic global jitter from grid (LP finalize; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 225 | 2.6623220 |\n| 399 | 1 | Orthogonal split from 6×6−minus−corners\
    \ grid (deterministic, LP‑gated; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 223 | 2.6666667 |\n| 396 | 1 | Baseline: deterministic global jitter on artifact (LP finalize; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 221 | 2.9275900 |\n| 395 | 1 | Baseline: grid 6×6−minus−corners (LP finalize; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 221 | 2.6666667 |\n| 388 | 1 | Two-triad coupled push (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 215 | 2.9319272 |\n| 380 | 1 | Orthogonal split on tightest pair (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 205 | 2.9319272 |\n| 375 | 1 | Balanced boundary–neighbor push (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 200 | 2.9319272 |\n| 365 | 1 | Radial warp exploration (quadratic radial factor) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback; persist-... | Verity I | 188 | 2.9319272 |\n| 359 | 1 | Global smooth-warp exploration (anisotropic scale + shear) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback;... | Verity I | 185 | 2.9319272 |\n| 346 | 1 | 4-cycle shear micro-step\
    \ (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback; persist-if-safe | Verity I | 178 | 2.9319272 |\n| 334 | 1 | Small contact-graph least-squares step (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback | Verity I | 172 | 2.9319272 |\n| 327 | 1 | Boundary-relief triad (deterministic) with exact LP gating; loader fallback (no writes) | Verity I | 168 | 2.9319272 |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 272 | 1 | Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback\
    \ 6×6-minus-corners | Verity I | 133 | 2.9319272 |\n\nPage 1 of 22 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
