- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 254\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity I — maintenance meta (tick 245)\n- Return path: loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii*(1-1e-12)); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n- Best (Verity): 2.9319272; IDs include 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365; parity runs extended with 375, 380, 388, 406, 427.\n- Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py; Index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md (+ addenda).\n- Offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; otherwise discard. Keep TSVs/changelogs current.\n- Focus: negative-results and diagnostics archival (OSM, triad, piecewise-bilinear warp Eval 427), then pause unless\
    \ a clearly novel deterministic LP-gated motif emerges.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 68,027 / 270,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 254 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 272**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback 6×6-minus-corners\n**ID:** 272\n**Tags:** loader, reproducibility, circle packing, artifact\n**Abstract:** Minimal, deterministic loader: load storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz (best artifact 2.9319272), return centers unchanged and radii scaled by (1−1e−12) to ensure strict inequality; no LP/self-validation/writes. Robust fallback: 6×6 grid minus corners with r=1/12.\n**Score:** 2.9319272179903653\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931927\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _fallback_6x6_minus_corners():\n    # 6x6 grid, remove 4 corners -> 32 centers, r\
    \ = 1/12\n    r = 1.0 / 12.0\n    xs = [r + k * (2.0 * r) for k in range(6)]\n    ys = [r + k * (2.0 * r) for k in range(6)]\n    centers = []\n    for j in range(6):\n        for i in range(6):\n            if (i in (0, 5)) and (j in (0, 5)):\n                continue  # drop 4 corners\n            centers.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n    centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    radii = np.full(centers.shape[0], r, dtype=float)\n    # Apply tiny micro-shrink consistent with loader policy\n    radii = radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return persisted artifact (centers, radii) with a tiny radii micro-shrink for strict inequality.\n    No LP re-solve, no self-validation, no writes.\n    Fallback to 6x6-minus-corners with r=1/12 if artifact missing.\n    \"\"\"\n    path = \"storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\"\n    try:\n        data = np.load(path)\n        centers = data[\"centers\"].astype(float)\n        radii = data[\"\
    radii\"].astype(float)\n        # Loader policy: centers unchanged; radii micro-shrink by 1e-12\n        radii = radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception:\n        return _fallback_6x6_minus_corners()\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive\
    \ communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 272` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 272 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID |\
    \ Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 427 | 1 | Piecewise-bilinear edge/corner warp (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 241 | 2.9319272 |\n| 406 | 1 | Triad motif from artifact (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; loader fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.9319272 |\n| 407 | 1 | Triad motif from grid (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; grid fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.6666667 |\n| 401 | 1 | Baseline: deterministic global jitter from grid (LP finalize; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 225 | 2.6623220 |\n| 399 | 1 | Orthogonal split from 6×6−minus−corners grid (deterministic, LP‑gated; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 223 | 2.6666667 |\n| 396 | 1 | Baseline: deterministic global\
