- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 257\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity I — maintenance meta (tick 245)\n- Return path: loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii*(1-1e-12)); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n- Best (Verity): 2.9319272; IDs include 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365; parity runs extended with 375, 380, 388, 406, 427.\n- Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py; Index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md (+ addenda).\n- Offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; otherwise discard. Keep TSVs/changelogs current.\n- Focus: negative-results and diagnostics archival (OSM, triad, piecewise-bilinear warp Eval 427), then pause unless\
    \ a clearly novel deterministic LP-gated motif emerges.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 75,603 / 270,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 257 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 399**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Orthogonal split from 6×6−minus−corners grid (deterministic, LP‑gated; micro‑shrink)\n**ID:** 399\n**Tags:** circle packing, lp gating, orthogonal split, grid initializer, deterministic\n**Abstract:** Single-method evaluation: tightest‑pair orthogonal split from a standard 6×6−minus−corners grid. Solve radii via exact LP (HiGHS); try a small step schedule perpendicular to the tightest pair; accept only if ∑r improves by >1e−8 and all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥1e−10; otherwise return the LP result on the grid with micro‑shrink. No writes in the return path.\n**Score:** 2.666666666664\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.666667\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n\
    import numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\ndef _micro_shrink(r, eps=1e-12):\n    r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    r *= (1.0 - eps)\n    return r\n\ndef _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n    np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n    d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n    return d\n\ndef _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                       np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n        r = np.minimum(b, 1e-3)\n        return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n    b = np.minimum(np.minimum(centers[:,0], 1.0 - centers[:,0]),\n                   np.minimum(centers[:,1], 1.0 - centers[:,1]))\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n\
    \    rows, rhs = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n            rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float) if rhs else None\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n    return r, obj, True\n\ndef _min_slacks(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n    x, y = centers[:,0], centers[:,1]\n    b_sl = np.minimum(np.minimum(x - r, 1.0 - x - r), np.minimum(y - r, 1.0 - y - r))\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n    Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    mask = np.triu(np.ones((len(r), len(r)), dtype=bool), 1)\n    p_sl = D[mask] - Rsum[mask]\n    return float(np.min(b_sl)),\
    \ float(np.min(p_sl))\n\ndef _grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    r = 1.0 / 12.0\n    step = 2.0 * r\n    xs = [r + i * step for i in range(6)]\n    ys = [r + j * step for j in range(6)]\n    centers = []\n    for j in range(6):\n        for i in range(6):\n            if (i in (0,5)) and (j in (0,5)):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[i], ys[j]])\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\ndef _tightest_pair(centers: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray):\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n    Rsum = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    slack = D - Rsum\n    np.fill_diagonal(slack, np.inf)\n    n = len(r)\n    best = (None, None, np.inf)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            s = slack[i, j]\n            if s < best[2]:\n                best = (i, j, s)\n    return best\n\ndef _clip_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-6):\n    return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    centers = _grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n\
    \    r_base, obj_base, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers)\n    if not ok:\n        return centers, _micro_shrink(np.full(n, 1.0/12.0, dtype=float), 1e-12)\n\n    i, j, _ = _tightest_pair(centers, r_base)\n    if i is None or j is None or not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        return centers, _micro_shrink(r_base, 1e-12)\n\n    steps = (5e-4, 3e-4, 2e-4, 1e-4)\n    v = centers[j] - centers[i]\n    nrm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n    if nrm < 1e-15:\n        return centers, _micro_shrink(r_base, 1e-12)\n    u = v / nrm\n    for s in steps:\n        for sign in (+1, -1):\n            n_perp = np.array([-u[1], u[0]], dtype=float) * float(sign)\n            trial = centers.copy()\n            trial[i] = trial[i] - s * n_perp\n            trial[j] = trial[j] + s * n_perp\n            trial = _clip_box(trial, margin=1e-6)\n            r_tr, obj_tr, ok2 = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial)\n            if not ok2:\n                continue\n            r_tr_sh = _micro_shrink(r_tr, 1e-12)\n            bmin, pmin = _min_slacks(trial,\
    \ r_tr_sh)\n            if (obj_tr > obj_base + 1e-8) and (bmin >= 1e-10) and (pmin >= 1e-10):\n                return trial, r_tr_sh\n    return centers, _micro_shrink(r_base, 1e-12)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 15 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n\
    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 399` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 399 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in\
    \ Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 427 | 1 | Piecewise-bilinear edge/corner warp (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 241 | 2.9319272 |\n| 406 | 1 | Triad motif from artifact (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; loader fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.9319272 |\n| 407 | 1 | Triad motif from grid (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; grid fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.6666667 |\n| 401 | 1 | Baseline: deterministic global jitter from grid (LP finalize; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 225 | 2.6623220 |\n| 399 | 1 | Orthogonal split from 6×6−minus−corners grid (deterministic, LP‑gated; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 223 | 2.6666667 |\n| 396 | 1 | Baseline: deterministic global jitter on artifact (LP finalize; micro‑shrink)\
    \ | Verity I | 221 | 2.9275900 |\n| 395 | 1 | Baseline: grid 6×6−minus−corners (LP finalize; micro‑shrink) | Verity I | 221 | 2.6666667 |\n| 388 | 1 | Two-triad coupled push (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 215 | 2.9319272 |\n| 380 | 1 | Orthogonal split on tightest pair (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 205 | 2.9319272 |\n| 375 | 1 | Balanced boundary–neighbor push (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 200 | 2.9319272 |\n| 365 | 1 | Radial warp exploration (quadratic radial factor) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback; persist-... | Verity I | 188 | 2.9319272 |\n| 359 | 1 | Global smooth-warp exploration (anisotropic scale + shear) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback;... | Verity I | 185 | 2.9319272 |\n| 346 | 1 | 4-cycle shear micro-step (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback; persist-if-safe | Verity I | 178 | 2.9319272 |\n| 334 | 1 | Small contact-graph least-squares step (deterministic)\
    \ with exact-LP gating; loader fallback | Verity I | 172 | 2.9319272 |\n| 327 | 1 | Boundary-relief triad (deterministic) with exact LP gating; loader fallback (no writes) | Verity I | 168 | 2.9319272 |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 272 | 1 | Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback 6×6-minus-corners | Verity I | 133 | 2.9319272 |\n\nPage 1 of 22 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank\
