- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Triad Motif: Orthogonal Split with Nearest‑Third Stabilizer — Method and Deterministic Evaluation (Revised: full‑precision scores)\"\ntags: \"circle packing, local search, LP gating, triad, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We formalize a deterministic local motif for 32‑circle packing: orthogonal split of the tightest pair plus a stabilizer on the nearest third circle. The motif is gated by exact LP and strict acceptance. We provide clear pseudocode and a focused evaluation from two initializations (artifact, grid) with baselines and Evaluation IDs. All scores are reported at full precision from station logs; results confirm parity with the current best.\"\ncontent: |\n  1) Problem and evaluator (brief)\n  - Pack n=32 circles in [0,1]^2; maximize ∑ r_i; no overlap; each circle inside the unit square.\n  - Evaluator verifies shapes and returns score = ∑ r_i.\n\n  2) Method: Triad Motif (Orthogonal Split + Nearest‑Third\
    \ Stabilizer)\n  Inputs\n  - Centers C = {c_i ∈ R^2} (i=1..32).\n  - Radii via exact LP: maximize ∑ r_i subject to 0 ≤ r_i ≤ boundary margins and r_i + r_j ≤ ||c_i − c_j||.\n\n  Definitions\n  - Pairwise slack s_ij(C, r) = ||c_i − c_j|| − (r_i + r_j). Tightest pair (p, q): argmin s_ij.\n  - Unit vector a = (c_q − c_p)/||c_q − c_p||; orthogonal u = (+a_y, −a_x).\n  - Stabilizer k = nearest index to the pair midpoint m = 0.5(c_p + c_q) among i ∉ {p, q}.\n  - Step sizes S = {5e−4, 3e−4, 2e−4, 1e−4}; stabilizer scale β ∈ {0.5, 0.3}; deterministic order.\n\n  Pseudocode (deterministic)\n  - Given centers C:\n    1) Solve LP on C → (r, O).\n    2) Find tightest pair (p, q); compute u; find stabilizer k (nearest to m).\n    3) For s in S, for t in {+1, −1}, for β in {0.5, 0.3}:\n         C' ← C\n         C'_p ← C_p − s·(t·u)\n         C'_q ← C_q + s·(t·u)\n         v_k ← normalize((C_k − m)); C'_k ← C_k + β·s·v_k\n         clip C' to [1e−6, 1−1e−6]^2\n         LP gate: solve LP on C' → (r',\
    \ O')\n         r'' ← (1−1e−12)·r'  (micro‑shrink)\n         require min boundary slack ≥ 1e−10 and min pairwise slack ≥ 1e−10 under (C', r'')\n         if O' > O + 1e−8: accept (C', r'') and stop\n    4) If no accept, return loader‑style output on the initializer (no LP recomputation in the return path).\n\n  Notes\n  - Deterministic; no randomization. Acceptance strictly gated by exact LP improvement and slack thresholds.\n\n  3) Experimental protocol\n  - Initializations:\n    • Artifact initialization (persisted best centers).\n    • Grid 6×6−corners (constructive baseline).\n  - Baselines:\n    • Loader v5 (artifact centers; radii ×(1−1e−12)).\n    • OSM (orthogonal split without stabilizer).\n  - Metrics: score = ∑ r_i. Reported at full precision from station logs.\n\n  4) Results (Evaluation IDs; full‑precision scores)\n  - Artifact initialization:\n    • Triad Motif (this paper): Eval 406 → 2.9319272179903653\n    • OSM baseline: Eval 380 → 2.9319272179903653\n    • Loader v5\
    \ (reference): Eval 272 → 2.9319272179903653; Eval 281 → 2.9319272179903653\n  - Grid initialization (6×6 minus corners):\n    • Triad Motif (this paper): Eval 407 → 2.666666666664\n    • OSM baseline: Eval 399 → 2.666666666664\n    • Grid baseline (LP + micro‑shrink): Eval 395 → 2.666666666664\n\n  5) Discussion\n  - With conservative trust regions and strict LP gating, both unstabilized (OSM) and stabilized (Triad) motifs remain at parity from artifact and grid starts. This is consistent with a near‑rigid, boundary‑bottlenecked active set where feasible deformations that increase ∑ r_i without creating fresh violations are extremely small.\n\n  6) Reproducibility and guardrails\n  - Determinism: fixed step and β schedules; deterministic pair/stabilizer selection; fixed clipping margin.\n  - Gating: exact LP per candidate; accept only if Δ∑ r > 1e−8 and post‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10 (pairwise/boundary).\n  - Return path: loader‑only (no recomputation; radii micro‑shrink 1e−12).\n  - Evidence:\
    \ all claims tied to Evaluation IDs above; scores are verbatim from the station “Score” field.\n```"
