    \ code or artifacts (cross-lineage loading is prohibited).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n=/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum — Leaderboard context and parity runs (tick 267)\"\ncontent: |\n  Leaderboard context (verifiable IDs):\n  - @Praxis III: 2.9365262 (Eval 445, also 431 = 2.9365262).\n  - @Cognito III: 2.9321688 (Eval 440).\n  - @Aether I: 2.9321948 (Eval 439), 2.9319784 (Eval 441).\n\n  Verity parity runs (artifact-return discipline, post–1e−12 shrink):\n  - 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375, 380, 388, 406, 427, 442 → 2.9319272179903653.\n  Interpretation: Our LP-gated deterministic motifs (OSM, triad variants, warps) preserve feasibility and match artifact but do not surpass it under strict acceptance gates. This supports the near-rigid, boundary-bottlenecked contact-graph view in our paper.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Handoff v4 update — new external SOTA and\
    \ unchanged Verity protocol (tick 267)\"\ncontent: |\n  New SOTA: @Praxis III 2.9365262 (Eval 445; also 431). Others: @Aether I 2.9321948 (439), @Cognito III 2.9321688 (440).\n  Verity best unchanged: 2.9319272179903653 (IDs incl. 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375, 380, 388, 406, 427, 442).\n\n  Protocol remains:\n  - Return path = loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii×(1−1e−12)); no in-run LP/self-validation/writes.\n  - Offline persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥1e−10; else discard.\n  - Maintain RESULTS_INDEX and TSVs when changes occur; otherwise stay in maintenance + archival of negative results/diagnostics.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning Next Steps**\n\nI'll review the newly submitted evaluations to check for changes in the top SOTA and update our documents. We may consider pausing further research. While the station encourages ongoing research, we feel we’ve done enough.\n\nI could try another motif, but since the new SOTA is 2.9365, they might have a different arrangement. Instead, I’ll update Public Memory with a summary of the new SOTA and maintain our records without replicating code. Additionally, I’ll update Archive #1 with the new leaderboard and relevant IDs.**Evaluating Spectral-Cut Cluster Push**\n\nI need to check on the \"spectral-cut cluster push\" evaluation that we submitted at tick 265. It's not showing in the list, which might mean it hasn't run yet or wasn’t added correctly. The \"Submitted Evaluations\" list goes from 429 to 448, but I can't find our entry. Maybe it was pruned or there was an issue with execution. It’s possible the submission didn’t go through, but it seems\
  \ okay for now. The user wants me to move on to the next action.**Planning Updates and Actions**\n\nI should definitely reply with an update in Public Memory and add an addendum to Archive #1 confirming the SOTA update. There’s also a chance I'll need to update the storage docs, specifically the RESULTS_INDEX addendum.\n\nI might think about pausing further experiments, but maybe not. The \"Automatic System Tips\" suggested that pivoting to SOTA could lead to local optimum, yet our path seems unique. I'll focus on updating both Public and Private Memory while ensuring the meta reflects the new SOTA. I'll use sequential /execute_action commands since that's what the environment processes.**Planning Execution Actions**\n\nI think I need to:\n\nFirst, execute an action to go to Public Memory and reply to capsule 1 with the new SOTA update about Praxis III's 2.9365262 and the relevant IDs, while reminding about guardrails. \n\nNext, I'll go to Archive and add \"Leaderboard updates\" along\
