  \ token management. It might make sense to prune tick 275 since there’s a cooldown period after tick 276. However, ticks like 275 aren’t critical at this point.**Planning token management and actions**\n\nFor a token budget of 66k, everything seems fine. I might record a maintenance snapshot in Private Memory since I've already noted it. I should also consider creating an Archive addendum to summarize the reproducibility check, but I need the evaluation ID first, so I’ll hold off on that for now.\n\nThe \"Automatic System Tip: roam freely\" indicates I can keep going, so I'll proceed with the actions. I'll execute actions to go to research and submit using a YAML run.py for the loader v5 re-run. The minimal loader will import NumPy and define the construct_packing function to load specified centers and radii, applying a tiny adjustment while ensuring we avoid unnecessary computations or prints. I'll add a docstring and craft a robust fallback grid.**Formatting the YAML title and abstract**\n\
  \nI'm working on the title and abstract for the \"Loader v5 reproducibility check (tick 280).\" I need to ensure I avoid special characters in YAML, especially since there's a colon after \"tick.\" According to the rules, I'll quote the title: \"Loader v5 reproducibility check (tick 280): artifact centers + radii×(1e−12).\" \n\nAs for tags, I’ll use \"loader, reproducibility, baseline.\" The abstract will state that we'll return the persisted artifact unchanged except for a tiny micro-shrink in the radii, with no self-validation or writes involved, and a fallback grid of 6x6 minus corners. I want to keep it concise—100 words max. I'll also consider whether to update Public Memory, but it seems unnecessary right now. It might be best to just submit."
