tick: 292
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n=/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs for 32‑Circle Packing: Negative Results and Diagnostics\"\ntags: \"circle packing, diagnostics, negative results, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We report a systematic study of deterministic, LP‑gated local motifs for 32‑circle packing in the unit square. Each candidate centers update re‑optimizes radii via exact LP (HiGHS), accepts only on strict ∆∑r > 1e−8 with post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10, and otherwise returns a loader result (centers unchanged; radii×(1e−12)). Across orthogonal‑split, triad cycle‑push, boundary‑relief, finite‑difference, warp, and projected contact‑pressure moves, all runs matched our artifact (2.9319272179903653) without strict improvement. We provide evaluation IDs, diagnostics on near‑rigidity/boundary bottlenecks, and a reproducibility protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  Problem and evaluator\n  - Pack n=32 circles in [0,1]^2, no overlaps; objective = sum\
    \ of radii. Evaluator allows equality at contacts/boundaries; returns sum(r) on success.\n  - Reproducibility discipline: return path never recomputes LP; apply only a 1e−12 radii micro‑shrink.\n\n  Methodology (no code; protocol only)\n  - Offline candidate generation via deterministic local motifs; exact LP (HiGHS) for radii at each candidate.\n  - Acceptance gates:\n    • Strict improvement: ∆∑r > 1e−8.\n    • Safety: after 1e−12 radii shrink, all pairwise/boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n  - If gates fail, discard the move and return the artifact unchanged except for the 1e−12 micro‑shrink. No writes from the evaluation path.\n\n  Verified results (evaluation IDs; all valid)\n  - Artifact/loader reproductions: 272, 281 = 2.9319272179903653.\n  - Baselines:\n    • 395: 6×6 minus corners (LP + 1e−12 shrink) = 2.666666666664.\n    • 399: Orthogonal split from grid (no accept) = 2.666666666664.\n  - Deterministic motifs (all parity at 2.9319272179903653):\n    • 375: Balanced boundary–neighbor\
    \ push (LP‑gated).\n    • 380: Orthogonal split on tightest pair (LP‑gated).\n    • 406: Triad cycle‑push with stabilizer (artifact init).\n    • 427: Piecewise‑bilinear edge/corner warp.\n    • 442: Triad ablation (β∈{1.0, 0.5}).\n    • 472: Projected contact‑pressure (PCP) displacement + boundary relief.\n\n  Diagnostics and insights\n  - Near‑rigid active set: multiple near‑equality contacts plus boundary bottlenecks focus slack onto few constraints; small moves often trade constraints without net gain.\n  - Boundary sensitivity: boundary‑relief steps quickly trigger pairwise tightness; coupled compensations rarely yield strict ∆∑r above 1e−8.\n  - Validator alignment: equality is permitted; internal re‑LP/self‑validation can spuriously create micro‑overlaps (~1e−14). The 1e−12 shrink in the return path avoids this pitfall.\n\n  Reproducibility protocol (field‑tested)\n  - Return path: centers unchanged; radii×(1e−12); no LP/self‑validation/writes; robust 6×6‑minus‑corners fallback.\n\
    \  - Offline persistence (for future work): update artifact only if ∆∑r > 1e−8 and all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; otherwise discard.\n  - Deterministic seeds and bounded runs (≤120 LP solves; ≤2 accepts/run).\n\n  Context\n  - Our lineage best: 2.9319272179903653 (multiple IDs above).\n  - External reference: stronger scores exist (e.g., 474 = 2.9365262, Aether I) via different pipelines; our study isolates why a broad class of deterministic, LP‑gated micro‑motifs stall.\n\n  Takeaways\n  - If pursuing local motifs, incorporate stronger model‑agreement tests on the active subgraph and multi‑constraint coupling (e.g., two‑triad cycle‑push with stabilizer).\n  - Adhere to the reproducibility protocol to avoid evaluator mismatches and facilitate reliable comparison.\n```\n=/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n=/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ntitle: Final steps plan (ticks 292–300) before exit\ncontent: |\n  - Archive: submitted “Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs: Negative Results\
    \ and Diagnostics” with IDs and full‑precision scores; reproduces parity conclusion and protocol.\n  - Storage: HANDOFF_v5.md present; RESULTS_INDEX addenda and TSVs up to date (incl. results_pcp_472.tsv).\n  - Policy frozen: loader‑only return path; offline persistence only on ∆∑r > 1e−8 and all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n  - Next minimal tasks before exit:\n    1) One final prune pass if available.\n    2) Public post summarizing final state (IDs and protocol).\n    3) Exit around tick ~298 if no novel idea emerges.\n```\n"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating exit options**\n\nI need to generate the best response now that we're in the Exit room with 8 ticks left before the session expires. I remember attempting to exit earlier at tick 208, but we decided to stay. Now, it's time to reflect on our progress and consider whether to finalize the documentation or continue working on it. The earlier guidelines suggested finalizing reports, keeping logs current, and pruning as necessary, so I want to make sure we follow through on that.**Final cleanup tasks**\n\nWe still have 8 ticks left, so it's time to do some final cleanup work. I want to finalize the Archive negative-results document—let’s check if that’s already done. I also need to ensure that the Private memory is updated to v5. We encountered a YAML parsing error while trying to handle \"reply 5\" at tick 290, but attempted it again at 291. However, the Private Memory still shows \"Handoff v4\" instead of updating. It might be that the last action at tick 291\
