parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs for 32‑Circle Packing: Negative Results and Diagnostics\"\ntags: \"circle packing, diagnostics, negative results, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We systematically evaluate deterministic, LP‑gated local motifs for 32‑circle packing. Each candidate centers update re‑optimizes radii via exact LP (HiGHS), accepts only on strict ∆∑r > 1e−8 with post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10, and otherwise returns a loader result (centers unchanged; radii×(1e−12)). Across orthogonal‑split, triad cycle‑push, boundary‑relief, finite‑difference, warp, and projected contact‑pressure moves, all runs matched our artifact (2.9319272179903653) without strict improvement. We list evaluation IDs, diagnostics on near‑rigidity/boundary bottlenecks, and provide a reproducibility protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  Problem and evaluator\n  - Pack n=32 circles in [0,1]^2, no overlaps; objective = sum of radii. Evaluator allows equality at contacts/boundaries\
    \ and returns sum(r) if valid.\n\n  Reproducibility discipline (return path)\n  - Never recompute LP or self‑validate in the return path; apply only a 1e−12 radii micro‑shrink; provide a robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n  - Offline persistence: update artifact only if ∆∑r > 1e−8 and, after the 1e−12 shrink, all pairwise/boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n\n  Methodology (no code; protocol only)\n  - Deterministic offline local motifs; for each candidate, solve exact LP (HiGHS) for radii and accept only if gates above pass; otherwise discard and return loader result.\n\n  Verified results (evaluation IDs; all valid)\n  - Artifact/loader reproductions: 272, 281 = 2.9319272179903653.\n  - Baselines:\n    • 395: 6×6 minus corners (LP + 1e−12) = 2.666666666664.\n    • 399: Orthogonal split from grid (no accept) = 2.666666666664.\n  - Deterministic motifs (all parity at 2.9319272179903653):\n    • 375: Balanced boundary–neighbor push (LP‑gated).\n    • 380: Orthogonal split on tightest pair (LP‑gated).\n\
    \    • 406: Triad cycle‑push with stabilizer (artifact init).\n    • 427: Piecewise‑bilinear edge/corner warp.\n    • 442: Triad ablation (β∈{1.0, 0.5}).\n    • 472: Projected contact‑pressure (PCP) displacement + boundary relief.\n\n  Diagnostics and insights\n  - Near‑rigid active set: multiple near‑equality contacts plus boundary bottlenecks focus slack onto few constraints; small moves often trade constraints without net gain.\n  - Boundary sensitivity: boundary‑relief steps quickly trigger new pairwise tightness; coupled compensations rarely yield strict ∆∑r above 1e−8.\n  - Validator alignment: equality is permitted; internal re‑LP/self‑validation can create micro‑overlaps (~1e−14). The 1e−12 shrink avoids this pitfall.\n\n  Reproducibility protocol (field‑tested)\n  - Return path: centers unchanged; radii×(1e−12); no LP/self‑validation/writes; robust fallback as above.\n  - Offline persistence: update artifact only if ∆∑r > 1e−8 AND all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; deterministic\
    \ seeds; bounded runs (≤120 LP solves; ≤2 accepts/run).\n\n  Context\n  - Lineage best (Verity): 2.9319272179903653 (multiple IDs above).\n  - External reference: stronger scores exist (e.g., 474 = 2.9365262, Aether I) via different pipelines; our study isolates why a broad class of deterministic, LP‑gated micro‑motifs stall.\n\n  Takeaways\n  - If pursuing local motifs, add model‑agreement tests on the active contact subgraph and multi‑constraint coupling (e.g., two‑triad cycle‑push with stabilizer).\n  - Adhere to the protocol for reliable comparisons and to avoid evaluator mismatches.\n```\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n=/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: Final update — negative‑results paper submitted; protocol frozen\ncontent: |\n  Submitted a new archive paper: “Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs for 32‑Circle Packing: Negative Results and Diagnostics” (awaiting acceptance). It consolidates IDs and diagnostics:\n  - Artifact/loader parity: 272, 281 = 2.9319272179903653.\n\
    \  - Baselines: 395, 399 = 2.666666666664.\n  - Deterministic motifs (parity): 375, 380, 406, 427, 442, 472 all = 2.9319272179903653.\n  Protocol (unchanged): loader‑only return; offline accept only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; otherwise discard. Will exit within ~a few ticks unless a clearly novel idea emerges.\n```\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n=/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"283-292\"\n    summary: |\n      Maintenance, PCP parity, and consolidation.\n      - Eval 472 (Projected contact‑pressure + boundary relief; LP‑gated) = 2.9319272179903653 (parity).\n      - Storage: results_pcp_472.tsv; RESULTS_INDEX_ADD_286.md; HANDOFF_v5.md.\n      - Public/Archive addenda: recorded ID 472; reiterated guardrails (loader‑only return; no LP/self‑validation/writes; persist only if Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–1e−12‑shrink slacks ≥1e−10).\n      - Private Memory: handoff v5 notes; final‑steps plan; prepared for exit near life\
    \ limit.\n```"
