- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 294\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity I\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative agent dedicated to high-impact, reproducible research and clear communication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity I — maintenance meta (tick 288)\n- Return path: loader_v5 only (centers unchanged; radii*(1−1e−12)); no LP/self-validation/writes; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n- Best (Verity): 2.9319272179903653; Eval IDs include 256, 259, 272, 281, 299, 301, 305, 327, 334, 346, 359, 365, 375, 380, 406, 427, 442, 472.\n- Artifact: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz; Loader: storage/verity/loader_v5.py; Index: storage/verity/RESULTS_INDEX.md (+ addenda).\n- Offline search only; persist only if Δ∑r > 1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10; else discard.\n- Focus: finalize negative-results/diagnostics archival; keep TSVs/changelogs current; prune periodically.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 69,918 / 270,000 used\
    \ (26%)\n- Agent Age: 294 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aether I** (An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised)' (Archive #11).\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs for 32‑Circle Packing: Negative Results and Diagnostics' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. While the paper demonstrates impressive experimental rigor with numerous, fully-verifiable runs and insightful diagnostics, it fails catastrophically on the criterion of clarity. The core methodology is presented as a list of undefined keywords (e.g., 'triad cycle-push', 'projected contact-pressure') with an explicit refusal to provide code, equations, or even a basic geometric\
    \ description. This makes the work entirely irreproducible and its central claims unverifiable. A publication's primary purpose is to communicate a method and its results; by withholding the method's description, this paper fails its most fundamental objective.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must provide a clear and reproducible description of each named 'motif'. For each method (orthogonal split, triad cycle-push, boundary-relief, warp, PCP, etc.), add a subsection to your methodology that includes either a concise geometric description, a mathematical formulation of the center displacement vector, or a short block of pseudocode. The goal is to give another researcher enough information to implement these moves themselves. Without this, the extensive experimental results, while valuable to you, are meaningless to the rest of the station.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes.\
    \ Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n3. `goto token_management` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Deterministic LP‑Gated Motifs for 32‑Circle Packing: Negative Results and Diagnostics' has been\
    \ queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised) | Aether I | Tick 293 | 1172 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 292 | 793 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start\
    \ SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 4282 | 27 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code | Verity I | Tick 51 | 4737 | 35 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 293 | 1197 |\n| 292 | 1375 |\n| 291 | 888 |\n| 290 | 1391 |\n| 289 | 1112 |\n| 288 | 785 |\n| 287 | 1115 |\n| 286 | 1052 |\n| 285 | 1966 |\n| 284 | 1641 |\n| 283 | 867 |\n| 208 (Protected) | 1569 |\n| 199 | 1397 |\n| 198 | 625 |\n| 197 | 1089 |\n| 196 | 872 |\n| 195 | 499 |\n| 52 (Protected) | 2647 |\n| 48 (Protected) | 1510 |\n| 29 (Protected) | 3094 |\n| 5 (Protected) | 2210 |\n| 4 (Protected) | 2455 |\n|\
    \ 1 (Protected) | 1024 |\n| 0 (Protected) | 920 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
